1
00:00:04,638 --> 00:00:07,708
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:07,742 --> 00:00:10,612
♪ NEXT SUNDAY A.D. ♪

3
00:00:10,645 --> 00:00:13,915
♪ THERE WAS A GUY NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:13,948 --> 00:00:17,018
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:17,052 --> 00:00:20,088
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:20,122 --> 00:00:23,290
♪ JUST ANOTHER
FACE IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:26,193
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB CLEANING
UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:26,227 --> 00:00:30,030
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES DIDN'T LIKE HIM
SO THEY SHOT HIM INTO SPACE ♪

9
00:00:32,733 --> 00:00:35,703
♪ WE'LL SEND
HIM CHEESY MOVIES ♪

10
00:00:35,737 --> 00:00:38,973
♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND
(LA-LA-LA) ♪

11
00:00:39,007 --> 00:00:41,742
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

12
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:45,213
♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND
(LA-LA-LA) ♪

13
00:00:45,247 --> 00:00:48,015
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

14
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:51,285
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END
(LA-LA-LA) ♪

15
00:00:51,318 --> 00:00:54,155
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

16
00:00:54,188 --> 00:00:56,892
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

17
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:02,363
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL
CAMBOT ♪

18
00:01:02,397 --> 00:01:03,898
♪ GYPSY
HI GIRL ♪

19
00:01:03,932 --> 00:01:05,367
♪ TOM SERVO!
WHAT A COOL GUY ♪

20
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,235
♪ CROW!
HE'S A WISECRACKER ♪

21
00:01:07,268 --> 00:01:09,803
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING
HOW HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

22
00:01:09,837 --> 00:01:13,173
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS
(LA LA LA) ♪

23
00:01:13,207 --> 00:01:16,077
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

24
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:19,380
♪ I SHOULD REALLY JUST RELAX ♪

25
00:01:19,413 --> 00:01:24,018
♪ FOR MYSTERY SCIENCE THEATER
3000 ♪♪

26
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:29,657
[GATES CLOSING]

27
00:01:34,695 --> 00:01:38,733
OH...
GOT FIVE SECONDS TO LIVE.

28
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:42,570
MUST GET PERSONAL FINANCES
IN ORDER.

29
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:44,805
JOEL, JOEL,
THANK HEAVEN YOU MADE IT.

30
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:46,340
BUT WHAT THE HECK WAS
THAT THING?

31
00:01:46,373 --> 00:01:47,675
WE LOST TOM, BUDDY.

32
00:01:47,708 --> 00:01:49,943
OH, I HATE TO THINK OF HIM IN
THERE WITH THAT, THAT...

33
00:01:49,977 --> 00:01:52,447
WAIT A MINUTE,
I'M BLIND, I'M BLIND.

34
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,315
THAT THING CUT ME.

35
00:01:54,348 --> 00:02:00,355
[TOM]
CROW, SOMETHING IS WRONG ON
SATURN THREE, OH!

36
00:02:00,388 --> 00:02:01,755
[CROW]
LOOKS LIKE I GOT IT, MAN.

37
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,290
AT LEAST I FOUND JOEL.

38
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:06,260
PANTY-WEIGHT PASSED OUT IN ALL
THE EXCITEMENT.

39
00:02:06,293 --> 00:02:08,797
[TOM]
KEEP TELLING
YOURSELF THAT, CROW.

40
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:12,233
OH, WHAT DO YOU MEAN, TOM,
YOU'RE CRYING?

41
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:13,467
WE'RE ALL TOGETHER AGAIN.

42
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,637
- CROW!
- I WAS JUST WITH HIM!

43
00:02:15,670 --> 00:02:18,807
DON'T YOU DO IT,
DON'T YOU DARE YOU DO IT.

44
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:21,375
[TOM]
JOEL, JOEL ROBINSON
IS DEAD!

45
00:02:21,408 --> 00:02:23,077
OH, GOD, HE'S DEAD.

46
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:25,980
- HEY, JUST KIDDING.
- WHOO-HOO-HOO.

47
00:02:26,013 --> 00:02:26,982
HEY, YOU LOOK GREAT.

48
00:02:27,015 --> 00:02:30,452
♪♪

49
00:02:33,287 --> 00:02:34,988
[ALL LAUGHING]

50
00:02:35,022 --> 00:02:36,757
OH, WE DO HAVE FUN,
DON'T WE?

51
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:38,827
BUT WHAT WAS
THAT LINE AGAIN, CROW?

52
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:41,862
OH, YOU MEAN, "I'M BLIND,
THAT THING CUT ME."

53
00:02:41,895 --> 00:02:44,398
NO, NO, NO, NO, THAT OTHER ONE,
THAT... DON'T YOU--

54
00:02:44,432 --> 00:02:45,400
OH, YEAH, OH, YEAH.

55
00:02:45,433 --> 00:02:46,767
DON'T YOU DO IT!

56
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,135
[ALL LAUGHING]

57
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:50,137
OH, JUST A SECOND,
THE MADS ARE CALLING.

58
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:52,907
DON'T YOU EVER LET ME CATCH YOU
FOOLING AROUND LIKE THAT UP--

59
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:55,510
WELL, IF I WAS UP THERE RIGHT
NOW, I'D SPANK YOUR HINDER.

60
00:02:55,543 --> 00:02:58,012
WELL, LET'S JUST RAGE ON WITH
THE INVENTION EXCHANGE, FRANK.

61
00:02:58,045 --> 00:03:00,382
TALL AND PROUD.

62
00:03:00,415 --> 00:03:04,152
OKAY, MY NAME IS BOND,
FRANK BOND.

63
00:03:04,185 --> 00:03:06,387
RIGHT, AND I'M URSULA ANDRESS.

64
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,755
I KNOW.

65
00:03:07,788 --> 00:03:10,023
DO I HAVE TO DO EVERYTHING
AROUND HERE, FRANK?

66
00:03:10,057 --> 00:03:13,560
OH, SORRY, BOSS, IT'S JUST THAT
WHEN YOU'RE A TOP SECRET AGENT

67
00:03:13,593 --> 00:03:15,363
WITH A LICENSE TO KILL
LIKE MYSELF,

68
00:03:15,397 --> 00:03:17,398
YOU ALWAYS FIND
YOURSELF IN SCUBA GEAR.

69
00:03:17,432 --> 00:03:19,267
BUT NOT ONLY THAT,
THERE'S THAT ENDLESS SERIES

70
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,268
OF FORMAL PARTIES,
DANCES

71
00:03:21,302 --> 00:03:23,503
AND DINNERS
THAT YOU HAVE TO ATTEND.

72
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:27,042
I MEAN, IT'S REALLY EASY TO FIT
A TUXEDO UNDER A WET SUIT,

73
00:03:27,075 --> 00:03:28,508
BUT WHAT ABOUT FOOTWEAR?

74
00:03:28,542 --> 00:03:29,943
SHOW THE PRODUCT,
FRANK.

75
00:03:29,977 --> 00:03:31,612
SMILE.

76
00:03:31,645 --> 00:03:33,513
INTRODUCING THE FORMAL FLIPPER.

77
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:35,850
STEP OUT OF THE OCEAN
AND INTO HIGH SOCIETY

78
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:37,718
WITH THE FORMAL FLIPPER.

79
00:03:37,752 --> 00:03:39,953
BY BASS,
AND WHAT ABOUT THE LADIES?

80
00:03:39,987 --> 00:03:41,255
THE LADIES,

81
00:03:41,288 --> 00:03:44,258
UH, PAN DOWN,
JERRY.

82
00:03:44,292 --> 00:03:47,095
HELLO, FEDERAL.

83
00:03:47,128 --> 00:03:48,428
OH, COULD WE JUST
GET ON WITH

84
00:03:48,462 --> 00:03:49,763
YOUR INVENTION EXCHANGE

85
00:03:49,797 --> 00:03:51,967
YOU BLINKING
PINKY RING?

86
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,267
I WANT CHILDREN.

87
00:03:55,202 --> 00:03:57,938
YOU KNOW, JOEL, EVERY DAY
IN EVERY WAY

88
00:03:57,972 --> 00:04:00,040
THOSE GUYS ARE
GETTING WEIRDER AND WEIRDER.

89
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:01,708
I KNOW, I COULDN'T AGREE
WITH YOU MORE.

90
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:05,145
ANYWAY, MY INVENTION EXCHANGE
TODAY IS BASED ON THE PREMISE

91
00:04:05,178 --> 00:04:08,548
THAT KIDS JUST DON'T LIKE
TO WEAR HATS IN THE WINTERTIME.

92
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:10,985
YOU KNOW, I MEAN,
HATS SMASH YOUR HAIR DOWN.

93
00:04:11,018 --> 00:04:13,788
HEADBANDS MAKE YOUR HAIR
ALL STATICKY

94
00:04:13,822 --> 00:04:16,057
AND EARMUFFS
JUST PLAIN LOOK DORKY.

95
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:19,093
YOU KNOW, I REMEMBER WINTER,
SLEDDING DOWN THE BACK HILL,

96
00:04:19,127 --> 00:04:21,028
OVER THE CREEK,
UNDER THE OLD BRIDGE,

97
00:04:21,062 --> 00:04:22,963
PAST THE SULLIVAN'S BIG
DARK TROUSER,

98
00:04:22,997 --> 00:04:24,398
WAVING TO LOIS
AND SABRINA.

99
00:04:24,432 --> 00:04:25,933
YEAH, YEAH, WHATEVER.

100
00:04:25,967 --> 00:04:27,835
ANYWAY, ANYWAY, YOU TWO.

101
00:04:27,868 --> 00:04:31,005
THIS IS A NEW INVENTION
THAT WILL ALLOW KIDS

102
00:04:31,038 --> 00:04:33,140
TO LOOK COOL AND STAY WARM

103
00:04:33,173 --> 00:04:34,908
AND AVOID ALL THAT
PEER MOCKERY

104
00:04:34,942 --> 00:04:36,977
THAT WE ALL KNOW
CAN HARM US

105
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:38,345
WELL INTO ADULTHOOD.

106
00:04:38,378 --> 00:04:39,713
CHECK IT OUT.

107
00:04:39,747 --> 00:04:41,615
THEY'RE EARMUFFS
THAT LOOK LIKE EARS,

108
00:04:41,648 --> 00:04:42,983
SEE WHAT I MEAN.

109
00:04:43,017 --> 00:04:45,453
OKAY, HERE, PUT THEM ON,
LET'S SEE HOW THEY LOOK, YEAH.

110
00:04:45,487 --> 00:04:47,088
OKAY?

111
00:04:47,122 --> 00:04:48,923
HEY, I FEEL LIKE
PRINCE CHARLES.

112
00:04:48,957 --> 00:04:50,223
YEAH.

113
00:04:50,257 --> 00:04:53,127
AND THEY'LL COME IN A RAINBOW
OF COLORS EVENTUALLY

114
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,895
TO MATCH EVERYBODY'S
COUNTENANCE,

115
00:04:54,928 --> 00:04:56,063
OKAY, LOOK.

116
00:04:56,097 --> 00:04:57,865
OH, SO SUDDENLY
I LOOK LIKE

117
00:04:57,898 --> 00:04:59,400
JIMMY J.J. WALKER.

118
00:04:59,433 --> 00:05:01,535
RIGHT, AND THEY'LL ALSO
COME IN

119
00:05:01,568 --> 00:05:03,470
A LOT OF NOVELTY STYLES, TOO.

120
00:05:03,503 --> 00:05:05,105
LIKE FOR NEXT YEAR'S BIG

121
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:07,742
SCI-FI LEVIATHON IN,
UM...

122
00:05:07,775 --> 00:05:09,843
IN ANCHORAGE, ALASKA,
I'VE INVENTED THESE:

123
00:05:09,877 --> 00:05:11,845
VULCAN EARMUFFS.

124
00:05:11,878 --> 00:05:13,782
- AH.
- SEE?

125
00:05:13,815 --> 00:05:15,315
FASCINATING.

126
00:05:15,348 --> 00:05:16,750
LIVE LONG AND PROSPER.

127
00:05:16,783 --> 00:05:18,218
NOT!

128
00:05:18,252 --> 00:05:19,387
AHH!

129
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:21,322
OH, SO JOEL--
WE DON'T SEE YOU WEARING

130
00:05:21,355 --> 00:05:23,223
ANY OF THESE DOPEY EARMUFFS.

131
00:05:23,257 --> 00:05:24,425
YEAH, WHAT'S THE DEAL?

132
00:05:24,458 --> 00:05:26,360
OH, WELL, YOU GUYS,
LOOKS ARE DECEIVING.

133
00:05:26,393 --> 00:05:27,728
YOU SEE,

134
00:05:27,762 --> 00:05:30,465
NOT ONLY AM I
PRESIDENT OF EAR CLUB FOR MEN,

135
00:05:30,498 --> 00:05:33,300
- I'M ALSO A CUSTOMER.
- WOW.

136
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,868
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

137
00:05:34,902 --> 00:05:36,837
VERY NICE, SY SPERLING.

138
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,940
TELL 'EM ABOUT THE EXPERIMENT
THIS WEEK, FRANK.

139
00:05:38,973 --> 00:05:40,708
THIS WEEK'S EXPERIMENT
IS CALLED

140
00:05:40,742 --> 00:05:43,043
JACK, MIGHTY JACK.

141
00:05:43,077 --> 00:05:44,712
IT'S PRODUCED
BY FRANK,

142
00:05:44,745 --> 00:05:45,947
SANDY FRANK.

143
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:48,348
OH, PUSH THE BUTTON,
SEND 'EM THE MOVIE, FRANK.

144
00:05:48,382 --> 00:05:50,718
I GOTTA GET OUT OF THESE
SIZE NINES.

145
00:05:50,752 --> 00:05:52,587
- [ALERT BUZZING]
- WHAT, WHAT?

146
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:54,422
OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN,

147
00:05:54,455 --> 00:05:56,057
WHOA!

148
00:05:56,090 --> 00:06:01,695
[GATES OPENING]

149
00:06:04,298 --> 00:06:06,067
THOSE GUYS ARE-- OH.

150
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:07,735
HEY, "MIGHTY JACK".

151
00:06:07,768 --> 00:06:09,303
THE STORY OF A BRAVE PANCAKE

152
00:06:09,337 --> 00:06:11,272
STARRING AUNT JEMIMA
AND FLAP, THE WONDER DOG.

153
00:06:11,305 --> 00:06:13,875
MIGHTY JACK, THE DOG--
ISN'T THAT A DOG FOOD?

154
00:06:13,908 --> 00:06:15,175
- COULD BE.
- I DON'T KNOW.

155
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,343
GOOD IDEA.

156
00:06:16,377 --> 00:06:19,147
FEATURING OUR
ALL VEGETARIAN DISHES.

157
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:22,150
"HITAKI, TERIYAKI,
AND NAOKO KOKO... KOBO."

158
00:06:22,183 --> 00:06:23,483
AH, THEY SHOULD REALLY

159
00:06:23,517 --> 00:06:25,953
WATERPROOF
THIS BASEMENT.

160
00:06:25,987 --> 00:06:27,322
GEORGE...

161
00:06:27,355 --> 00:06:28,688
MARSHA.

162
00:06:28,722 --> 00:06:30,323
CORNJOB.

163
00:06:30,357 --> 00:06:33,060
KIND OF SOAP
OPERA MUSIC HERE.

164
00:06:33,093 --> 00:06:34,462
♪ I AM A LINEMAN ♪

165
00:06:34,495 --> 00:06:36,197
♪ FOR THE STAR FLEET ♪

166
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:38,967
YEE-HOO.

167
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,202
LOVE BUG 2000
STARRING

168
00:06:41,235 --> 00:06:43,003
ADMIRAL GAVIN MACLEOD.

169
00:06:43,037 --> 00:06:44,438
SAY...

170
00:06:44,472 --> 00:06:47,442
[MIMICKING TROTTING HORSE]

171
00:06:47,475 --> 00:06:49,610
WRITERS,
OH BROTHER,

172
00:06:49,643 --> 00:06:51,245
TELL ME ABOUT IT.

173
00:06:51,278 --> 00:06:54,215
[MIMICKING TROTTING HORSE]

174
00:06:54,248 --> 00:06:56,550
NOW THERE'S
JESSIE "THE BODY" VOGEL.

175
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:58,820
[CHUCKLING]

176
00:06:58,853 --> 00:07:00,822
- MAYOR.
- HE'S RIGHT.

177
00:07:00,855 --> 00:07:03,523
[MIMICKING TROTTING HORSE]

178
00:07:03,557 --> 00:07:06,260
YEE-HOO.

179
00:07:06,293 --> 00:07:09,263
I'M NOT TOO PROUD OF THIS,
JUST PRINT MY NAME SMALL.

180
00:07:09,297 --> 00:07:10,898
I DON'T BLAME HIM.

181
00:07:10,932 --> 00:07:13,902
♪♪

182
00:07:13,935 --> 00:07:16,303
OOH, DRAMATIC.

183
00:07:16,337 --> 00:07:17,972
SEX CAMERAMAN,
IS THIS--

184
00:07:18,005 --> 00:07:20,007
- NO, NO, S-F-X, JOEL.
- AAH.

185
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,075
HEY, TWIN EVINRUDES,
YEAH, BUT YOU KNOW,

186
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:24,378
I GOT A BASS BOAT FLYER
UP ON THE FRONT THERE.

187
00:07:24,412 --> 00:07:26,013
YOU GOT ONE OF THEM
BIG BASS CHAIRS UP FRONT?

188
00:07:26,047 --> 00:07:27,248
OH, YOU BET'CHA.

189
00:07:27,282 --> 00:07:28,917
GOTTA KEEP YOUR TIPS UP
WHEN YOU'RE GETTING PULLED

190
00:07:28,950 --> 00:07:30,652
BEHIND ONE OF THEM BABIES.

191
00:07:30,685 --> 00:07:32,253
[TOGETHER]
MIGHTY JACK!

192
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:35,557
HM, WHOA.

193
00:07:35,590 --> 00:07:37,258
COME ON.

194
00:07:37,292 --> 00:07:39,693
WE DON'T
NEED TO SEE THIS.

195
00:07:39,727 --> 00:07:41,062
NO, NO, NO.

196
00:07:41,095 --> 00:07:42,463
DECLARING THAT
IF THEY CONTINUE TO FIGHT

197
00:07:42,497 --> 00:07:45,165
AMONG THEMSELVES THEY FACE
AN EVEN GREATER DANGER

198
00:07:45,198 --> 00:07:47,402
- FROM AN UNEXPECTED SOURCE.
- PEGGY LEE.

199
00:07:47,435 --> 00:07:49,870
AN ORGANIZATION,
KNOWN AS "Q", EQUIPPED...

200
00:07:49,903 --> 00:07:52,072
WHOA, WE'RE FALLING OFF
DON'T DO THAT.

201
00:07:52,105 --> 00:07:53,640
...MORE THAN EVER
TO PURSUE ITS GOAL

202
00:07:53,673 --> 00:07:55,408
OF COMPLETE CONQUEST
OF THE EARTH.

203
00:07:55,442 --> 00:07:57,778
TO CARRY ON
ITS DIABOLICAL SCHEMES...

204
00:07:57,812 --> 00:07:59,780
[JOEL GROANING]
HELP HIM.

205
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:02,850
THAT FUNK & WAGNALLS
IS HEAVY.

206
00:08:02,883 --> 00:08:05,820
AMONG FRIENDLY
PEACE-LOVING COUNTRIES...

207
00:08:05,853 --> 00:08:07,120
LET'S SEE, "P"...

208
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:08,488
KITTY!

209
00:08:08,522 --> 00:08:10,423
CAN NO LONGER STAND BY
SILENTLY AND TOLERATE...

210
00:08:10,457 --> 00:08:12,227
JAPANESE CALVIN AND HOBBES.

211
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:14,728
THEREFORE, THE PRESIDENT
PROPOSES TO FORM

212
00:08:14,762 --> 00:08:17,365
A TEAM OF SPECIALLY
TRAINED MEN AND WOMEN

213
00:08:17,398 --> 00:08:20,200
TO COMBAT THE ORGANIZATION
KNOWN AS Q AND STOP...

214
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:22,870
CUE FOR THE NARRATOR.

215
00:08:22,903 --> 00:08:25,873
THIS TEAM WILL BE
CODE NAMED MIGHTY JACK.

216
00:08:25,907 --> 00:08:27,342
USING THE LATEST TECHNOLOGY,

217
00:08:27,375 --> 00:08:29,043
MIGHTY JACK WILL HAVE
AS ITS MISSION

218
00:08:29,077 --> 00:08:30,745
THE ANNIHILATION OF THE
ORGANIZATION KNOWN AS Q.

219
00:08:30,778 --> 00:08:31,978
[SNORING]

220
00:08:32,012 --> 00:08:33,647
BUT IT WILL NOT BE AN
EASY TASK.

221
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:35,282
FOR Q IS CLEVER...

222
00:08:35,315 --> 00:08:38,285
[LOUD SNORING]

223
00:08:38,318 --> 00:08:39,987
- START!
- CUE THAT UP!

224
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,488
[CHUCKLING]

225
00:08:41,522 --> 00:08:43,823
LIVE FROM
THE Q-NOTE CAFE,

226
00:08:43,857 --> 00:08:45,392
THE Q-TIPS.

227
00:08:45,425 --> 00:08:47,895
[JAZZ PLAYING]

228
00:08:47,928 --> 00:08:49,563
TOKYO, 10:00 A.M.

229
00:08:49,597 --> 00:08:52,300
DO YOU KNOW
WHERE YOUR CHILDREN ARE?

230
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:54,135
SAIGON, 7:30 A.M.

231
00:08:54,168 --> 00:08:55,770
HEY, HE'S EATING
Q-RATIONS.

232
00:08:55,803 --> 00:08:57,405
HMMM.

233
00:08:57,438 --> 00:09:00,173
MOSCOW,
IT'S 7:00 A.M.

234
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:01,742
AND PARIS, 2:00 A.M.

235
00:09:01,775 --> 00:09:04,445
AH, PARIS, CITY OF LAMPS.

236
00:09:04,478 --> 00:09:06,947
HEY, LOOK, RICHARD CARPENTER'S
GETTING DRUNK.

237
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:09,417
UNBELIEVABLE AND KAREN.

238
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:11,952
- COME ON, FINISH IT.
- FINISH IT, WHOO!

239
00:09:11,985 --> 00:09:14,122
HEY, GERALDINE FERRARO.

240
00:09:14,155 --> 00:09:17,057
OH.

241
00:09:17,090 --> 00:09:18,425
WHO'S THE GUY?

242
00:09:18,458 --> 00:09:19,460
[WHISPERING]
GIRL.

243
00:09:19,493 --> 00:09:21,395
HEY, IT'S JFK.

244
00:09:21,428 --> 00:09:23,363
WOW.

245
00:09:23,397 --> 00:09:24,765
BOBBY.

246
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:28,568
OKAY, LET'S SEE NOW.

247
00:09:28,602 --> 00:09:30,805
WHY DO BEES
SUDDENLY REAPPEAR...

248
00:09:30,838 --> 00:09:33,807
OH, SCREW IT, FORGET IT.

249
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,242
MONSIEUR?

250
00:09:35,275 --> 00:09:38,145
WON'T YOU STAY WITH
ME A FEW MORE MINUTES?

251
00:09:38,178 --> 00:09:40,313
WHILE I SPACKLE MY TEETH?

252
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:44,585
HEY, DJANGO REINHARDT.

253
00:09:44,618 --> 00:09:47,287
- NAH, TOO MANY FINGERS.
- OH, YOU'RE RIGHT.

254
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,890
A JAPANESE IN PARIS.

255
00:09:49,923 --> 00:09:52,593
[MIMICKING JAPANESE ACCENT TO
"AN AMERICAN IN PARIS" THEME"

256
00:09:52,627 --> 00:09:54,262
[CHUCKLING]

257
00:09:54,295 --> 00:09:55,262
WAS THAT KIND OF RACIST?

258
00:09:55,295 --> 00:09:58,265
NO, NO,
I DON'T THINK SO.

259
00:09:58,298 --> 00:10:01,268
- DOOR IS AJAR.
- DING-DONG.

260
00:10:01,302 --> 00:10:03,403
- IGNITE CIGARETTE.
- DING-DONG.

261
00:10:03,437 --> 00:10:05,572
HAVE SECOND THOUGHTS
ABOUT GIRL IN BAR.

262
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:07,342
DING-DONG.

263
00:10:07,375 --> 00:10:09,043
[CHUCKLES]

264
00:10:09,077 --> 00:10:10,377
HEY.

265
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,948
♪♪

266
00:10:14,982 --> 00:10:17,652
[WITH FRENCH ACCENT]
OH, LORD, WON'T YOU BUY
ME A MERCEDES BENZ.

267
00:10:17,685 --> 00:10:20,620
MY FRIENDS
ALL DRIVE PORCHES...

268
00:10:20,653 --> 00:10:22,923
AH, WE'RE COMING TO THE FORK
IN THE PLOT.

269
00:10:24,592 --> 00:10:27,362
- DON'T TAKE A WRONG TURN.
- WHAT?

270
00:10:27,395 --> 00:10:29,630
WELL, IT'S KIND OF A KEITH
HARING PAINTING IT LOOKS LIKE.

271
00:10:29,663 --> 00:10:31,332
HUH?

272
00:10:31,365 --> 00:10:32,500
WHOA!

273
00:10:32,533 --> 00:10:33,533
[TIRES SCREECH]

274
00:10:33,567 --> 00:10:35,068
OTON, ICHTON,
SCHLOTOMEYER.

275
00:10:35,102 --> 00:10:37,805
SHH, IXNAY, FRENCH.

276
00:10:37,838 --> 00:10:39,207
OH, BONJOUR.

277
00:10:42,108 --> 00:10:43,710
HUH?

278
00:10:43,743 --> 00:10:45,678
SHIELD YOUR EYES
FROM THE NET!

279
00:10:45,712 --> 00:10:47,280
OOH, BIG, BIG.

280
00:10:49,683 --> 00:10:51,985
IT'S THE HELICOPTER
FROM "DAKTARI."

281
00:10:52,018 --> 00:10:54,822
OH, THEY'RE GONNA RETURN
THAT JAPANESE CAR TO THE WILD.

282
00:10:54,855 --> 00:10:56,790
- OH.
- THEY GOTTA TAG IT.

283
00:10:56,823 --> 00:10:58,858
BON VOYAGE!

284
00:10:58,892 --> 00:11:01,062
YOU WILL ALWAYS
HAVE "PAREE!"

285
00:11:03,397 --> 00:11:04,865
- OH, BOY.
- [HORN HONKING]

286
00:11:04,898 --> 00:11:07,033
YOU CAN ALWAYS TELL
IT'S A JAPANESE NET,

287
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,335
IT'S FILLED WITH DOLPHINS.

288
00:11:08,368 --> 00:11:10,170
OH, WHAT A BURN.

289
00:11:10,203 --> 00:11:13,173
[MAN]
JUST RELAX, MR. ATARI,
AND ENJOY THE RIDE,

290
00:11:13,207 --> 00:11:15,708
- IT'S A BEAUTIFUL NIGHT.
- FOR A MOONDANCE.

291
00:11:15,742 --> 00:11:18,712
LOOK, WHAT DO YOU
THINK YOU'RE DOING?

292
00:11:18,745 --> 00:11:21,715
[MAN]
YOUR ALTITUDE IS 2,000 FEET.

293
00:11:21,748 --> 00:11:24,118
I'M SURE YOU'LL ENJOY
THE VIEW,

294
00:11:24,152 --> 00:11:25,485
GOOD NIGHT.

295
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:26,887
TO YOUR LEFT YOU'LL SEE

296
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,523
THE CHAMPS-ÉLYSÉES
AND THE RIVE GAUCHE.

297
00:11:29,557 --> 00:11:31,958
THIS IS NO PLACE
FOR A CONVERTIBLE.

298
00:11:35,328 --> 00:11:37,030
JOHN WAYNE IS BRANNIGAN.

299
00:11:38,932 --> 00:11:40,935
MEDICAL CENTER
IN COLOR.

300
00:11:40,968 --> 00:11:43,937
OOH-HOO,
THAT'S GOOD WEED.

301
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:45,807
HMM-MMM.

302
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,240
HEY, IT'S J. EDGAR HOOVER.

303
00:11:47,273 --> 00:11:49,110
I WILL CRUSH
THE KENNEDYS.

304
00:11:49,143 --> 00:11:50,310
COME IN.

305
00:11:54,448 --> 00:11:56,717
IT'S REGARDING
MR. ATARI, COLONEL.

306
00:11:56,750 --> 00:11:59,153
I'VE MADE SEVERAL CALLS
TO PARIS TO TRY TO GET MORE

307
00:11:59,187 --> 00:12:01,588
DETAILED INFORMATION.

308
00:12:01,622 --> 00:12:02,857
ON THE DAY HE DISAPPEARED,

309
00:12:02,890 --> 00:12:05,860
MR. ATARI LEFT THE CABARET
AT 2:00 IN THE MORNING.

310
00:12:05,893 --> 00:12:09,197
DROVE PAST
THE PORT DORDOGNE
HEADING SOUTH.

311
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:11,732
AND THEN HE SUDDENLY DISAPPEARED
ALONG THE HIGHWAY SOMEWHERE.

312
00:12:11,765 --> 00:12:14,235
AND THE AIRPORTS?

313
00:12:14,268 --> 00:12:15,635
- NOTHING AS YET.
- [SNICKERING]

314
00:12:15,668 --> 00:12:17,403
[SNICKERING CONTINUES]

315
00:12:22,877 --> 00:12:25,545
ALL RIGHT, THAT'LL BE ALL,
THANK YOU.

316
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:26,847
OH, GOD.

317
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:29,283
[SNIFFING]

318
00:12:29,317 --> 00:12:31,118
I AM SO HIGH.

319
00:12:31,152 --> 00:12:34,087
[THINKING]
IT'S NOT A CASE
OF ROBBERY.

320
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,590
I'D BETTER
CONTACT MIGHTY JACK.

321
00:12:36,623 --> 00:12:39,593
WHY IS MY INTERNAL VOICE
DIFFERENT FROM EXTERNAL VOICE?

322
00:12:39,627 --> 00:12:41,595
INSIDE I'M TAN
AND HANDSOME.

323
00:12:41,628 --> 00:12:44,097
OUTSIDE, I'M THE GRINCH
WHO STOLE CHRISTMAS.

324
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:47,100
[DIALING ROTARY PHONE]

325
00:12:47,133 --> 00:12:49,803
[KISSING SOUNDS]

326
00:12:49,837 --> 00:12:52,138
HELLO?

327
00:12:52,172 --> 00:12:54,942
HELLO, IS THAT YOU,
CATHERINE?

328
00:12:54,975 --> 00:12:57,912
HEY, WHAT ARE
THEY OPENING A BOUTIQUE?

329
00:13:01,182 --> 00:13:03,150
SHE'LL NOT HAVE MY APPLE.

330
00:13:03,183 --> 00:13:05,987
IT'S MINE.

331
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:07,522
HERE'S THE MESSAGE
FROM COLONEL YABUKI.

332
00:13:07,555 --> 00:13:08,922
MY BOOKIE?

333
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:11,292
I WANT YOU TO RESCUE
A CERTAIN MAN.

334
00:13:11,325 --> 00:13:13,860
HE DISAPPEARED
SUDDENLY NEAR PARIS.

335
00:13:13,893 --> 00:13:15,495
HE'S VERY IMPORTANT
TO MIGHTY JACK.

336
00:13:15,528 --> 00:13:18,498
IT COULD BE A DANGEROUS
MISSION SO BE CAREFUL.

337
00:13:18,532 --> 00:13:20,968
OH, AND SABRINA,
YOU POSE AS A SCIENTIST

338
00:13:21,002 --> 00:13:23,470
AND WEAR THAT STRING
BIKINI WE GOT YOU.

339
00:13:23,503 --> 00:13:25,372
THAT'S THE MAN.

340
00:13:25,405 --> 00:13:26,807
SAY, THAT'S A MAN?
OH.

341
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,242
HOW INTERESTING.

342
00:13:28,275 --> 00:13:31,045
OH... YOU KNOW A LOT OF
GIRLS THAT LOOK LIKE THAT?

343
00:13:31,078 --> 00:13:32,378
THIS ONE I DO.

344
00:13:32,412 --> 00:13:34,815
- SHE'S A WELL-KNOWN DANCER.
- COOL.

345
00:13:34,848 --> 00:13:37,350
SHE'S NOT MISSING,
IT'S THE MAN WE'RE LOOKING FOR.

346
00:13:37,383 --> 00:13:38,952
OH, TOO BAD.

347
00:13:38,985 --> 00:13:41,155
SO HE'S OUR NEXT
ASSIGNMENT.

348
00:13:41,188 --> 00:13:42,488
MEASURE IT.

349
00:13:42,522 --> 00:13:44,692
HIS NAME
IS HAROLD ATARI.

350
00:13:44,725 --> 00:13:47,762
HE'S A PROFESSIONAL
MOUNTAINEER.

351
00:13:47,795 --> 00:13:50,730
♪♪

352
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:54,968
WHAT ABOUT THAT TRANSMITTER?

353
00:13:55,002 --> 00:13:57,170
I KIND OF LOOKS LIKE
THE $10,000 PYRAMID HERE.

354
00:13:57,203 --> 00:13:58,638
WHAT'S BEING DONE
TO FIND IT?

355
00:13:58,672 --> 00:14:01,375
CAPTAIN TENDA AND LIEUTENANT
JERRY ARE OUT SEARCHING

356
00:14:01,408 --> 00:14:02,442
WITH THE ELECTRO SCOUT.

357
00:14:02,475 --> 00:14:03,977
AH, THINGS YOU
SAY IN A DOLLY SHOT.

358
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:06,180
WELL, THE MAXIMUM RANGE
IS 700 MILES.

359
00:14:06,213 --> 00:14:07,882
UH, THINGS
YOU'D SAY TO MARCONI.

360
00:14:07,915 --> 00:14:10,383
THERE SHOULDN'T BE ANY PROBLEM
IF IT'S WITHIN THAT RADIUS.

361
00:14:10,417 --> 00:14:11,652
THINGS YOU
KEEP IN YOUR PURSE.

362
00:14:11,685 --> 00:14:12,820
HMM.

363
00:14:12,853 --> 00:14:14,488
THERE'S ONE SLIGHT
PROBLEM, THOUGH.

364
00:14:14,522 --> 00:14:15,957
UH, THINGS YOU
SAY WHEN YOU'RE DIM.

365
00:14:15,990 --> 00:14:17,992
MR. ATARI DOESN'T KNOW HE HAS
THE TRANSMITTER ON HIM.

366
00:14:18,025 --> 00:14:20,593
THEN HE WON'T
KNOW THAT WE...

367
00:14:20,627 --> 00:14:22,162
YOU SEE, CATHERINE,

368
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:24,163
I HAD IT ISSUED
MERELY AS A PRECAUTION THAT...

369
00:14:24,197 --> 00:14:25,565
THINGS YOU SAY IN A TEACUP.

370
00:14:25,598 --> 00:14:27,735
... MR. ATARI WAS CALLED AWAY
VERY SUDDENLY,

371
00:14:27,768 --> 00:14:30,070
BEFORE HE WAS
INSTRUCTED IN ITS USES.

372
00:14:30,103 --> 00:14:32,572
IF HE DOESN'T FIND
IT, THEN.

373
00:14:32,605 --> 00:14:35,042
- SOONER OR LATER...
- LOVE IS GOING TO GET YOU.

374
00:14:35,075 --> 00:14:36,477
... HE WILL DISCOVER
THAT HE HAS IT ON HIM.

375
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:39,480
BLESS US, OUR BUDDHA, THESE--
WAIT, I'M NOT A BUDDHIST.

376
00:14:39,513 --> 00:14:42,482
YOU'RE SHINTO.

377
00:14:42,515 --> 00:14:44,485
WAIT A MINUTE.

378
00:14:44,518 --> 00:14:46,287
BUTTON, BUTTON,

379
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,088
I'VE GOT THE BUTTON.

380
00:14:48,122 --> 00:14:49,990
AND I'M GONNA USE
IT, TOO.

381
00:14:51,892 --> 00:14:54,462
HMM, THE BUTTON'S
KIND OF DULL.

382
00:14:54,495 --> 00:14:56,763
HMM, LIKE THIS MOVIE?

383
00:14:56,797 --> 00:14:58,498
[CHUCKLING]

384
00:14:58,532 --> 00:15:00,133
WOO!

385
00:15:02,435 --> 00:15:04,905
HAZA, ALAKAZAM,
AND I'M GONE.

386
00:15:04,938 --> 00:15:07,040
OH, I GOTTA
WORK ON THAT.

387
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:09,175
GOT THE PATTER DOWN,
THOUGH.

388
00:15:09,208 --> 00:15:12,145
IF I'M NOT MISTAKEN
I SHOULD HAVE A RABBIT
OVER THERE AT LEAST.

389
00:15:13,513 --> 00:15:14,848
OH?

390
00:15:14,882 --> 00:15:17,083
[GASPING]

391
00:15:18,818 --> 00:15:20,787
I WAS JUST
DAYDREAMING, DOCTOR.

392
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:22,757
GOD.

393
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:25,292
VERY WELL,
AND WHEN ARE YOU COMING BACK?

394
00:15:25,325 --> 00:15:26,960
I'M NOT SURE.

395
00:15:26,993 --> 00:15:28,695
DON'T STAY AWAY
TOO LONG.

396
00:15:28,728 --> 00:15:31,265
IF YOU
KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

397
00:15:31,298 --> 00:15:34,267
YOU'VE ALWAYS BEEN
ONE OF OUR BEST MEN.

398
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,137
- THANK YOU, SIR.
- I THINK.

399
00:15:36,170 --> 00:15:38,672
OH, DO YOU
SEE THAT BOX THERE?

400
00:15:38,705 --> 00:15:41,575
THAT SUIT, IT'S MY PARTING
GIFT TO YOU.

401
00:15:41,608 --> 00:15:44,277
FROM SPIEGEL,
CHICAGO, ILLINOIS, 60609.

402
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:45,878
WAIT A MINUTE,
IS THIS A FLASHBACK.

403
00:15:45,912 --> 00:15:47,948
I-I-I'M LOST.

404
00:15:50,850 --> 00:15:53,587
HMM, GOOD WORKMANSHIP--
MORTY MUST'VE MADE THIS.

405
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,422
NICE HANKEY POOF, TOO.

406
00:15:55,455 --> 00:15:56,957
HMM,
WHAT A WEIRD GUY,

407
00:15:56,990 --> 00:15:59,927
HE GIVES LOVELY PARTING GIFTS
AFTER A MEETING BUT I--

408
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:02,462
HM?

409
00:16:02,495 --> 00:16:04,932
YOU HEAR ANYTHING?

410
00:16:04,965 --> 00:16:07,433
NO, I'VE GOT WOOD CLAMPS
ON MY EARS.

411
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:08,968
IT'S NO USE.

412
00:16:09,002 --> 00:16:10,637
I'M NOT
GETTING A SIGNAL.

413
00:16:10,670 --> 00:16:13,240
I'M GOING TO TRY
FURTHER WEST.

414
00:16:13,273 --> 00:16:15,942
CREST, CREST.

415
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:17,812
[MIMICKING FLATULENCE]

416
00:16:17,845 --> 00:16:19,278
HA-HA,
I LOVE THAT ONE.

417
00:16:21,482 --> 00:16:22,950
[IMITATING MR. ROGERS]
HI, BOYS AND GIRLS,

418
00:16:22,983 --> 00:16:24,317
I'M GONNA TAKE MY SHOES OFF

419
00:16:24,350 --> 00:16:26,053
AND PUT MY LITTLE
SNEAKERS ON.

420
00:16:26,087 --> 00:16:27,387
[SNIFFING]

421
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:28,988
[ALL GAGGING]
OH, MAN,

422
00:16:29,022 --> 00:16:30,423
YOU NEED DR. SCHOLLS.

423
00:16:30,457 --> 00:16:33,093
IT EITHER SMELLS LIKE BAD MEAT
OR GOOD CHEESE, OOH!

424
00:16:33,127 --> 00:16:34,662
PHEW!

425
00:16:34,695 --> 00:16:36,530
IF I'M NOT MISTAKEN,
THERE'S A PHONE--

426
00:16:36,563 --> 00:16:39,533
UH, OH-NO,
THAT'S JUST MY INSOLE.

427
00:16:39,567 --> 00:16:41,335
OH, I SEE,
THERE'S A HEE--

428
00:16:41,368 --> 00:16:42,870
A REALLY GOOD HEE--

429
00:16:42,903 --> 00:16:44,370
WHAT?

430
00:16:44,403 --> 00:16:46,940
OH, WOW, CHERRY CORDIALS,

431
00:16:46,973 --> 00:16:48,942
WHAT A THOUGHTFUL
OLD MAN.

432
00:16:51,077 --> 00:16:52,378
SEE.

433
00:16:55,015 --> 00:16:56,683
OH, PLAYING
HOUSE IS FUN.

434
00:16:56,717 --> 00:16:58,418
TABLE FOR TWO, SIR?

435
00:16:58,452 --> 00:17:00,720
OH, OUI, OUI.

436
00:17:00,753 --> 00:17:04,525
I'M HAVING A TEA PARTY
FOR MY LITTLE FRIENDS.

437
00:17:04,558 --> 00:17:05,792
OOH.

438
00:17:05,825 --> 00:17:07,327
COATS A REAL RIP-OFF.

439
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,895
WOULDN'T YOU SAY THAT?

440
00:17:08,928 --> 00:17:12,465
LET'S SEE, UH, PAPERCLIP,
AND OLD STICK OF GUM... UH.

441
00:17:12,498 --> 00:17:15,102
SEE WHAT ELSE I GOT IN HERE.

442
00:17:15,135 --> 00:17:18,138
A BUNCH OF PEANUT SHELLS FROM
THAT KARAOKE BAR STUCK IN THERE.

443
00:17:18,172 --> 00:17:19,573
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

444
00:17:19,607 --> 00:17:20,973
WELL,
HE'S BUILDING A MEAL.

445
00:17:21,007 --> 00:17:23,943
YOU SEE, HE'S GOT THE FOUR
BUTTON GROUPS, CHECK 'EM OUT.

446
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:29,517
[HUMMING]

447
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:32,218
I DID IT ONE PIECE AT A TIME
AND IT DIDN'T COST ME A DIME.

448
00:17:32,252 --> 00:17:33,987
[HUMMING]

449
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:36,190
OH, GREAT, THE INSTRUCTIONS
ARE IN JAPANESE.

450
00:17:36,223 --> 00:17:37,523
D'OH!

451
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:39,560
[HUMMING]

452
00:17:39,593 --> 00:17:41,962
♪ PEOPLE COME FROM TREES ♪

453
00:17:41,995 --> 00:17:44,732
[HUMMING]

454
00:17:44,765 --> 00:17:46,733
[CHUCKLING]
IT'S A ONE-HITTER.

455
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:48,668
[CHUCKLING]

456
00:17:50,537 --> 00:17:52,105
WHAT'S HE DOING THERE?

457
00:17:52,138 --> 00:17:56,310
THAT REALLY HELD HIS
TIE IN PLACE, DIDN'T IT?

458
00:17:56,343 --> 00:17:59,212
MAYBE HE CAN GET INTO THE CRAFT
FAIR NEXT YEAR WITH THAT.

459
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:02,148
[BEEPING]

460
00:18:02,182 --> 00:18:04,250
THEY MIGHT
BE MONITORING IT.

461
00:18:04,283 --> 00:18:05,985
THEY MIGHT BE
GIANTS.

462
00:18:06,018 --> 00:18:08,488
[BEEPING]

463
00:18:08,522 --> 00:18:09,890
- THERE IT IS AGAIN.
- [BEEPING]

464
00:18:09,923 --> 00:18:11,123
THIS IS ONLY A TEST,

465
00:18:11,157 --> 00:18:14,360
HAD THIS BEEN
AN ACTUAL MOVIE...

466
00:18:14,393 --> 00:18:16,430
IT'S GONE AGAIN.

467
00:18:16,463 --> 00:18:18,298
THERE'S ONE THING
PRETTY SURE, THOUGH.

468
00:18:18,332 --> 00:18:19,600
THAT WAS ON
THE 20-METER BAND.

469
00:18:19,633 --> 00:18:21,768
- BOOTY'S 20-METER BAND?
- RUBBER.

470
00:18:21,802 --> 00:18:24,203
IT'S MUCH TOO FAR
TO FIGURE OUT, SIR.

471
00:18:24,237 --> 00:18:26,507
TRY TO GET THE GENERAL
DIRECTION.

472
00:18:28,308 --> 00:18:29,710
- UH, THAT WAY?
- PACIFIC OCEAN.

473
00:18:29,743 --> 00:18:31,245
A SPECIFIC OCEAN?

474
00:18:31,278 --> 00:18:34,782
YEAH, BUT WHICH ONE, BE MORE
"PACIFIC," HA-HA!

475
00:18:34,815 --> 00:18:36,583
- JERRY, LOOK.
- JERRY?

476
00:18:36,617 --> 00:18:39,518
DEAN, WE'RE FLYING IN
THE THING WITH...
[IMITATING JERRY LEWIS]

477
00:18:42,588 --> 00:18:44,223
OH, LOOK.

478
00:18:44,257 --> 00:18:46,827
THAT MUST BE A WEDDING,
THEY'RE THROWING RICE.

479
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:48,362
REALLY BIG RICE.

480
00:18:48,395 --> 00:18:51,865
THEY'RE HOLDING HANDS
AND SKIMMING STONE.

481
00:18:51,898 --> 00:18:53,500
TOY BOAT.

482
00:18:53,533 --> 00:18:56,102
[ALL]
TOY BOAT, TOY BOAT,
TOY BOAT.

483
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,470
TOY BOAT.

484
00:18:57,503 --> 00:19:00,373
OH, IT'S THE CAPTAIN
OF THE VALDEZ, THERE.

485
00:19:00,407 --> 00:19:03,343
HM, STATELY, PLUMP BUCK MULLIGAN
CAME DOWN FROM THE STAIRWELL--

486
00:19:03,377 --> 00:19:04,878
THIS BOOK IS AWFUL.

487
00:19:04,912 --> 00:19:06,447
NO PICTURES.

488
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,915
[MAN]
DOCTOR!

489
00:19:07,948 --> 00:19:10,383
I GOT THIS
AWFUL HEADACHE.

490
00:19:10,417 --> 00:19:11,685
OKAY, CLIMB IN.

491
00:19:11,718 --> 00:19:13,320
LOOKS LIKE
YOU'RE HOMESICK AGAIN.

492
00:19:13,353 --> 00:19:15,722
NO, NO, IT'S NOT
THAT AT ALL.

493
00:19:15,755 --> 00:19:17,657
IT'S THOSE
CRAZY RADIO SIGNALS.

494
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:19,860
THEY GET LOUDER AND SOFTER
AND SOFTER AND LOUDER.

495
00:19:19,893 --> 00:19:21,895
THEY'RE DRIVING
ME OUT OF MY MIND.

496
00:19:21,928 --> 00:19:23,030
[CHUCKLING]

497
00:19:23,063 --> 00:19:24,765
BUT I'M GETTING A LOT
OF INTERFERENCE.

498
00:19:24,798 --> 00:19:27,800
THEY'RE TRANSMITTING
ABOUT EVERY TEN MINUTES.

499
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:31,472
BUTYL NITRATE?

500
00:19:31,505 --> 00:19:33,507
UH, SOMETHING SUSPICIOUS,
THOUGH.

501
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,808
THERE'S NO STATION
ON THE 20-METER BAND.

502
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:37,410
IT'S A CALAMITY.

503
00:19:37,443 --> 00:19:39,647
YOU SAY IT'S
ON THE 20-METER BAND?

504
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,180
YEAH.

505
00:19:41,213 --> 00:19:43,317
MAYBE THAT'S ATARI.

506
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:45,785
TRY TO GET THE EXACT DIRECTION
OF THOSE SIGNALS.

507
00:19:45,818 --> 00:19:47,287
DO IT IMMEDIATELY.

508
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,388
COULDN'T YOU GIVE ME SOME
MEDICINE FIRST, DOCTOR?

509
00:19:49,422 --> 00:19:52,225
I'D PRESCRIBE ME,
DR. JACK FEELGOOD.

510
00:19:52,258 --> 00:19:54,862
MEANWHILE, BACK
ON THE GREASY BASTARD.

511
00:19:54,895 --> 00:19:56,997
WHEN DID YOU START
HEARING THEM?

512
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:58,332
WHEN I WAS TEN.

513
00:19:58,365 --> 00:20:00,467
I PICKED UP THE FIRST
SIGNALS A FEW DAYS AGO.

514
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:03,770
I WAS TRYING TO GET HEADQUARTERS
BUT RECEPTION WAS BAD

515
00:20:03,803 --> 00:20:06,607
SO I CHANGED
WAVEBANDS AND NOTICED IT.

516
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:09,643
NOW I'M GETTING THE RUSH
LIMBAUGH SHOW.

517
00:20:09,677 --> 00:20:13,080
OH, DOCTOR, THAT'S IT.

518
00:20:13,113 --> 00:20:15,315
SEE IF YOU CAN GET
THE EXACT LOCATION.

519
00:20:15,348 --> 00:20:16,750
YES, SIR.

520
00:20:16,783 --> 00:20:19,452
ENOUGH OF THESE DAMN
BUREAUCRATS IN WASHINGTON

521
00:20:19,485 --> 00:20:22,288
SPENDING ALL OUR HARD-EARNED
DOLLARS IN LAZY WELFARE SLUMS.

522
00:20:22,322 --> 00:20:23,523
BACK IN A MOMENT.

523
00:20:23,557 --> 00:20:25,225
THIS IS MY LAST CHANCE,
I MUST RISK IT.

524
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:28,728
[TONE SIGNALING]

525
00:20:28,762 --> 00:20:32,098
THIS IS LAY CANON WITH
THE JAZZ IMAGE, TONIGHT.

526
00:20:32,132 --> 00:20:35,835
- [TOM IMITATING BASS LINE]
- THAT'S THE SIGNAL.

527
00:20:35,868 --> 00:20:38,672
IT'S VERY CLOSE,
IT'S HIM ALL RIGHT.

528
00:20:38,705 --> 00:20:40,640
- HIM?
- IT'S ATARI.

529
00:20:40,673 --> 00:20:42,708
STOP THEM TRANSMITTING
THOSE SIGNALS.

530
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:46,045
ISN'T THAT
RIGHT, FLOPSY?

531
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:48,215
- [GASPS]
- HUH?

532
00:20:50,917 --> 00:20:52,652
[GASPS]
OH, NO.

533
00:20:52,685 --> 00:20:55,355
OH, NO, IT'S THE SHOWER MASSAGE
BY WATERPIK.

534
00:20:58,592 --> 00:21:00,227
- ARE THE SIGNALS GONE?
- YES, SIR.

535
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:02,762
ONLY THEY LASTED OVER
FIVE MINUTES THIS TIME.

536
00:21:02,795 --> 00:21:04,430
WOW.

537
00:21:04,463 --> 00:21:06,433
GOOD, DID YOU GET
THE LOCATION?

538
00:21:06,467 --> 00:21:08,935
YES, 7-0-7-0.

539
00:21:08,968 --> 00:21:10,603
[ALL]
SUNSET STRIP.

540
00:21:10,637 --> 00:21:11,738
OKAY.

541
00:21:11,772 --> 00:21:13,573
- I CAN'T DO THAT.
- YOU GET AN "A".

542
00:21:13,607 --> 00:21:15,808
[CHUCKLES]

543
00:21:15,842 --> 00:21:18,745
DR. HYDE HEARD SIGNALS
ON OUR EMERGENCY BAND.

544
00:21:18,778 --> 00:21:21,815
HE'S EITHER KEITH RICHARDS
OR HE'S DEAD.

545
00:21:21,848 --> 00:21:24,017
I CAN'T QUITE TELL.

546
00:21:24,050 --> 00:21:25,918
THE FREQUENCY'S THE SAME AS ON
MR. ATARI'S TRANSMITTER.

547
00:21:25,952 --> 00:21:27,287
DOES ANYONE
KNOW WHAT'S GOING ON?

548
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:29,990
ANYONE?
LIME-GREEN, ORANGE-ORANGE.

549
00:21:30,023 --> 00:21:31,925
THERE'S NO
ISLAND IN THAT AREA.

550
00:21:31,958 --> 00:21:33,860
IT COULD BE A SHIP.

551
00:21:33,893 --> 00:21:36,262
THEY SAY THE TRANSMITTER
WAS STATIONARY.

552
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,498
WELL, THEY SAY THAT
FALLING IN LOVE IS WONDERFUL.

553
00:21:38,532 --> 00:21:41,402
THEN IT MUST BE AN ISLAND.

554
00:21:41,435 --> 00:21:44,403
WELL, THEN, WE'D BETTER
SEND OUT MIGHTY JACK.

555
00:21:44,437 --> 00:21:45,938
HMM, HE LIVES IN A DRAWER?

556
00:21:45,972 --> 00:21:47,640
OH, YEA-- NO.

557
00:21:55,148 --> 00:21:56,683
UNZIP ME, WOULD YA?

558
00:21:56,717 --> 00:21:58,052
WE'LL LINK UP
WITH MIGHTY JACK SOON.

559
00:21:58,085 --> 00:21:59,485
YES, SIR.

560
00:21:59,518 --> 00:22:01,120
WHAT A WILD SENSATION
THAT'LL BE.

561
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,688
WHOO.

562
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:10,130
HMM.

563
00:22:10,163 --> 00:22:13,433
AH, THIS MUST BE THE SYMBOLIC,
CINEMATIC LOVE SCENE.

564
00:22:13,467 --> 00:22:14,968
OOH.

565
00:22:17,370 --> 00:22:19,807
[HUMMING]

566
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,207
ALL RIGHT,
FULL SPEED AHEAD.

567
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:23,810
- ELVIS COSTELLO.
- OH, COOL.

568
00:22:23,843 --> 00:22:26,813
COURSE SOUTHWEST.

569
00:22:26,847 --> 00:22:29,415
- DECORATE IN PINK AND BLUE.
- WE MUST BE CAREFUL.

570
00:22:29,448 --> 00:22:31,485
THAT MAN
STOLE THEIR HOSTAGE.

571
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:37,657
HMM, NICE.

572
00:22:39,058 --> 00:22:40,560
AW, NOW HE'S GOTTA
WATCH HAZEL,

573
00:22:40,593 --> 00:22:43,530
- STRAPPED IN THE
ERIC ROBERTS SEX CHAIR.
- MR. ATARI.

574
00:22:43,563 --> 00:22:45,532
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

575
00:22:45,565 --> 00:22:47,833
[MAN]
I WANT YOU TO TELL
US ABOUT YOUR MISSION.

576
00:22:47,867 --> 00:22:49,002
NEVER.

577
00:22:49,035 --> 00:22:50,803
THEN TELL US
ABOUT THE RABBITS, GEORGE.

578
00:22:50,837 --> 00:22:53,807
[MAN]
AS LONG AS YOU COOPERATE,
NO HARM WILL COME TO YOU.

579
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:56,577
WELL, I'D CALL THAT HARM.

580
00:22:56,610 --> 00:22:58,778
OOH.

581
00:22:58,812 --> 00:23:01,013
[MAN]
THOSE LIGHTS ARE
CAPABLE OF BLINDING YOU.

582
00:23:01,047 --> 00:23:02,948
I'M NOT AFRAID,
I'LL KEEP MY EYES CLOSED

583
00:23:02,982 --> 00:23:04,117
BUT I WON'T ANSWER ANY
QUESTIONS.

584
00:23:04,150 --> 00:23:05,385
WOW, IS HE SMART.

585
00:23:05,418 --> 00:23:06,920
[MAN]
YOU'RE BEING VERY FOOLISH.

586
00:23:06,953 --> 00:23:09,823
SOON, YOU'LL OPEN YOUR EYES AND
THEN YOU'LL BE BLINDED FOR LIFE.

587
00:23:09,857 --> 00:23:11,825
TELL US ONE THING.

588
00:23:11,858 --> 00:23:13,527
WHERE IS
COMEDY CENTRAL?

589
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,395
WHERE'S MIGHTY JACK'S
SECRET BASE?

590
00:23:15,428 --> 00:23:17,497
I DON'T KNOW.

591
00:23:17,530 --> 00:23:18,832
HEY, HE'S GETTING
TAN AND HANDSOME IN THERE.

592
00:23:18,865 --> 00:23:20,133
I DON'T KNOW ANYTHING.

593
00:23:20,167 --> 00:23:23,370
ATARI, YOU MUSTN'T UNDERESTIMATE
THE STRENGTH OF Q.

594
00:23:23,403 --> 00:23:25,338
OUR AGENTS
ARE EVERYWHERE.

595
00:23:25,372 --> 00:23:27,873
PARIS, BERLIN, LONDON,
MADRID.

596
00:23:27,907 --> 00:23:30,177
- FRESNO.
- WHY DID THEY SEND YOU
TO PARIS?

597
00:23:30,210 --> 00:23:32,245
'CAUSE I LOVES PARIS IN
THE SPRINGTIME, THAT'S WHY.

598
00:23:32,278 --> 00:23:34,513
I WAS THERE TO MEET A BUSINESS
COLLEAGUE OF MINE.

599
00:23:34,547 --> 00:23:35,782
WE SELL AMWAY.

600
00:23:35,815 --> 00:23:37,983
- AND THEN I DID
A LITTLE SIGHTSEEING.
- HMM.

601
00:23:38,017 --> 00:23:40,387
IT IS NO USE STALLING.

602
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:42,788
I PROMISE WE'LL
LET YOU GO.

603
00:23:42,822 --> 00:23:46,927
BUT FIRST, YOU HAVE TO TELL
US EVERYTHING WE WANT TO KNOW.

604
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:49,897
BUT NO SLIDES.

605
00:23:49,930 --> 00:23:52,465
[MAN]
YOU CAN'T HOLD OUT
MUCH LONGER.

606
00:23:52,498 --> 00:23:54,667
I'LL ASK YOU ONCE AGAIN.

607
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,837
WHERE IS MIGHTY
JACK'S BASE?

608
00:23:56,870 --> 00:23:59,538
IT'S NEXT TO THE DRUMS
AND THE GUITAR, HA-HA.

609
00:23:59,572 --> 00:24:02,108
I'VE NEVER HEARD OF
MIGHTY JACK.

610
00:24:02,142 --> 00:24:04,277
[MAN]
WHAT A STUBBORN MAN YOU ARE.

611
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:06,212
I HOPE YOUR EYES
ARE STILL CLOSED.

612
00:24:06,245 --> 00:24:09,115
NOW FOR THE LAST TIME,
WHERE IS MIGHTY JACK'S BASE?

613
00:24:09,148 --> 00:24:11,450
IT'S NOT EASY BEING GREEN.

614
00:24:11,483 --> 00:24:13,018
I'LL TELL YOU
WHAT YOU WANT TO KNOW.

615
00:24:13,052 --> 00:24:15,655
JUST TURN OFF THE LIGHTS,
PLEASE.

616
00:24:15,688 --> 00:24:18,692
[GATES CLOSING]

617
00:24:24,563 --> 00:24:26,700
OKAY, UH, EVERYBODY,
YOU KNOW WHAT TO DO?

618
00:24:26,733 --> 00:24:28,133
- SERVO?
- ROGER.

619
00:24:28,167 --> 00:24:29,535
- UH, GYPSY
- RICHARD.

620
00:24:29,568 --> 00:24:30,870
UH, YEAH, WHATEVER.

621
00:24:30,903 --> 00:24:32,705
OKAY, PLACES EVERYBODY,
HE'S COMING.

622
00:24:32,738 --> 00:24:34,807
HEY, HI, YOU GUYS,
WHAT YOU UP TO?

623
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,475
WELL, YOU KNOW, WE'VE BEEN
TALKING ABOUT HOW HUMANS

624
00:24:36,508 --> 00:24:37,743
HAVE A NEED FOR PETS.

625
00:24:37,777 --> 00:24:39,612
LIKE IN THIS FILM,
THE EVIL GUY HAS A PET CAT.

626
00:24:39,645 --> 00:24:41,948
YEAH, AND HUMANS HAVE A LOT OF
PROGRAMMING AND COMMERCIALS

627
00:24:41,982 --> 00:24:44,283
DIRECTED SPECIFICALLY
AT PETS SO...

628
00:24:44,317 --> 00:24:46,887
SO WE'VE COME UP WITH A LITTLE
AD CAMPAIGN BASED ON THIS MOVIE.

629
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,522
YEAH, AND WE'D LIKE YOU
TO BE OUR TEST MARKET.

630
00:24:48,555 --> 00:24:49,855
WE'D LIKE YOUR FEEDBACK,
YOU BEING HUMAN AND ALL.

631
00:24:49,888 --> 00:24:51,423
- PRETTY MUCH, RIGHT?
- [GYPSY] COME ON, YOU GUYS,

632
00:24:51,457 --> 00:24:52,692
[GYPSY]
I GOT STUFF TO DO.

633
00:24:52,725 --> 00:24:54,827
OKAY, WELL, I'D LOVE TO SEE
WHAT YOU GUYS GOT GOING,

634
00:24:54,860 --> 00:24:56,328
- WHAT YOU GOT COOKING.
- OKAY, GIVE ME A SECOND.

635
00:24:56,362 --> 00:24:57,463
OKAY, HERE WE GO.

636
00:24:57,497 --> 00:24:58,865
UH, CAMBOT,
HIT THAT MUSIC.

637
00:24:58,898 --> 00:25:00,300
♪♪

638
00:25:00,333 --> 00:25:02,935
NEW FROM THE MAKERS OF
MIGHTY DOG AND HUNGRY JACK

639
00:25:02,968 --> 00:25:05,172
COMES A TASTE COMBINATION
THAT CAN'T BE BEAT.

640
00:25:05,205 --> 00:25:07,340
INTRODUCING MIGHTY JACK!

641
00:25:07,373 --> 00:25:09,508
HI, I'M MIGHTY JACK.

642
00:25:09,542 --> 00:25:11,712
I MAKE MY
OWN GRAVY, HA!

643
00:25:11,745 --> 00:25:14,547
JOEL, GIVE ME A HAND,
POUR THAT WATER ON ME.

644
00:25:14,580 --> 00:25:17,417
THERE YOU GO, WHEE,
HOO-HOO-HOO-HOO, AH-HA.

645
00:25:17,450 --> 00:25:20,387
MIGHTY JACK DOG FOOD IS HIGH IN
PROTEIN, LOW IN SODIUM,

646
00:25:20,420 --> 00:25:22,988
PURE BEEF, PARTIALLY
HYDROGENATED, GREAT TASTING FEED

647
00:25:23,022 --> 00:25:25,125
MADE WITH A MATURE MEMBER
OF YOUR FAMILY AND MINE.

648
00:25:25,158 --> 00:25:27,260
THAT'S SOME
MATURE DOG, I MEAN...

649
00:25:27,293 --> 00:25:28,562
AHH!

650
00:25:28,595 --> 00:25:29,963
MIGHTY JACK HAS
THE TASTE DOGS LOVE

651
00:25:29,997 --> 00:25:32,165
AND IS COMPLETELY FREE OF
PERFUMES OR STABILIZERS.

652
00:25:32,198 --> 00:25:34,867
STRONG ENOUGH FOR A MANX
BUT MADE FOR A ROTTWEILER.

653
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:37,237
STORE IN A COOL, DRY PLACE AND
DO NOT EXPOSE TO LIVING TISSUE

654
00:25:37,270 --> 00:25:39,138
OR TEMPERATURES
OVER 72 DEGREES FAHRENHEIT.

655
00:25:39,172 --> 00:25:40,873
NOW AVAILABLE IN THREE
DELICIOUS FLAVORS,

656
00:25:40,907 --> 00:25:43,142
REGULAR, MAILMAN AND CAT.

657
00:25:43,175 --> 00:25:45,278
I'M SO HUNGRY
I COULD EAT A HORSE.

658
00:25:45,312 --> 00:25:47,480
I HAVE JUST ONE MESSAGE
FOR ALL DOGS.

659
00:25:47,513 --> 00:25:49,148
- BITE ME.
- HEY!

660
00:25:49,182 --> 00:25:52,685
AHH, I'M BEING EATEN
BY A DOG, HELP ME OUT!

661
00:25:52,718 --> 00:25:54,553
REMEMBER,
MIGHTY JACK DOG FOOD

662
00:25:54,587 --> 00:25:55,955
AND THE MIGHTY JACK
CORPORATE SYMBOL

663
00:25:55,988 --> 00:25:57,623
ARE IN NO WAY REPRESENTATIONAL
OR MEANT TO INFER

664
00:25:57,657 --> 00:25:59,425
RELATIONSHIP TO
ANY SIMILARITY OF ANY OTHER

665
00:25:59,458 --> 00:26:01,393
CORPORATE SYMBOLS, LOGOS OR
TRADEMARKS, DOG FOODS,

666
00:26:01,427 --> 00:26:03,095
DOG TREATS, DOG SNACKS
OR PERSONS LIVING OR DEAD.

667
00:26:03,128 --> 00:26:04,630
- THE END, WHAT DO YOU THINK?
- WHAT DO YOU THINK?

668
00:26:04,663 --> 00:26:08,668
UH, I THINK WE HAVE VERY
DIFFERENT VIEWS OF ADVERTISING.

669
00:26:08,702 --> 00:26:10,570
LET'S SEE HOW
THE PROS DO IT.

670
00:26:10,603 --> 00:26:12,872
♪♪

671
00:26:19,278 --> 00:26:20,813
I WILL, MASTER.

672
00:26:20,847 --> 00:26:24,683
- I'LL TAKE CARE OF COLONEL...
- MY SWEET LIPSTICK.

673
00:26:24,717 --> 00:26:27,620
- AH, HEY.
- SECRET AGENT ESTÉE LAUDER.

674
00:26:27,653 --> 00:26:29,622
IN EASY SPIRIT PUMPS.

675
00:26:33,627 --> 00:26:35,928
- WELL...
- YOU'LL BE...

676
00:26:35,962 --> 00:26:37,363
AND YOU'LL BE HOT,
HOT, HOT

677
00:26:37,397 --> 00:26:41,267
WITH THE LATEST TALKING
LIPSTICK FASHIONS FROM PARIS.

678
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:44,103
BREATH OF FRESH AIR, HA!

679
00:26:44,137 --> 00:26:47,273
I'LL FIX HER REAL GOOD,
YOU CAN BET ON THAT.

680
00:26:47,307 --> 00:26:49,075
DON'T FORGET,
I'M COUNTING ON YOU

681
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:51,277
TO ACCOMPANY ME TO
THE MEETING TONIGHT.

682
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:53,012
WHAT ABOUT MY NEEDS?

683
00:26:53,045 --> 00:26:54,647
I'LL SEND THE CAR
FOR YOU.

684
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,215
- OKAY.
- COME IN.

685
00:26:56,248 --> 00:26:59,518
SHE'S A LOUSY TRAITOR,
SIR.

686
00:26:59,552 --> 00:27:03,590
HEY, IT'S
THE DOUBLEMINT GEISHAS.

687
00:27:03,623 --> 00:27:05,125
IF THAT'S ALL,

688
00:27:05,158 --> 00:27:07,327
I'LL GO HOME NOW AND PREPARE
FOR TONIGHT'S MEETING.

689
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,962
- AND FOR BEING A TRAITOR.
- BYE.

690
00:27:14,167 --> 00:27:16,368
HERE'S THE RECEIPT
FOR YOUR DEPENDS.

691
00:27:16,402 --> 00:27:20,005
HMM, LET'S SEE,
"BITE ME," WHAT'S THIS MEAN?

692
00:27:20,038 --> 00:27:22,108
♪♪

693
00:27:22,142 --> 00:27:23,677
HM?

694
00:27:23,710 --> 00:27:25,445
[SNIFFING]

695
00:27:25,478 --> 00:27:26,612
DO YOU...?

696
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:29,082
[SNIFFING]

697
00:27:29,115 --> 00:27:31,885
WAIT, THIS MIRROR MAKES
ME LOOK LIKE A MODIGLIANI.

698
00:27:31,918 --> 00:27:34,020
THIS IS REALLY
A WONDERFUL PAINTING.

699
00:27:34,053 --> 00:27:35,855
SHE HAS SUCH
MYSTERIOUS EYES.

700
00:27:35,888 --> 00:27:37,190
ACTUALLY, IT'S MY FATHER.

701
00:27:37,223 --> 00:27:38,692
OOH.

702
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:43,262
- THEY'RE CONTACTS.
- WOW.

703
00:27:44,897 --> 00:27:47,167
I'VE ALWAYS
ENJOYED MODERN ART.

704
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:49,302
NOT!

705
00:27:49,335 --> 00:27:51,037
I KNOW IT SOUNDS STRANGE...

706
00:27:51,070 --> 00:27:52,738
BUT I
THINK I'M A ZEBRA.

707
00:27:52,772 --> 00:27:54,073
WE DON'T KNOW VERY
MUCH OURSELVES.

708
00:27:54,107 --> 00:27:55,642
ALL THEY TOLD US
WAS THAT THE KIDNAPPED MAN

709
00:27:55,675 --> 00:27:57,377
WAS VERY IMPORTANT
TO MIGHTY JACK.

710
00:27:57,410 --> 00:27:58,712
ASH, PLEASE.

711
00:27:58,745 --> 00:27:59,912
THERE'S ONE THING
WE DO KNOW, THOUGH.

712
00:27:59,945 --> 00:28:01,180
ASH.

713
00:28:01,213 --> 00:28:03,248
THE KIDNAPPERS MUST BE
CLEVER AND RUTHLESS.

714
00:28:07,287 --> 00:28:09,388
WE CAN'T JUST SIT
HERE LIKE THIS.

715
00:28:09,422 --> 00:28:10,657
WE'RE GETTING HEMORRHOIDS.

716
00:28:10,690 --> 00:28:12,292
MARY, HAVE THEY
FOUND THE SITE YET?

717
00:28:12,325 --> 00:28:14,227
UNH-UNH, I'M WAITING FOR
THEIR NEXT MESSAGE, THOUGH.

718
00:28:14,260 --> 00:28:17,597
- NICE FLIP.
- OH, NO, TIME FOR BAND
PRACTICE.

719
00:28:23,837 --> 00:28:25,772
- ♪ WELL I USED TO GET-- ♪
- HI, ELVIS!

720
00:28:25,805 --> 00:28:27,173
I DON'T KNOW
HOW IMPORTANT HE IS

721
00:28:27,207 --> 00:28:28,808
BUT HE'S SURE GIVING US
A LOT OF TROUBLE.

722
00:28:28,842 --> 00:28:29,875
NO TROUBLE AT ALL.

723
00:28:29,908 --> 00:28:31,610
- THIS IS A JOY RIDE.
- HUH?

724
00:28:31,643 --> 00:28:33,913
WHEN HE FINDS OUT THAT MIGHTY
JACK'S ON THE WAY TO RESCUE HIM,

725
00:28:33,947 --> 00:28:35,615
HE'LL JUMP FOR JOY.

726
00:28:35,648 --> 00:28:37,617
[ALL LAUGHING]

727
00:28:37,650 --> 00:28:39,685
A SIGNAL.

728
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:42,455
[BEEPING]

729
00:28:42,488 --> 00:28:43,957
♪ WESTERN UNION ♪

730
00:28:43,990 --> 00:28:45,392
♪ DAH DAH-DAH DAH-DAH,
DAH DAH-DAH DAH-DAH ♪

731
00:28:45,425 --> 00:28:47,060
♪ DAH DAH-DAH DAH-DAH,
DAH DAH-DAH DAH-DAH ♪

732
00:28:47,093 --> 00:28:49,995
CALLING MIGHTY JACK,
CALLING MIGHTY JACK.

733
00:28:50,028 --> 00:28:52,532
COME IN, MIGHTY JACK,
RESPOND IMMEDIATELY.

734
00:28:52,565 --> 00:28:54,100
THIS IS MIGHTY JACK.

735
00:28:54,133 --> 00:28:56,435
WE HAVE A NUCLEAR MISSILE
AIMED DIRECTLY AT YOU.

736
00:28:56,468 --> 00:28:58,605
BUT WE HAVE NO
INTENTION OF ATTACKING YOU.

737
00:28:58,638 --> 00:29:01,573
WE ONLY DEMAND THAT YOU
TURN OVER MIGHTY JACK TO US,

738
00:29:01,607 --> 00:29:04,643
IN EXCHANGE FOR
MR. HAROLD ATARI'S LIFE.

739
00:29:04,677 --> 00:29:06,578
THE ANTI-MISSLES ARE LOADED,
SIR, READY TO FIRE.

740
00:29:06,612 --> 00:29:08,080
SHH, NOT HERE.

741
00:29:08,113 --> 00:29:11,217
WE HAVE ALREADY DELIVERED
THIS DEMAND TO COLONEL YABUKI.

742
00:29:11,250 --> 00:29:14,320
DO YOU READ ME,
MIGHTY JACK?

743
00:29:14,353 --> 00:29:16,522
HOW DO WE KNOW THAT
MR. ATARI IS STILL ALIVE?

744
00:29:16,555 --> 00:29:18,257
WAIT A MOMENT.

745
00:29:18,290 --> 00:29:20,893
- ARE YOU ALIVE?
- EXCHANGING HIM FOR
MIGHTY JACK.

746
00:29:20,927 --> 00:29:22,828
WHO IS
THIS ATARI ANYWAY?

747
00:29:22,862 --> 00:29:24,497
CAPTAIN TENDA?

748
00:29:24,530 --> 00:29:26,765
ALL WE KNOW IS THAT
IT'S SOMEONE VERY SPECIAL.

749
00:29:26,798 --> 00:29:29,902
HELLO, MIGHTY JACK,
IT'S ME, HAROLD ATARI.

750
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:33,038
MR. ATARI, MIGHTY JACK
WILL RESCUE YOU.

751
00:29:33,072 --> 00:29:34,640
YOU'D BETTER RESCUE ME.

752
00:29:34,673 --> 00:29:36,475
I DON'T FEEL LIKE
BEING LEFT OUT HERE TO ROT.

753
00:29:36,508 --> 00:29:38,143
WHY OF ALL THE--

754
00:29:38,177 --> 00:29:39,745
SAY, WHO DOES HE THINK
HE IS?

755
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:41,047
AND BE QUICK ABOUT IT.

756
00:29:41,080 --> 00:29:42,548
UNLESS YOU'RE
ALL FRIGHTENED PIGEONS.

757
00:29:42,582 --> 00:29:44,050
BOY, THAT'S THE LAST STRAW.

758
00:29:44,083 --> 00:29:45,452
PIGEON, YOURSELF.

759
00:29:45,485 --> 00:29:46,752
HEY, WATCH YOUR MOUTH.

760
00:29:46,785 --> 00:29:48,187
IF YOU DON'T THINK
YOU CAN HANDLE THE JOB,

761
00:29:48,220 --> 00:29:49,755
YOU MIGHT AS WELL TURN
AROUND AND GO HOME.

762
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:51,223
- OOH...
- LISTEN TO THAT.

763
00:29:51,257 --> 00:29:52,692
- WHAT A BURN.
- WELL, I'VE HAD ENOUGH.

764
00:29:52,725 --> 00:29:54,660
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO HOME.

765
00:29:54,693 --> 00:29:55,895
WHY SHOULD WE SAVE HIM?

766
00:29:55,928 --> 00:29:58,732
LOOK, HECKLING IS
PART OF THE BUSINESS.

767
00:29:58,765 --> 00:30:02,768
- I ADMIRE HIS COURAGE.
- YOU WOULD, KISS-UP.

768
00:30:02,802 --> 00:30:04,270
DO YOU READ ME, MIGHTY JACK?

769
00:30:04,303 --> 00:30:06,005
WELL, WHAT
HAVE YOU DECIDED?

770
00:30:06,038 --> 00:30:07,940
HMM?

771
00:30:07,973 --> 00:30:09,875
WE READ YOU ALL RIGHT?

772
00:30:09,908 --> 00:30:11,443
WE NEED A LITTLE TIME.

773
00:30:11,477 --> 00:30:14,847
VERY WELL, WE'LL TAKE
THIS UP WITH COLONEL YABUKI.

774
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:17,350
[ALL]
♪ YABUKI, YABUKI, YABUKI ♪

775
00:30:17,383 --> 00:30:19,785
IS EVERYTHING
READY FOR THE CONFERENCE?

776
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:22,522
- HELEN OF TROY.
- WHAT'S THE MATTER?

777
00:30:22,555 --> 00:30:23,757
I'M THROUGH MAKING
COFFEE!

778
00:30:23,790 --> 00:30:25,023
[GASPING]

779
00:30:25,057 --> 00:30:26,492
YOU'VE FINALLY
REVEALED YOUR TRUE COLORS.

780
00:30:26,525 --> 00:30:28,795
YOU'RE THE ONE WHO
BETRAYED US.

781
00:30:28,828 --> 00:30:30,430
I'M DISAPPOINTED IN YOU.

782
00:30:30,463 --> 00:30:33,065
ACCEPT THE PROPOSAL
THEY'VE OFFERED YOU.

783
00:30:33,098 --> 00:30:36,202
ATARI'S LIFE IN EXCHANGE
FOR MIGHTY JACK.

784
00:30:36,235 --> 00:30:37,903
IT'S PURE BEEF.

785
00:30:37,937 --> 00:30:40,473
UNLESS, COLONEL,
YOU WOULD RATHER EXCHANGE

786
00:30:40,507 --> 00:30:41,807
YOUR LIFE FOR MIGHTY JACK.

787
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:43,910
[LAUGHING]

788
00:30:43,943 --> 00:30:45,812
OH, GRAMPS, GET SOME
PEARL DROPS.

789
00:30:45,845 --> 00:30:47,313
[GASPING]

790
00:30:47,347 --> 00:30:49,048
HUH?
OH.

791
00:30:49,082 --> 00:30:52,985
ALL RIGHT, DROP THE GUN.

792
00:30:53,018 --> 00:30:56,990
I'LL JUST PLACE IT VERY
CAREFULLY ON THE COUNTER AND--

793
00:30:57,023 --> 00:30:58,992
[SHOUTING]

794
00:30:59,025 --> 00:31:00,527
[LAUGHING]

795
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:04,097
SHE WON'T GET VERY FAR
IN THOSE CHEAP PUMPS.

796
00:31:04,130 --> 00:31:08,033
FEEL LIKE
A SNEAKER, THOUGH.

797
00:31:08,067 --> 00:31:10,235
- SAM SPADE'S OFFICE.
- HMM?

798
00:31:10,268 --> 00:31:13,172
SPACIOUS.

799
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:16,575
- MCGARRETT, GET HER!
- MANNIX, STOP HER!

800
00:31:16,608 --> 00:31:18,745
HOOKER'S A GOOD COP.

801
00:31:18,778 --> 00:31:20,447
I GOTTA SAY IT.

802
00:31:23,950 --> 00:31:26,552
OOH.

803
00:31:26,585 --> 00:31:31,257
SORRY I BLEW UP
LIKE THAT.

804
00:31:31,290 --> 00:31:34,427
- HM, SO?
- SHE'S DEAD, SIR.

805
00:31:34,460 --> 00:31:38,230
I BELIEVE SHE HAD SWALLOWED
SOME SORT OF LETHAL CAPSULE.

806
00:31:38,263 --> 00:31:39,732
AND THEN IT--

807
00:31:39,765 --> 00:31:41,400
WRIGGLED AND WIGGLED
AND TRIGGERED INSIDE HER.

808
00:31:41,433 --> 00:31:42,968
IT EXPLODED INSIDE HER.

809
00:31:43,002 --> 00:31:45,270
AS IF IT HAD BEEN TRIGGERED
OFF BY REMOTE CONTROL.

810
00:31:45,303 --> 00:31:48,440
[TOM AND CROW]
THE CRAPPY GAME SHOW?

811
00:31:48,473 --> 00:31:50,175
OKAY, KIDS,
COME ON, IT'S IN OR OUT.

812
00:31:50,208 --> 00:31:52,612
CLOSE THE SCREEN DOOR,
COME ON.

813
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:58,517
OOH, WHOA, IT LOOKS
LIKE IT'S GETTING KIND OF
LOW ON BAKING SODA.

814
00:31:58,550 --> 00:32:01,087
YEAH, THAT HAPPENS.

815
00:32:01,120 --> 00:32:04,090
COME BACK AS SOON AS
YOU'VE SCOUTED THE ISLAND.

816
00:32:04,123 --> 00:32:05,958
GOTTA GET THIS SUIT BACK
TO IVAN TORS.

817
00:32:05,992 --> 00:32:07,293
- ROGER.
- WHITTAKER.

818
00:32:07,327 --> 00:32:09,628
[CHUCKLES]

819
00:32:09,662 --> 00:32:13,232
[JAZZ PLAYING]

820
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:17,837
WOW, IT'S THE ISLAND
OF MILES DAVIS, COOL.

821
00:32:17,870 --> 00:32:20,640
YOU KNOW, I BET HE HAS A
PERFECTLY DRY TUXEDO UNDER THAT.

822
00:32:20,673 --> 00:32:23,508
OR A PERFECTLY DRY MARTINI.

823
00:32:23,542 --> 00:32:25,878
GLENN CORBETT,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

824
00:32:25,912 --> 00:32:27,547
HUH?

825
00:32:27,580 --> 00:32:31,750
♪♪

826
00:32:31,783 --> 00:32:33,753
OH, IT'S
AARON SPELLING'S HOUSE.

827
00:32:33,787 --> 00:32:35,320
OH.

828
00:32:35,353 --> 00:32:37,690
IKIBA.

829
00:32:37,723 --> 00:32:40,693
[GRUNTING]

830
00:32:40,727 --> 00:32:44,630
YOU KNOW, I'VE ALWAYS
WANTED TO SEE THE INSIDE
OF BEBE REBOZO'S HOUSE.

831
00:32:44,663 --> 00:32:49,235
[TOM IMITATING NIXON]
DICK.

832
00:32:49,268 --> 00:32:53,072
POWDER BLUE,
SPIES ASK FOR IT BY NAME.

833
00:32:53,105 --> 00:32:55,842
[WHISPERING]
COOL, DADDY.

834
00:32:55,875 --> 00:33:01,147
♪♪

835
00:33:01,180 --> 00:33:03,582
SOMETHING TELLS ME
THAT WYNTON MARSALIS

836
00:33:03,615 --> 00:33:05,585
IS AROUND
THE NEXT CORNER.

837
00:33:08,420 --> 00:33:11,990
OH, AKIO, AKIO,
WHEREFORE ART THOU, AKIO.

838
00:33:12,023 --> 00:33:17,597
♪♪

839
00:33:17,630 --> 00:33:19,998
WHOA, BIG DOG,
ROTTWEILER, OOH.

840
00:33:20,032 --> 00:33:22,168
OOH, LOOK OUT.

841
00:33:22,202 --> 00:33:23,803
[GASPS]

842
00:33:23,837 --> 00:33:24,937
THAT'S TEO MACERO.

843
00:33:25,938 --> 00:33:28,240
♪♪

844
00:33:31,677 --> 00:33:33,212
CALLING MIGHTY JACK,
IT'S JERRY.

845
00:33:33,245 --> 00:33:36,382
MIGHTY JACK,
I SEE YOU FINALLY MADE IT.

846
00:33:36,415 --> 00:33:37,583
HEY.

847
00:33:37,617 --> 00:33:38,952
WHERE'S THE INSTALLATION?

848
00:33:38,985 --> 00:33:40,787
ON THE SOUTH SIDE
OF THE ISLAND.

849
00:33:40,820 --> 00:33:41,953
HOW'S ATARI?

850
00:33:41,987 --> 00:33:43,322
KIND OF A JERK
BUT HE GROWS ON YOU.

851
00:33:43,355 --> 00:33:44,923
[CHUCKLING]

852
00:33:44,957 --> 00:33:48,895
AND SO THE MALE ZYGOTE SWIMS
OUT TO MEET THE EGG AND--

853
00:33:48,928 --> 00:33:52,332
♪ HEY AQUALUNG ♪

854
00:33:52,365 --> 00:33:55,067
"NAVY SEALS"
STARRING CHARLIE SHEEN.

855
00:33:55,100 --> 00:33:57,603
UH...

856
00:33:57,637 --> 00:33:59,638
HELLO, MIGHTY JACK.

857
00:33:59,672 --> 00:34:01,107
I'M ON
THE ISLAND NOW.

858
00:34:01,140 --> 00:34:02,575
I'M GONNA TRY
TO RECUE THEM.

859
00:34:02,608 --> 00:34:05,143
YES, SIR.

860
00:34:05,177 --> 00:34:09,515
UH, I'LL JUST COVER
MY SCAT HERE.

861
00:34:09,548 --> 00:34:11,117
NOW LET'S SEE
WHAT WE HAVE HERE.

862
00:34:11,150 --> 00:34:12,818
UH, CHICKEN LEG.

863
00:34:12,852 --> 00:34:15,253
OH, KRAFT SINGLES AND A NOTE
FROM MY MOTHER:

864
00:34:15,287 --> 00:34:17,022
"I'M SO PROUD OF YOU."

865
00:34:20,358 --> 00:34:22,528
WHAT IS THAT,
A POOL CUE OR A SILENCER?

866
00:34:22,562 --> 00:34:25,465
JUST PUT THAT PART ON,
THAT MAKES IT LOUD AGAIN.

867
00:34:25,498 --> 00:34:28,835
OH, AND THAT ATTACHMENT FOR
THE HARD-TO-REACH ASSIGNATIONS.

868
00:34:28,868 --> 00:34:30,737
[CHUCKLES]

869
00:34:30,770 --> 00:34:32,572
HOW MANY
SILENCERS DOES HE NEED?

870
00:34:32,605 --> 00:34:33,940
I DON'T KNOW.

871
00:34:36,408 --> 00:34:38,243
BOY, YOU KNOW,
THESE FERN PRISONS

872
00:34:38,277 --> 00:34:39,845
WERE REALLY POPULAR
IN THE '70s, WEREN'T THEY?

873
00:34:39,878 --> 00:34:41,013
NATCH.

874
00:34:41,047 --> 00:34:42,182
PUMA?

875
00:34:44,283 --> 00:34:47,320
- TODD?
- WATCH OUT FOR THAT PALM LEAF!

876
00:34:47,353 --> 00:34:51,557
♪ DUM, DUM, DUM, DUM,
DUM-DUM, DUM ♪

877
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:53,492
I WILL SUCCEED
WHERE HE FAILED.

878
00:34:53,525 --> 00:34:55,193
JERRY, WHERE ARE YOU?

879
00:34:55,227 --> 00:34:57,730
OH, HELLO, MR. RESCUE PERSON,
I'M IN THE...

880
00:34:57,763 --> 00:35:00,365
IT'S THE DOOR
ON THE RIGHT.

881
00:35:00,398 --> 00:35:01,700
OKAY.

882
00:35:01,733 --> 00:35:04,103
IT'S BY
THE ICE MACHINE.

883
00:35:06,472 --> 00:35:10,042
I HAVE A FEELING THAT
KOOKY CHAOS IS ABOUT TO ENSUE.

884
00:35:10,075 --> 00:35:12,312
IT'S THE M.C. ESCHER HOUSE.

885
00:35:12,345 --> 00:35:13,612
ESCHER HOUSE.

886
00:35:13,645 --> 00:35:15,648
[SINGING]

887
00:35:15,682 --> 00:35:16,848
OH.

888
00:35:21,020 --> 00:35:22,788
ROOM SERVICE.

889
00:35:22,822 --> 00:35:25,257
IS THAT YOU CAPTAIN,
THE DOOR'S LOCKED.

890
00:35:28,727 --> 00:35:30,797
OH, THANKS
FOR KNOCKING, DEAN.

891
00:35:30,830 --> 00:35:33,465
THEY'RE TRYING TO KILL US
WITH POISON GAS.

892
00:35:33,498 --> 00:35:34,867
WHO, EXXON?

893
00:35:34,900 --> 00:35:36,135
OH, BOY.

894
00:35:36,168 --> 00:35:37,135
OH, THAT'LL HELP A LOT.

895
00:35:37,168 --> 00:35:38,137
HOLD STILL.

896
00:35:38,170 --> 00:35:39,305
IT'S BETTER
IF YOU DON'T MOVE.

897
00:35:39,338 --> 00:35:40,405
WE'VE GOT TO GET
OUT OF HERE.

898
00:35:40,438 --> 00:35:42,242
I SAVED MY HANDKERCHIEF.

899
00:35:42,275 --> 00:35:44,510
[COUGHING]

900
00:35:44,543 --> 00:35:47,480
IT'S HERE
IN MY ESPADRILLES.

901
00:35:52,285 --> 00:35:54,453
IT'S A SNAP.

902
00:35:54,487 --> 00:35:56,588
COME ON.

903
00:35:56,622 --> 00:35:59,325
[PANTING]

904
00:36:01,693 --> 00:36:03,862
WAIT.

905
00:36:03,895 --> 00:36:05,632
BEFORE WE GO.

906
00:36:05,665 --> 00:36:07,132
WE HAVE TO
BLOW THE PLACE UP.

907
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:10,302
OH, THAT'S CRAZ-- WHY DIDN'T
YOU TELL US THAT BEFORE?

908
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:15,808
- OKAY, LET'S DO IT.
- LET'S FALL IN LOVE.

909
00:36:15,842 --> 00:36:17,977
JERRY, RETURN TO MIGHTY JACK.

910
00:36:18,010 --> 00:36:20,445
- WHAT ABOUT YOU?
- I'VE GOT THE BUGGY HERE.

911
00:36:20,478 --> 00:36:22,113
- BUT, CAPTAIN.
- THAT'S AN ORDER.

912
00:36:22,147 --> 00:36:24,083
YES, SIR.

913
00:36:24,117 --> 00:36:27,118
HE NEVER LETS
ME DRIVE THE BUGGY.

914
00:36:27,152 --> 00:36:30,122
DON'T MOVE!

915
00:36:30,155 --> 00:36:32,223
YOU MOVED... OOH.

916
00:36:32,257 --> 00:36:33,558
HEY, GIVE ME A TURN
AT THAT.

917
00:36:33,592 --> 00:36:35,728
OOH, IT'S FUN.

918
00:36:35,762 --> 00:36:38,263
- ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO.
- RIGHT.

919
00:36:38,297 --> 00:36:42,033
[EXPLODING]
YEAH.

920
00:36:42,067 --> 00:36:43,868
UNREAL.

921
00:36:45,972 --> 00:36:47,273
OOH.

922
00:36:47,307 --> 00:36:48,273
OOH.

923
00:36:48,307 --> 00:36:49,775
PRETTY.

924
00:36:49,808 --> 00:36:51,243
THEY SOUND LIKE HORSES,
DON'T THEY?

925
00:36:51,277 --> 00:36:52,545
WHAT?

926
00:36:52,578 --> 00:36:56,048
WHAT, WE GOT A VOLKSWAGEN?

927
00:36:56,082 --> 00:36:59,385
WHAT-- OH, GREAT,
GOOD THING THERE HAPPENED
TO BE A CHOPPER AROUND.

928
00:36:59,418 --> 00:37:01,687
[CHUCKLING]

929
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:04,257
TRAFFIC OVER THE
PACIFIC OCEAN IS LIGHT TODAY.

930
00:37:04,290 --> 00:37:06,592
EXPECT NO DELAYS BETWEEN
MINDANAO AND HAWAII.

931
00:37:06,625 --> 00:37:09,662
LOOKS LIKE THE TY-D-BOL
MAN TRADED UP HERE.

932
00:37:09,695 --> 00:37:11,863
THE WATER'S BLUE.

933
00:37:11,897 --> 00:37:12,898
YEAH.

934
00:37:17,002 --> 00:37:19,372
WE'RE INFORMAL HERE AT
MIGHTY JACK, STEVE.

935
00:37:19,405 --> 00:37:21,207
SHIRTSLEEVES.

936
00:37:26,312 --> 00:37:27,813
WOW.

937
00:37:30,048 --> 00:37:31,850
WELL, THEN,
DOWN THE HATCH.

938
00:37:31,883 --> 00:37:34,387
ORRIN HATCH, YOU SEE THAT'S
A LITTLE JOKE

939
00:37:34,420 --> 00:37:36,755
FOR OUR FRIENDS
IN UTAH, SENATOR.

940
00:37:36,788 --> 00:37:38,992
FINE, DISTINGUISHED
COLLEAGUE FROM...

941
00:37:42,528 --> 00:37:43,997
ALL RIGHT, ENGINES ON.

942
00:37:44,030 --> 00:37:46,298
- YES, SIR.
- COMBAT STATIONS.

943
00:37:46,332 --> 00:37:48,433
BOY, JUST THINK IF THIS
MOVIE HAD A PLOT.

944
00:37:48,467 --> 00:37:49,635
IT MIGHT REALLY BE NEAT.

945
00:37:49,668 --> 00:37:50,870
YEAH.

946
00:37:54,707 --> 00:37:57,443
HUH?

947
00:37:57,477 --> 00:37:59,278
NEAT DECALS.

948
00:37:59,312 --> 00:38:03,048
- YEAH, NICE.
- EXCELLENT DETAILING.

949
00:38:03,082 --> 00:38:04,817
WAIT A MINUTE.

950
00:38:06,718 --> 00:38:09,688
SHERWOOD SCHWARTZ PRESENTS
GILLIGAN'S ISLAND 2000,

951
00:38:09,722 --> 00:38:11,223
WITH GILLIGAN,

952
00:38:11,257 --> 00:38:12,892
♪ THE ADMIRAL TOO ♪

953
00:38:12,925 --> 00:38:15,360
♪ THE BILLIONAIRE ♪

954
00:38:15,393 --> 00:38:17,897
WEENIE LAUNCH, WEENIE LAUNCH.

955
00:38:21,567 --> 00:38:23,068
WOW.

956
00:38:25,537 --> 00:38:28,540
NO!

957
00:38:28,573 --> 00:38:30,408
OH, NO, THEY HIT
THE HOWELL'S HUT.

958
00:38:30,442 --> 00:38:32,845
LOVEY, I'M ON FIRE.

959
00:38:32,878 --> 00:38:34,180
FLASH.

960
00:38:34,213 --> 00:38:36,048
[ALL]
OHH...FLASH.

961
00:38:36,082 --> 00:38:38,517
IT GETS
TIRING AFTER A WHILE.

962
00:38:41,187 --> 00:38:44,690
HOO, "APOCALYPSE NOW,"
AH-HA, APOCALYPSE NOT.

963
00:38:46,925 --> 00:38:49,295
DECEMBER 7, 2041,

964
00:38:49,328 --> 00:38:52,432
A FILM
THAT WILL LIVE IN INFAMY.

965
00:38:52,465 --> 00:38:53,865
OH, LOOK, THE MOSQUITO.

966
00:38:53,898 --> 00:38:57,235
THE MINNESOTA STATE BIRD--
FOR OUR FRIENDS IN MINNESOTA.

967
00:38:57,268 --> 00:39:00,338
WEENIE LAUNCH.

968
00:39:00,372 --> 00:39:01,873
TEST.

969
00:39:01,907 --> 00:39:04,410
OOH, OOH!

970
00:39:04,443 --> 00:39:05,978
[ALL]
AAHH...

971
00:39:06,012 --> 00:39:07,980
[CLAPPING]
OH, BEAUTIFUL.

972
00:39:08,013 --> 00:39:09,148
IT'S MEMPHIS BELLE.

973
00:39:09,182 --> 00:39:13,785
OOH, OOH, OOH, OH, OH,
WOW, OH.

974
00:39:13,818 --> 00:39:15,687
BEAUTIFUL.

975
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:19,925
THEY'RE USING EVERY TOY
IN THE BOX.

976
00:39:19,958 --> 00:39:21,160
HERE COMES
THE GRAND FINALE.

977
00:39:21,193 --> 00:39:22,528
MORE THRUST.

978
00:39:22,562 --> 00:39:25,397
REALLY?

979
00:39:25,430 --> 00:39:28,200
GAMERA!-- UH--
OH, SORRY.

980
00:39:28,233 --> 00:39:31,837
FROM THE FUN AND SUN CAPITAL OF
THE WORLD, MIAMI BEACH, COMES...

981
00:39:31,870 --> 00:39:33,338
OH.

982
00:39:35,073 --> 00:39:36,475
YOU KNOW,
THE TOMMY BARTLETT SHOW

983
00:39:36,508 --> 00:39:37,977
IS REALLY GETTING EXPENSIVE.

984
00:39:38,010 --> 00:39:41,147
NOW WE SEE HERE WHERE
THE PATRIOT MISSILES

985
00:39:41,180 --> 00:39:43,082
INTERCEPT THE SCUDS.

986
00:39:46,052 --> 00:39:48,253
AND...

987
00:39:48,287 --> 00:39:51,523
GOD BLESS
THE PATRIOT MISSILES.

988
00:39:51,557 --> 00:39:55,027
AND WE'D LIKE TO WELCOME YOU
TO COLLATERAL DAMAGE PLAYHOUSE.

989
00:39:57,930 --> 00:40:00,198
WOW.

990
00:40:00,232 --> 00:40:02,902
WHOO.

991
00:40:02,935 --> 00:40:05,003
- DID YOU DO THAT?
- LET'S GO AFTER THEM?

992
00:40:05,037 --> 00:40:07,072
IT'S NO USE.

993
00:40:07,105 --> 00:40:08,807
THEIR SPEED IS
MUCH FASTER THAN OURS.

994
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:11,510
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT--
FASTER THAN MIGHTY JACK?

995
00:40:11,543 --> 00:40:12,612
NEVER UNDERRATE
YOUR ENEMY.

996
00:40:12,645 --> 00:40:14,413
UH, I THINK
THAT'S HOW IT GOES.

997
00:40:14,447 --> 00:40:17,015
ANYWAY, WE SAVED MR. ATARI
AND THAT'S ALL THAT MATTERS.

998
00:40:17,048 --> 00:40:18,683
[MAN]
CAPTAIN.

999
00:40:18,717 --> 00:40:21,787
I THINK WE OUGHT TO DESTROY
THE ISLAND COMPLETELY.

1000
00:40:21,820 --> 00:40:23,955
OKAY, MR. MANIFEST DESTINY.

1001
00:40:23,988 --> 00:40:26,192
TOMMY, LET'S GO
BACK TO THE ISLAND.

1002
00:40:26,225 --> 00:40:27,960
YES, SIR.

1003
00:40:27,993 --> 00:40:30,062
BANK TURN.

1004
00:40:36,935 --> 00:40:39,738
ACCIDENTS WILL-- HUH?

1005
00:40:39,772 --> 00:40:41,740
I DON'T LIKE THAT GUY--
WHO DOES HE THINK HE IS?

1006
00:40:41,773 --> 00:40:44,243
CAREFUL, HE MIGHT HEAR YOU,
HE'S A V.I.P.

1007
00:40:44,277 --> 00:40:45,810
YEAH, YOU DON'T SAY.

1008
00:40:45,843 --> 00:40:48,247
WE RISK OUR NECKS TO SAVE HIS
LIFE AND NOW HE'S GIVING ORDERS.

1009
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:49,582
HEY, NICE HAT.

1010
00:40:49,615 --> 00:40:51,350
WE'LL BE OVER
THE TARGET VERY SOON.

1011
00:40:51,383 --> 00:40:53,985
SAY, CAPTAIN, SHOULD WE
DROP A FEW BOMBS?

1012
00:40:54,018 --> 00:40:55,653
IT'LL KEEP HIM
QUIET FOR A WHILE.

1013
00:40:55,687 --> 00:40:57,188
GOOD IDEA.

1014
00:40:57,222 --> 00:40:59,458
THAT'S WHAT
KISSINGER WOULD DO.

1015
00:41:05,130 --> 00:41:07,633
HEY, THAT'S A BABY
FORMULA FACTORY.

1016
00:41:07,667 --> 00:41:09,735
NOW YOU'VE DONE IT.

1017
00:41:09,768 --> 00:41:13,572
AH, TET, MY
FAVORITE HOLIDAY, YOU KNOW?

1018
00:41:13,605 --> 00:41:16,108
THERE GOES THE KEN AND
BARBIE DREAM HOME.

1019
00:41:16,142 --> 00:41:17,743
OOH.

1020
00:41:23,582 --> 00:41:25,683
OH, NO, NOT THE
A.M. RADIO TOWERS.

1021
00:41:25,717 --> 00:41:28,187
CLARK AND HANSON IN
THE MORNING...

1022
00:41:28,220 --> 00:41:30,588
GOD, I LOVE
THE SMELL OF BURNING FLESH

1023
00:41:30,622 --> 00:41:31,890
AND THE SOUND OF
BREAKING GLASS.

1024
00:41:31,923 --> 00:41:33,358
OOH.

1025
00:41:35,527 --> 00:41:36,495
WELL, THEN.

1026
00:41:36,528 --> 00:41:38,897
MISSION ACCOMPLISHED.

1027
00:41:38,930 --> 00:41:40,632
NOW LET'S GO HOME.

1028
00:41:40,665 --> 00:41:42,902
THE WIMBLEDON
JUDGES AGREE.

1029
00:41:42,935 --> 00:41:46,038
[CHUCKLING]

1030
00:41:46,072 --> 00:41:48,707
- DICKWEED.
- OOH.

1031
00:41:48,740 --> 00:41:50,875
TAG.

1032
00:41:50,908 --> 00:41:52,510
YEAH, YEAH.

1033
00:41:52,543 --> 00:41:54,045
OH, BOY, HERE
COMES ANOTHER...

1034
00:41:54,078 --> 00:41:55,213
[TOGETHER]
BANK TURN.

1035
00:41:55,247 --> 00:41:57,248
HOW MANY MORE YOU
GOTTA LOOK AT?

1036
00:41:57,282 --> 00:41:59,418
[MAN]
YOU HAVE NOT
DESTROYED US, MIGHTY JACK.

1037
00:41:59,452 --> 00:42:01,620
WE WILL RETALIATE
FOR THIS.

1038
00:42:01,653 --> 00:42:04,088
OUR ORGANIZATION
IS POWERFUL.

1039
00:42:04,122 --> 00:42:07,492
Q WILL RETURN AND
ANNIHILATE YOU FOREVER!

1040
00:42:07,525 --> 00:42:10,528
BUT FIRST THESE MESSAGES
FROM CREST.

1041
00:42:10,562 --> 00:42:13,732
YEAH, YEAH, WE ALL LIVE IN A
YELLOW SUBMARINE, WE KNOW, YEAH.

1042
00:42:13,765 --> 00:42:16,402
SUPERSLOW...

1043
00:42:16,435 --> 00:42:17,937
MOVING CAR.

1044
00:42:17,970 --> 00:42:19,237
SUPER SLOW.

1045
00:42:19,270 --> 00:42:20,538
DA-DUM.

1046
00:42:25,343 --> 00:42:28,313
MEANWHILE, AT THE MOVIE'S
BIGGEST PHALLIC SYMBOL...

1047
00:42:28,347 --> 00:42:31,783
HEY, PULL MY FINGER.

1048
00:42:31,817 --> 00:42:34,687
OH, JEANNIE'S REALLY DONE IT
THIS TIME, MAJOR HEALEY.

1049
00:42:39,458 --> 00:42:41,193
I'M GOING OUT,
ANYBODY NEED ANYTHING?

1050
00:42:41,227 --> 00:42:43,395
WE FINALLY MADE IT BACK
TO BASE.

1051
00:42:43,428 --> 00:42:45,730
AND WE'RE NOT
ALLOWED TO GET OFF.

1052
00:42:45,763 --> 00:42:47,767
THOSE WERE THE ORDERS
FROM HEADQUARTERS.

1053
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:49,067
POOR GUY.

1054
00:42:49,100 --> 00:42:51,003
[SINGING]

1055
00:42:51,037 --> 00:42:53,305
OH-HO, THE CHICKS ARE HERE.

1056
00:42:53,338 --> 00:42:54,773
WHOO!

1057
00:42:54,807 --> 00:42:57,575
WELCOME BACK, JERRY, THE MISSION
WAS SUCCESSFUL, WASN'T IT?

1058
00:42:57,608 --> 00:42:59,378
YEAH, BUT
I DIDN'T ENJOY IT.

1059
00:42:59,412 --> 00:43:01,280
OH, AND THAT'S ALL
THAT MATTERS.

1060
00:43:01,313 --> 00:43:02,547
WHY NOT?

1061
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:04,350
WELL, YOU SEE,
UH, THERE WAS THIS GUY.

1062
00:43:04,383 --> 00:43:05,917
I JUST COULDN'T
STAND HIM.

1063
00:43:05,950 --> 00:43:07,653
OOH.

1064
00:43:07,687 --> 00:43:09,053
DOH!

1065
00:43:09,087 --> 00:43:11,357
ASK NOT WHAT YOUR COUNTRY
CAN DO FOR YOU.

1066
00:43:11,390 --> 00:43:12,758
[GASPING]

1067
00:43:12,792 --> 00:43:15,860
ALLOW ME TO INTRODUCE...

1068
00:43:15,893 --> 00:43:17,930
MAJOR HAROLD ATARI.

1069
00:43:17,963 --> 00:43:21,733
[TOGETHER]
♪ WHA, WHA, WHA, WHA ♪

1070
00:43:21,767 --> 00:43:24,102
OPEN MOUTH,
INSERT FOOT.

1071
00:43:24,135 --> 00:43:27,305
HEH-HEH-HEH.

1072
00:43:27,338 --> 00:43:28,573
HAIKIBA.

1073
00:43:28,607 --> 00:43:31,177
WELCOME ABOARD...
COMMANDER.

1074
00:43:31,210 --> 00:43:33,078
THE CAPTAIN IS
YOUR EXECUTIVE OFFICER.

1075
00:43:33,112 --> 00:43:35,113
HE'LL BE KISSING UP TO
YOU RIGHT AWAY.

1076
00:43:35,147 --> 00:43:36,282
CAPTAIN?

1077
00:43:36,315 --> 00:43:38,117
IT'S AN HONOR, SIR.

1078
00:43:38,150 --> 00:43:39,852
YOU GOT A CUTE SMILE.

1079
00:43:39,885 --> 00:43:42,487
LIEUTENANT JERRY.

1080
00:43:42,520 --> 00:43:44,923
NO, WITH THE THING--
I'M SORRY, THE, NO...

1081
00:43:44,957 --> 00:43:46,358
IT'S GOOD TO SEE YOU.

1082
00:43:46,392 --> 00:43:47,827
I'D LIKE TO THANK YOU
FOR RESCUING ME.

1083
00:43:47,860 --> 00:43:49,628
OH, IT WAS NOTHING...

1084
00:43:49,662 --> 00:43:52,732
IF YOU HADN'T COME.

1085
00:43:52,765 --> 00:43:54,633
- SIR, ALLOW ME TO INTRODUCE...
- WE SHOULD GET GOING.

1086
00:43:54,667 --> 00:43:55,933
OUR OTHER CREW MEMBERS.

1087
00:43:55,967 --> 00:43:57,435
- COME ON...
- I DON'T KNOW.

1088
00:43:57,468 --> 00:43:58,603
WITH ITS NEW COMMANDER,

1089
00:43:58,637 --> 00:44:00,405
THE MIGHTY JACK TEAM
IS COMPLETE.

1090
00:44:00,438 --> 00:44:02,540
♪♪

1091
00:44:06,678 --> 00:44:08,880
GUYS, HEY GUYS, WHAT'S--

1092
00:44:08,913 --> 00:44:11,817
HEY! NO! I KNEW YOU
WERE GONNA DO THIS TO ME.

1093
00:44:11,850 --> 00:44:13,352
WOULD YOU GET THIS THING
OFF MY HEAD?

1094
00:44:13,385 --> 00:44:14,687
SILENCE FOOL, SILENCE!

1095
00:44:14,720 --> 00:44:16,855
- MEOW.
- THANK YOU, THERE,
THERE FLOPSY.

1096
00:44:16,888 --> 00:44:18,790
YOU'D BETTER TELL ME
WHAT WE WANT TO KNOW.

1097
00:44:18,823 --> 00:44:21,025
THE LIGHTS IN THERE ARE CAPABLE
OF BLINDING YOU.

1098
00:44:21,058 --> 00:44:22,593
[JOEL]
OH, THAT DOESN'T BOTHER ME.

1099
00:44:22,627 --> 00:44:24,262
I'LL JUST KEEP MY EYES SHUT.

1100
00:44:24,295 --> 00:44:26,432
D'OH, FOILED AGAIN
BUT BOY IS HE SMART.

1101
00:44:26,465 --> 00:44:28,167
YOU CAN SAY THAT--
WOULD YOU KNOCK IT OFF.

1102
00:44:28,200 --> 00:44:29,635
- YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO BE A CAT.
- UH, MEOW.

1103
00:44:29,668 --> 00:44:31,170
- THANK YOU.
- YEAH, SURE.

1104
00:44:31,203 --> 00:44:33,538
HEY, WOULD YOU GUYS HURRY UP,
IT'S HOT IN HERE.

1105
00:44:33,572 --> 00:44:35,773
JOEL, AREN'T YOU JUST
THE TINIEST BIT CURIOUS

1106
00:44:35,807 --> 00:44:37,175
ABOUT THOSE BLINDING LIGHTS?

1107
00:44:37,208 --> 00:44:38,610
DON'T YOU WANT TO
PEEK JUST A LITTLE BIT?

1108
00:44:38,643 --> 00:44:39,812
NO!

1109
00:44:39,845 --> 00:44:41,613
HEY, LIKE I SAID,
HE'S SMART.

1110
00:44:41,647 --> 00:44:44,115
OH, BOY, GUESS ALL OF THOSE
SWIMSUIT POSTERS ON THE WALL

1111
00:44:44,148 --> 00:44:46,185
ARE GOING TO GO COMPLETELY
TO WASTE, AREN'T THEY?

1112
00:44:46,218 --> 00:44:47,887
AND I GUESS YOU
WOULDN'T EVEN BE INTERESTED

1113
00:44:47,920 --> 00:44:50,455
IN THAT RARE PAUL KLEE
PAINTING ON THE WALL, EITHER?

1114
00:44:50,488 --> 00:44:53,125
OH, YOU GUYS DON'T HAVE
A PAUL KLEE PAINTING.

1115
00:44:53,158 --> 00:44:55,560
- BOY, IS HE SMART.
- YEAH, THE GUY IS SMART.

1116
00:44:55,593 --> 00:44:57,228
AREN'T YOU
SUPPOSED TO BE MY CAT?

1117
00:44:57,262 --> 00:44:58,697
- UM, MEOW.
- THANK YOU.

1118
00:44:58,730 --> 00:45:00,665
- SURE.
- OH, I GOT AN IDEA.

1119
00:45:00,698 --> 00:45:03,635
JOEL, I SEEM TO HAVE MISPLACED
THE HOPE DIAMOND.

1120
00:45:03,668 --> 00:45:05,603
WOULD YOU LOOK
AROUND IN THERE FOR ME?

1121
00:45:05,637 --> 00:45:08,007
- OH, IT'S NOT IN HERE.
- WELL, DID YOU EVEN LOOK?

1122
00:45:08,040 --> 00:45:09,708
NO, I'M NOT GOING TO.

1123
00:45:09,742 --> 00:45:11,577
- BOY, IS HE SMART.
- SMART IS THE WORD.

1124
00:45:11,610 --> 00:45:12,845
[TOGETHER]
PLAN B, PLAN B, PLAN B.

1125
00:45:12,878 --> 00:45:14,747
OKAY, JOEL,
I HATE TO GET TOUGH,

1126
00:45:14,780 --> 00:45:17,415
BUT INSIDE THAT BOX WITH YOU
IS A POISON "SAMICH."

1127
00:45:17,448 --> 00:45:19,818
UH, I JUST WON'T EAT IT.

1128
00:45:19,852 --> 00:45:21,587
D'OH, FOILED AGAIN.

1129
00:45:21,620 --> 00:45:23,688
YOU'VE COMPLETELY LOST
THE CAT THING, HAVEN'T YOU?

1130
00:45:23,722 --> 00:45:25,123
I ADMIT IT,
I'M WAY OFF SCRIPT.

1131
00:45:25,157 --> 00:45:26,625
I'VE GOT NO
IDEA WHAT I'M DOING.

1132
00:45:26,658 --> 00:45:28,993
- OH, GUYS, COME ON.
- WHAT'RE YOU...

1133
00:45:29,027 --> 00:45:31,397
IT'S SO UNCOMFORTABLE
IN THERE.

1134
00:45:31,430 --> 00:45:32,998
OH, HAS THE GREAT
JOEL ROBINSON DECIDED

1135
00:45:33,032 --> 00:45:34,232
THAT FUN TIME IS
OVER NOW?

1136
00:45:34,265 --> 00:45:35,667
CHEESH.

1137
00:45:35,700 --> 00:45:37,837
- MAN, WHAT'S THE MATTER WITH--
- OKAY, JOEL, DON'T SAY HI.

1138
00:45:37,870 --> 00:45:40,438
- MEOW.
- YOU HAVE GOT TO BE
KIDDING ME, CROW!

1139
00:45:40,472 --> 00:45:44,175
HEY CROW, YOU WANNA GO GET SOME
FROZEN YOGURT OR SOMETHING--

1140
00:45:44,208 --> 00:45:46,478
[GATES OPENING]

1141
00:45:46,512 --> 00:45:49,682
[BUZZING]
HEY, WE GOT A MOVIE...

1142
00:45:55,220 --> 00:45:57,122
OH, MY CIGARETTES
ARE RINGING.

1143
00:45:57,155 --> 00:45:58,957
YOU THINK
YOU'RE SO SMART.

1144
00:45:58,990 --> 00:46:01,160
- MEOW.
- SHUT UP.

1145
00:46:01,193 --> 00:46:02,293
ATARI, HERE.

1146
00:46:02,327 --> 00:46:03,928
[MAN]
WE HAVE PROBLEMS.

1147
00:46:03,962 --> 00:46:05,130
WHAT?

1148
00:46:05,163 --> 00:46:07,065
THEY'VE DESTROYED
THE INSTALLATION.

1149
00:46:07,098 --> 00:46:09,935
WE'LL HAVE TO
RECARPET EVERYTHING.

1150
00:46:09,968 --> 00:46:12,470
YES, I'M AFRAID SO.

1151
00:46:12,503 --> 00:46:14,973
IT'S Q AGAIN.

1152
00:46:15,007 --> 00:46:16,675
NOTHING COMPARES TO Q.

1153
00:46:16,708 --> 00:46:19,645
WE URGENTLY
NEED THE TITANIUM ALLOY

1154
00:46:19,678 --> 00:46:22,713
FOR A TOP PRIORITY MILITARY
RESEARCH PROJECT.

1155
00:46:22,747 --> 00:46:24,348
GOT ANY IN
YOUR JUNK DRAWER?

1156
00:46:24,382 --> 00:46:27,385
HOW SOON CAN YOU BE READY
FOR REDEPLOYMENT?

1157
00:46:27,418 --> 00:46:30,788
WELL, LET'S SEE, I HAVE TO
SHAVE AND THEN I'LL WANT TO EAT

1158
00:46:30,822 --> 00:46:34,560
A DECENT BREAKFAST WITH TOAST,
SCRAMBLED EGGS AND BLACK COFFEE.

1159
00:46:34,593 --> 00:46:37,095
THAT'S FASCINATING,
GET OVER HERE!

1160
00:46:37,128 --> 00:46:38,797
TAKE YOUR TIME.

1161
00:46:38,830 --> 00:46:40,998
HA, HA.

1162
00:46:43,302 --> 00:46:45,703
AND DON'T FORGET,
I WANT SCRAMBLED EGGS...

1163
00:46:45,737 --> 00:46:47,738
- D'OH!
- IT REALLY GETS ME OFF.

1164
00:46:47,772 --> 00:46:50,475
[ALL]
♪ WHA, WAH, WAH, WAH ♪

1165
00:46:50,508 --> 00:46:51,977
I'LL HAVE
SOME ORANGE JUICE.

1166
00:46:52,010 --> 00:46:53,145
YES, SIR.

1167
00:46:53,178 --> 00:46:54,547
AND DON'T
FORGET THE TOAST.

1168
00:46:54,580 --> 00:46:57,482
OH, THAT RAZZY SON
OF A GUN.

1169
00:46:57,515 --> 00:46:59,552
- ENGINES ON.
- ENGINES ON.

1170
00:46:59,585 --> 00:47:01,453
THEN STRAP YOUR
HANDS ACROSS MY ENGINES.

1171
00:47:01,487 --> 00:47:04,823
- TOAST IS READY, SIR.
- READY FOR SUBMERGING.

1172
00:47:04,857 --> 00:47:06,992
- SUBMERGE!
- SUBMERGE.

1173
00:47:08,860 --> 00:47:10,728
I SAID, DRY TOAST.

1174
00:47:13,565 --> 00:47:15,867
HOW ARE WE ON
THE ABOUT-THIS-BIG METER?

1175
00:47:15,900 --> 00:47:17,468
[MAN]
WATER LEVEL, 50 FEET.

1176
00:47:17,502 --> 00:47:20,338
- UNLOCK GATES.
- UNLOCK GATES.

1177
00:47:20,372 --> 00:47:22,440
DARYL GATES, DAVID GATES
AND BREAD.

1178
00:47:22,473 --> 00:47:24,175
THERE'S
THE TOAST THING AGAIN.

1179
00:47:24,208 --> 00:47:25,877
WHAT'S WITH THE TOAST?

1180
00:47:25,910 --> 00:47:28,180
WHY'D THEY FLY THROUGH
THE WINDOW?

1181
00:47:28,213 --> 00:47:31,182
WE'VE REPLACED THE PACIFIC OCEAN
WITH FOLGERS CRYSTALS.

1182
00:47:31,215 --> 00:47:35,187
LET'S WATCH.

1183
00:47:35,220 --> 00:47:37,455
WE'LL FIRST SEARCH
THE AREA IN THE ARCTIC ZONE.

1184
00:47:37,488 --> 00:47:40,825
- YES, SIR.
- OPEN THE VENETIAN BLINDS.

1185
00:47:40,858 --> 00:47:41,827
ON COURSE, SIR.

1186
00:47:41,860 --> 00:47:44,328
WHAT'S OUR PRESENT
SPEED?

1187
00:47:44,362 --> 00:47:45,330
MACH TWO.

1188
00:47:45,363 --> 00:47:47,598
I'VE GOT A MAC CLASSIC.

1189
00:47:47,632 --> 00:47:50,868
MAINTAIN SPEED AND PROCEED IN
THE DIRECTION NORTH-NORTHWEST.

1190
00:47:50,902 --> 00:47:52,870
SEE IF
JAMES MASON'S THERE.

1191
00:47:52,903 --> 00:47:55,473
NORTH BY NORTHWEST,
THAT'S KIND OF A STRETCH.

1192
00:47:55,507 --> 00:47:57,175
ENOUGH WITH
THE BANK TURNS.

1193
00:47:57,208 --> 00:48:00,378
REALLY.

1194
00:48:00,412 --> 00:48:04,115
♪ YOU AIN'T WOMAN ENOUGH
TO TAKE MY MIGHTY JACK ♪

1195
00:48:04,148 --> 00:48:06,217
YEE-WHO.

1196
00:48:06,250 --> 00:48:09,253
WOW, IT'S
THE COVER OF "DIANETICS."

1197
00:48:09,287 --> 00:48:12,958
AND ANOTHER BANK TURN,
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1198
00:48:12,992 --> 00:48:16,462
THEY'RE CHASING THAT BRIGHT,
ELUSIVE BUTTERFLY OF LOVE.

1199
00:48:16,495 --> 00:48:18,463
KYLE MACLACHLAN.

1200
00:48:18,497 --> 00:48:20,365
YOU KNOW IT'S
REALLY GOOD TODAY, ISN'T IT?

1201
00:48:20,398 --> 00:48:21,767
UM-HMM.

1202
00:48:21,800 --> 00:48:23,168
THEY'RE ALL ENJOYING IT.

1203
00:48:23,202 --> 00:48:24,870
SIR, WHAT'S THAT?!

1204
00:48:24,903 --> 00:48:27,472
HA! MADE YOU LOOK.

1205
00:48:27,505 --> 00:48:30,075
OH, THAT'S
JUST THE SET OF "ORCA."

1206
00:48:30,108 --> 00:48:31,577
OH, IT'S JUST AN ICEBERG.

1207
00:48:31,610 --> 00:48:33,378
WE'LL BE AT THE NORTH POLE
IN FIVE MINUTES.

1208
00:48:33,412 --> 00:48:35,013
HEH-HEH.

1209
00:48:35,047 --> 00:48:38,383
SANTA CLAUS
GOING TO BE THERE?

1210
00:48:38,417 --> 00:48:39,818
HEY, IT'S ICE STATION
ZEBRA.

1211
00:48:39,852 --> 00:48:41,753
AND LOOK, HOWARD HUGHES
IS IN HIS DRAWSTRING SHORTS

1212
00:48:41,787 --> 00:48:43,322
AND HE'S GOT A MASON
JAR FILLED--

1213
00:48:43,355 --> 00:48:44,890
OH!

1214
00:48:44,923 --> 00:48:49,393
[MENACING LAUGHING]

1215
00:48:49,427 --> 00:48:51,128
NEAT.

1216
00:48:51,162 --> 00:48:52,297
[GASPS]

1217
00:48:52,330 --> 00:48:56,100
EVIL GOOD HUMOR MEN.

1218
00:48:56,133 --> 00:48:57,502
ENEMY APPROACHING.

1219
00:48:57,535 --> 00:49:00,105
PREPARE TO
LAUNCH MISSILES, PRONTO.

1220
00:49:00,138 --> 00:49:02,140
OH, HE'S ITALIAN.

1221
00:49:02,173 --> 00:49:04,108
HOW ABOUT ALLEGRO.

1222
00:49:10,715 --> 00:49:12,817
THE ENEMY
HAS NOW GONE.

1223
00:49:12,850 --> 00:49:14,318
CLOSE MISSILE SITES.

1224
00:49:14,352 --> 00:49:16,053
MEOW.

1225
00:49:16,087 --> 00:49:18,723
FREEZER
DOOR WON'T CLOSE.

1226
00:49:18,757 --> 00:49:20,692
THEY REALLY SHOULD DEFROST.

1227
00:49:20,725 --> 00:49:23,395
THAT WAS Q ALL RIGHT.

1228
00:49:23,428 --> 00:49:25,197
A CLEVER HIDING PLACE.

1229
00:49:25,230 --> 00:49:26,665
UNTIL SPRING HITS.

1230
00:49:26,698 --> 00:49:28,700
WE'LL JUST WAIT
TILL WE'RE READY TO ATTACK.

1231
00:49:28,733 --> 00:49:31,235
WHAT A BLOWHARD.

1232
00:49:31,268 --> 00:49:35,173
OUR FIRST DUTY IS TO GO INSPECT
THE FROZEN ISLAND.

1233
00:49:35,207 --> 00:49:37,975
AND THEN FIGURE OUT WHY
THE HOWELLS HAD SO MUCH LUGGAGE.

1234
00:49:38,008 --> 00:49:39,945
OH-- HMM?

1235
00:49:39,978 --> 00:49:41,713
I'M BATMAN.

1236
00:49:44,548 --> 00:49:46,818
NOW, SEE, THAT BOAT MUST
HAVE VERY LOW FAT CONTENT.

1237
00:49:46,852 --> 00:49:48,487
- NOW WHY DO YOU SAY THAT?
- GOING RIGHT TO THE BOTTOM.

1238
00:49:48,520 --> 00:49:49,888
HOLDING POSITION.

1239
00:49:49,922 --> 00:49:51,857
THERE'S NO TRACE OF THE STATION
AT THE BOTTOM OF THE SEA.

1240
00:49:51,890 --> 00:49:53,892
MAYBE THEY
SUCCEEDED IN FLOATING IT.

1241
00:49:53,925 --> 00:49:55,127
- HOW'S THE GOATEE COMING?
- THEY COULD HAVE REMOVED

1242
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:56,495
IT IN SEPARATE SECTIONS.

1243
00:49:56,528 --> 00:49:59,463
YES, THOUGH I DON'T THINK
THEY HAD TIME TO DISMANTLE IT.

1244
00:49:59,497 --> 00:50:02,233
- EDDIE, YURI.
- YES, SIR?

1245
00:50:02,267 --> 00:50:04,135
PUT ON YOUR DIVING SUITS
AND SCOUT THE WHOLE AREA.

1246
00:50:04,168 --> 00:50:05,403
YES, SIR.

1247
00:50:05,437 --> 00:50:07,405
YOU, PUT ON YOUR DIVING SUIT
AND MEET ME IN MY CABIN.

1248
00:50:07,438 --> 00:50:08,507
- YES, SIR.
- KEEP RADIO CONTACT.

1249
00:50:08,540 --> 00:50:09,540
YES, SIR.

1250
00:50:09,573 --> 00:50:11,510
SOMEBODY ELSE,
SAY, "YES, SIR."

1251
00:50:11,543 --> 00:50:13,378
- YES, SIR.
- THANK YOU.

1252
00:50:13,412 --> 00:50:15,380
[TOGETHER]
TOY DIVER,
TOY DIVER, TOY DRIVER.

1253
00:50:15,413 --> 00:50:17,248
IT'S TOY DONAHUE.
[CHUCKLES]

1254
00:50:17,282 --> 00:50:21,085
IT'S A TOY DIVE--
HA, HA...

1255
00:50:21,118 --> 00:50:23,053
SORRY.

1256
00:50:23,087 --> 00:50:26,157
FLIPPER IS MADE
OF LIQUID METAL.

1257
00:50:26,190 --> 00:50:31,195
♪♪

1258
00:50:31,228 --> 00:50:33,165
OH, WOW, MAN, THEY'RE
SWIMMING RIGHT THROUGH

1259
00:50:33,198 --> 00:50:35,500
ROBERT SCHULLER'S
CRYSTAL CATHEDRAL.

1260
00:50:35,533 --> 00:50:38,203
LOOK, SIR!

1261
00:50:38,237 --> 00:50:40,038
OH.

1262
00:50:43,508 --> 00:50:48,247
LOAD THE ROCKETS.

1263
00:50:48,280 --> 00:50:50,882
WOW, JET-PROPELLED
BLUE GILLS,

1264
00:50:50,915 --> 00:50:53,017
I READ ABOUT IT
IN "FIELD AND STREAM."

1265
00:50:53,050 --> 00:50:54,752
FIRE!

1266
00:50:54,785 --> 00:50:56,888
YES, SIR.

1267
00:50:56,922 --> 00:50:58,623
[TORPEDOS ROARING]

1268
00:50:58,657 --> 00:51:00,492
UH-OH.

1269
00:51:00,525 --> 00:51:02,227
LOOK OUT.

1270
00:51:05,197 --> 00:51:06,765
A DIRECT HIT.

1271
00:51:06,798 --> 00:51:08,500
WITH A BULLET GOING RIGHT TO
THE TOP OF THE CHARTS.

1272
00:51:08,533 --> 00:51:11,102
- JERRY, RELOAD ROCKETS.
- YES, SIR.

1273
00:51:11,135 --> 00:51:13,037
- MARY, KEEP TRACKING THEM.
- YES, SIR.

1274
00:51:13,070 --> 00:51:14,772
- BARRY, YOU GRAB MARY.
- YES, SIR.

1275
00:51:14,805 --> 00:51:16,407
I THINK ONE
OF THEM'S HURT.

1276
00:51:16,440 --> 00:51:20,445
WHEN MODELS GOOSE THEMSELVES,
NEXT ON GERALDO.

1277
00:51:20,478 --> 00:51:22,947
- LASER GUN.
- LASER GUN.

1278
00:51:22,980 --> 00:51:24,883
LASER GUN
STARRING PAT CARROLL.

1279
00:51:28,587 --> 00:51:31,288
UH, COULD SOMEONE EXPLAIN TO ME
WHAT'S GOING ON HERE, PLEASE?

1280
00:51:31,322 --> 00:51:34,425
- IT MAKES NO SENSE.
- ABSURD.

1281
00:51:34,458 --> 00:51:36,193
EDDIE, YURI,
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

1282
00:51:36,227 --> 00:51:37,528
ANSWER.

1283
00:51:37,562 --> 00:51:40,765
PLEASE PHRASE IN THE FORM
OF A QUESTION, SIR.

1284
00:51:40,798 --> 00:51:42,467
WE'RE GOING
AFTER THEM, GET READY.

1285
00:51:42,500 --> 00:51:43,702
YES, SIR.

1286
00:51:43,735 --> 00:51:45,937
- MARY, RADIO HEADQUARTERS.
- YES, SIR.

1287
00:51:45,970 --> 00:51:47,305
DOCTOR HYDE,
YOU TAKE OVER.

1288
00:51:47,338 --> 00:51:50,008
- YES, SIR.
- IT'S MISTER HYDE, SIR,
HA-HA-HA.

1289
00:51:52,810 --> 00:51:54,145
HMM.

1290
00:51:54,178 --> 00:51:57,048
[MIMICKING UNDERWATER TALKING]

1291
00:51:59,918 --> 00:52:03,955
OH, WOW, LOOK, IT'S A WAY COOL
KIND OF SCARY JELL-O THING.

1292
00:52:03,988 --> 00:52:06,825
WHAT WAS THE RESEARCH
AGENCY'S CONCLUSION?

1293
00:52:06,858 --> 00:52:08,293
I DON'T KNOW,
THEY HAVEN'T ANNOUNCED IT YET.

1294
00:52:08,327 --> 00:52:09,527
IT'S IMELDA MARCOS.

1295
00:52:09,560 --> 00:52:10,962
THERE'S ONE THING
THAT BOTHERS ME, SIR.

1296
00:52:10,995 --> 00:52:12,363
MY SERGEANT PEPPER OUTFIT.

1297
00:52:12,397 --> 00:52:14,432
THERE WAS A STRANGE CARGO SHIP
IN THE HARBOR.

1298
00:52:14,465 --> 00:52:17,702
I HAD THE FEELING THAT IT WAS
SPYING ON OUR INSTALLATIONS.

1299
00:52:17,735 --> 00:52:19,872
I TRIED TO
GET ITS NATIONALITY,

1300
00:52:19,905 --> 00:52:21,740
BUT THEN IT VANISHED,
SUDDENLY.

1301
00:52:21,773 --> 00:52:22,940
WOW.

1302
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:24,142
WOULD YOU
RECOGNIZE IT AGAIN?

1303
00:52:24,175 --> 00:52:25,510
- YES, I'M PRETTY SURE.
- COULD YOU PICK IT OUT

1304
00:52:25,543 --> 00:52:26,678
OF A LINEUP?

1305
00:52:26,712 --> 00:52:28,213
WELL, THEN I THINK YOU
OUGHT TO DO A LITTLE

1306
00:52:28,247 --> 00:52:29,513
SIGHTSEEING ALONG THE DOCKS.

1307
00:52:29,547 --> 00:52:30,515
- YES, SIR.
- SAY.

1308
00:52:30,548 --> 00:52:32,683
[SEXY]
- YES, SIR.

1309
00:52:32,717 --> 00:52:33,685
HERE IS THAT REPORT

1310
00:52:33,718 --> 00:52:35,620
FROM THE TECHNICAL
RESEARCH AGENCY.

1311
00:52:35,653 --> 00:52:37,988
OH, HEY, LOOK, IT'S
THE OLD DRUGGY GUY AGAIN.

1312
00:52:38,022 --> 00:52:40,692
THEY BELIEVE THE ISLAND
HAD NO DENSITY.

1313
00:52:40,725 --> 00:52:43,528
IT WAS ONLY H2O.

1314
00:52:43,562 --> 00:52:46,898
THAT MEANS NO MASSIVE LAND,
MERELY SOLIDIFIED WATER.

1315
00:52:46,932 --> 00:52:48,267
[ALL]
YOU MEAN, ICE?

1316
00:52:48,300 --> 00:52:50,235
THEN IT SHOULD BE
FLOATING ON THE SURFACE

1317
00:52:50,268 --> 00:52:52,237
BECAUSE OF THE SPECIFIC
GRAVITY.

1318
00:52:52,270 --> 00:52:53,772
COULD YOU
BE MORE SPECIFIC?

1319
00:52:53,805 --> 00:52:55,607
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT COULD SINK
TO THE BOTTOM OF THE OCEAN

1320
00:52:55,640 --> 00:52:57,208
WITHOUT MELTING
IN THE WARM WATER.

1321
00:52:57,242 --> 00:52:59,010
IT'S AGAINST ALL
THE LAWS OF PHYSICS.

1322
00:52:59,043 --> 00:53:01,545
CAN WE MAKE IT STICK,
CAN THE D.A. MAKE A CASE?

1323
00:53:01,578 --> 00:53:03,448
ONE THING IS CERTAIN,
TO MELT THE ICE,

1324
00:53:03,482 --> 00:53:04,917
THEY REQUIRE INTENSE HEAT.

1325
00:53:04,950 --> 00:53:07,585
OR THERE'S
ANOTHER POSSIBILITY.

1326
00:53:07,618 --> 00:53:10,355
Q HAS FOUND A WAY TO CONVERT
MOLECULAR ENERGY.

1327
00:53:10,388 --> 00:53:12,290
- THOSE STINKERS.
- D'OH.

1328
00:53:12,323 --> 00:53:14,825
VARIOUS SCIENTISTS
HAVE BEEN WORKING ON IT,

1329
00:53:14,858 --> 00:53:16,928
BUT Q MAY HAVE FOUND
THE SOLUTION.

1330
00:53:16,962 --> 00:53:18,630
- Q'S ON FIRST.
- THAT'S WHAT I'M ASKING.

1331
00:53:18,663 --> 00:53:19,897
THIRD BASE.

1332
00:53:19,930 --> 00:53:22,467
IF SUCH AN IMPORTANT
SCIENTIFIC DISCOVERY

1333
00:53:22,500 --> 00:53:25,070
WERE USED ONLY
TO SERVE EVIL PURPOSES.

1334
00:53:25,103 --> 00:53:27,372
Q IS POWERFUL.

1335
00:53:27,405 --> 00:53:30,475
THEY MAY HAVE BEEN ABLE
TO INFILTRATE OUR
OWN RESEARCH CENTER...

1336
00:53:30,508 --> 00:53:32,443
DUCK.

1337
00:53:32,477 --> 00:53:35,447
OR MAYBE THEY HAVE BEEN
ABLE TO BRIBE SOME OF
THE SCIENTISTS WORKING FOR THEM.

1338
00:53:35,480 --> 00:53:38,182
- GOOSE!
- NICE COUNTER-BLOCKING, DAD.

1339
00:53:38,215 --> 00:53:42,220
WELL, PRINCIPALLY
DR. TAKEBANA OF JAPAN.

1340
00:53:42,253 --> 00:53:46,290
I THINK THE CAMERAMAN'S
KIND OF LOST INTEREST
IN WHAT'S GOING ON THERE.

1341
00:53:46,323 --> 00:53:48,593
DR. TAKEBANA IS...

1342
00:53:48,627 --> 00:53:52,930
WALLPAPER THEATER WILL
BE BACK RIGHT AFTER THIS.

1343
00:53:52,963 --> 00:53:55,000
[WOMAN]
COULD THEY HAVE SOME
CONNECTION WITH Q?

1344
00:53:55,033 --> 00:53:57,102
COULD THEY BE AGENTS
FOR THE ORGANIZATION?

1345
00:53:57,135 --> 00:53:58,168
THEY'RE TALKING ABOUT US.

1346
00:53:58,202 --> 00:53:59,737
I LOVE WHEN
THEY TALK ABOUT US.

1347
00:53:59,770 --> 00:54:01,305
[MAN]
...TO INVESTIGATE
THE MATTER FOR US.

1348
00:54:01,338 --> 00:54:02,973
BUT THEY FINALLY REPORTED...

1349
00:54:03,007 --> 00:54:05,577
NOW THAT IS A SWELL
BLAUPUNKT.

1350
00:54:05,610 --> 00:54:08,847
IN-DASH REEL-TO-REEL.

1351
00:54:08,880 --> 00:54:13,352
HAVE YOU GOT
THEIR PHOTOGRAPHS?

1352
00:54:13,385 --> 00:54:15,120
GOT ANY WALLETS?

1353
00:54:15,153 --> 00:54:18,890
- HERE YOU ARE.
- THANK YOU.

1354
00:54:18,923 --> 00:54:21,258
THAT'S CHARLES DURNING
AND WALT DISNEY.

1355
00:54:24,762 --> 00:54:27,732
UH, WHAT?

1356
00:54:27,765 --> 00:54:31,468
OH, CHERRY CAR, MAN,
GLASS PACKS AND THRUSH PIPES.

1357
00:54:31,502 --> 00:54:33,738
OH, MAN.

1358
00:54:33,772 --> 00:54:36,007
LOOK AT THIS.

1359
00:54:36,040 --> 00:54:38,643
THIS IS CNN.

1360
00:54:38,677 --> 00:54:41,378
HUH, PLANNED PARENTHOOD?

1361
00:54:41,412 --> 00:54:44,115
STOP THE KETTLE DRUM.

1362
00:54:44,148 --> 00:54:45,983
MEOW.

1363
00:54:46,017 --> 00:54:47,918
[MAN]
COME IN, GENTLEMEN,

1364
00:54:47,952 --> 00:54:51,188
COME IN.

1365
00:54:51,222 --> 00:54:54,692
WE ARE NOW ENTERING THE FINAL
PHASE OF OUR OPERATION.

1366
00:54:54,725 --> 00:54:58,530
THE TIME HAS COME FOR US TO USE
ALL THE MEANS AT OUR DISPOSAL.

1367
00:54:58,563 --> 00:55:00,398
EVEN YOU,
THE RITZ BROTHERS.

1368
00:55:00,432 --> 00:55:02,600
AND ESPECIALLY MIGHTY JACK.

1369
00:55:02,633 --> 00:55:04,202
THEY HAVE ANNOYED US
TOO LONG.

1370
00:55:04,235 --> 00:55:08,072
I WISH YOU EVERY SUCCESS
IN THIS OUR LAST COMBAT.

1371
00:55:08,105 --> 00:55:10,007
GOOD LUCK, GENTLEMEN.

1372
00:55:10,040 --> 00:55:12,610
NOW, YOU MAY GO.

1373
00:55:12,643 --> 00:55:15,913
- YES, MASTER.
- YES, MASTER

1374
00:55:15,947 --> 00:55:19,283
[MENACING LAUGHING]

1375
00:55:19,317 --> 00:55:21,887
HMM, WHY DIDN'T THEY CALL ME
MASTER?

1376
00:55:24,022 --> 00:55:26,657
OOH.

1377
00:55:26,690 --> 00:55:28,760
ON THE WATERFRONT.

1378
00:55:28,793 --> 00:55:32,697
OH, WOW, SHE'S GOT NO TOES,
FOOT BINDING.

1379
00:55:32,730 --> 00:55:36,633
[HORN BLOWING]

1380
00:55:36,667 --> 00:55:38,537
WHAT IS SHE, A MERCHANT MARINE
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

1381
00:55:38,570 --> 00:55:40,372
AQUA MARINE,
THAT'S THE COLOR.

1382
00:55:40,405 --> 00:55:42,640
OH, MY ACHING
IMPERIALIST DOGS.

1383
00:55:42,673 --> 00:55:46,043
[HUMMING]

1384
00:55:46,077 --> 00:55:47,512
[GASPING]

1385
00:55:48,980 --> 00:55:51,215
[GASPS]

1386
00:55:51,248 --> 00:55:53,283
ALL RIGHT, LADY, WHICH DETERGENT
DO YOU PREFER?

1387
00:55:55,052 --> 00:55:57,488
HAIKIBA!

1388
00:55:57,522 --> 00:55:59,157
WHOA.

1389
00:55:59,190 --> 00:56:01,292
SHE IS A LEAN, MEAN,
LIME GREEN

1390
00:56:01,325 --> 00:56:03,093
FIGHTIN' MACHINE HERE.

1391
00:56:03,127 --> 00:56:04,128
[GRUNTING]

1392
00:56:04,162 --> 00:56:05,563
GOOD JOB.

1393
00:56:05,597 --> 00:56:07,698
OH, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT,
TWO ON ONE?

1394
00:56:07,732 --> 00:56:09,967
HEY, HEY, COME ON.

1395
00:56:10,000 --> 00:56:12,070
OH.

1396
00:56:12,103 --> 00:56:14,738
UNCALLED FOR.

1397
00:56:14,772 --> 00:56:15,807
HOLD IT, RIGHT THERE.

1398
00:56:15,840 --> 00:56:16,875
RICKY RICARDO!

1399
00:56:16,908 --> 00:56:18,375
OH, RICKY,
THEY'RE BEATING ME UP

1400
00:56:18,408 --> 00:56:21,378
FOR MESSING UP
IN THE CHOCOLATE FACTORY.

1401
00:56:21,412 --> 00:56:23,413
[GRUNTING]

1402
00:56:23,447 --> 00:56:25,983
OOH.

1403
00:56:26,017 --> 00:56:27,152
COME WITH ME.

1404
00:56:27,185 --> 00:56:29,620
♪♪

1405
00:56:29,653 --> 00:56:32,623
HEY, SHE'S BEEN KIDNAPPED
BY THE PARTRIDGE FAMILY.

1406
00:56:32,657 --> 00:56:34,058
AND THEY'RE PLAYING

1407
00:56:34,092 --> 00:56:36,828
"ECHO VALLEY 6080209".

1408
00:56:36,862 --> 00:56:39,797
♪♪

1409
00:56:39,830 --> 00:56:40,932
[GASPS]

1410
00:56:40,965 --> 00:56:42,733
♪ CUANDO PARA MUNDO ♪

1411
00:56:42,767 --> 00:56:44,435
♪ CONDIDO ESCOBAR ♪

1412
00:56:44,468 --> 00:56:46,370
♪ ESTA MI CORAZON ♪

1413
00:56:46,403 --> 00:56:47,738
♪ CHI CHI CHIMICHANGA ♪

1414
00:56:47,772 --> 00:56:48,740
OH?

1415
00:56:48,773 --> 00:56:50,175
YOU'RE BACK WITH US AGAIN.

1416
00:56:50,208 --> 00:56:51,175
WHERE AM I?

1417
00:56:51,208 --> 00:56:52,677
VASER REQUISITON.

1418
00:56:52,710 --> 00:56:54,212
MY NAME IS BOBBY ZIMMERMAN.

1419
00:56:54,245 --> 00:56:55,347
COZY, ISN'T IT?

1420
00:56:55,380 --> 00:56:57,615
HAVE YOU ANY IDEA
OF WHAT THEY WANTED?

1421
00:56:57,648 --> 00:57:00,452
NO, I HAD NO IDEA AT ALL.

1422
00:57:00,485 --> 00:57:02,720
MAYBE THEY WERE
AFTER MY MONEY.

1423
00:57:02,753 --> 00:57:04,622
THANK YOU FOR RESCUING ME.

1424
00:57:04,655 --> 00:57:06,557
NOTHING,
DON'T EVEN MENTION IT.

1425
00:57:06,590 --> 00:57:07,692
OKAY.

1426
00:57:07,725 --> 00:57:09,327
- OH.
- SOMETHING ANNOYING YOU?

1427
00:57:09,360 --> 00:57:10,728
YEAH, YOUR CAPO.

1428
00:57:10,762 --> 00:57:11,997
YOU'RE MANUEL PEREZ.

1429
00:57:12,030 --> 00:57:13,397
NO, I'M SANCHO PANZA.

1430
00:57:13,430 --> 00:57:14,565
I RECOGNIZE YOU.

1431
00:57:14,598 --> 00:57:16,100
AREN'T YOU MANUEL PEREZ?

1432
00:57:16,133 --> 00:57:17,902
[FRENCH ACCENT]
OUI, I AM THAT PERSON.

1433
00:57:17,935 --> 00:57:20,905
YOU'VE ALWAYS BEEN
A HERO FIGURE TO ME.

1434
00:57:20,938 --> 00:57:22,407
I'VE READ YOUR BOOKS

1435
00:57:22,440 --> 00:57:23,508
AND KNOW ALL ABOUT
YOUR EARLY STRUGGLES.

1436
00:57:23,542 --> 00:57:25,310
SAY.

1437
00:57:25,343 --> 00:57:27,312
YOU DID SUCH GOOD WORK
IN THE THIRD WORLD.

1438
00:57:27,345 --> 00:57:29,680
OH, ARE YOU SPEAKING TO ME?

1439
00:57:29,713 --> 00:57:31,748
ARE YOU STILL INVOLVED
IN POLITICS?

1440
00:57:31,782 --> 00:57:34,752
♪♪

1441
00:57:34,785 --> 00:57:37,222
WHOA,
THE POLITICS OF MOTION.

1442
00:57:37,255 --> 00:57:39,357
THE POLITICS OF FEELING GOOD.

1443
00:57:39,390 --> 00:57:42,960
AH, WE'LL ORDER OFF THE MENU.

1444
00:57:42,993 --> 00:57:44,562
OH, MAN, LOOK AT
THE APPENDIX SCAR,

1445
00:57:44,595 --> 00:57:46,230
WHO'S THE BODY DOUBLE,
JACK KLUGMAN?

1446
00:57:46,263 --> 00:57:48,867
YEOW.

1447
00:57:48,900 --> 00:57:51,235
UH, WE'RE TRYING
TO EAT OVER HERE.

1448
00:57:51,268 --> 00:57:53,337
I LOVE GOING TO FRIDAY'S.

1449
00:57:53,370 --> 00:57:55,473
SALUT.

1450
00:57:55,507 --> 00:57:57,075
I WAS IN ANNA CHRISTIE
AT THE PROVINCETOWN--

1451
00:57:57,108 --> 00:57:58,710
THANK YOU.

1452
00:57:58,743 --> 00:58:03,247
[JAZZ PLAYING]

1453
00:58:03,280 --> 00:58:05,317
EXCUSE ME A SECOND.

1454
00:58:05,350 --> 00:58:07,285
- LOOK AFTER HIM.
- SURE.

1455
00:58:07,318 --> 00:58:09,620
SHE'S GOING TO THROW UP.

1456
00:58:11,555 --> 00:58:12,657
WHAT TOOK YOU SO LONG?

1457
00:58:12,690 --> 00:58:14,425
I WAS BEGINNING
TO GET WORRIED.

1458
00:58:14,458 --> 00:58:16,493
- WAS THAT THE SHIP?
- NO.

1459
00:58:16,527 --> 00:58:19,130
BUT SOMETHING ELSE HAPPENED.
Q TRIED TO KIDNAP ME.

1460
00:58:19,163 --> 00:58:20,498
[GASPING]

1461
00:58:20,532 --> 00:58:22,267
ONLY I WAS SAVED
BY THIS MAN, PEREZ.

1462
00:58:22,300 --> 00:58:24,002
DID HE GIVE YOU THOSE JAMMIES?

1463
00:58:24,035 --> 00:58:26,270
HEY, A VIEW MASTER.

1464
00:58:26,303 --> 00:58:28,105
AND IT'S MOUNT RUSHMORE.

1465
00:58:32,343 --> 00:58:33,410
HMM?

1466
00:58:33,443 --> 00:58:36,080
- IT'S MEL TORME.
- IT'S DON ADAMS.

1467
00:58:36,113 --> 00:58:38,048
- NOEL COWARD?
- TOMMY SLEDGE?

1468
00:58:38,082 --> 00:58:40,083
OH, CAN I HELP YOU?

1469
00:58:40,117 --> 00:58:41,920
ARE YOU LOOKING FOR
ANYTHING SPECIAL.

1470
00:58:41,953 --> 00:58:44,355
WELL, NO,
I'M JUST BROWSING AROUND.

1471
00:58:44,388 --> 00:58:46,557
YOU SEE, I HAVE TO DO
A LOT OF TRAVELING

1472
00:58:46,590 --> 00:58:48,860
SO I'M ALWAYS
BUYING TRAVEL GUIDES.

1473
00:58:48,893 --> 00:58:51,328
THAT'S A PICTURE OF YOU NAKED.
YOU ARE SICK.

1474
00:58:51,362 --> 00:58:54,565
SPECIAL CORRESPONDENT
FOR WORLD MAGAZINE.

1475
00:58:54,598 --> 00:58:57,068
ROBERTO OKUMURA.

1476
00:58:57,102 --> 00:58:59,870
WELL... YOU'RE THE FAMOUS
WRITER, AREN'T YOU?

1477
00:58:59,903 --> 00:59:02,373
WELL, COULD BE, YOUR GUESS
IS AS GOOD AS MINE.

1478
00:59:02,407 --> 00:59:04,975
I READ ONE OF YOUR ARTICLES
A SHORT WHILE AGO.

1479
00:59:05,008 --> 00:59:06,143
IT SUCKED.

1480
00:59:06,177 --> 00:59:07,578
AND I THOUGHT YOU DID A
WONDERFUL JOB DESCRIBING

1481
00:59:07,612 --> 00:59:09,947
Q'S INCREASING POWER
IN THE VARIOUS COUNTRIES.

1482
00:59:09,980 --> 00:59:11,682
OUI, I DID DO THAT.

1483
00:59:11,715 --> 00:59:14,418
I SEE YOU HAVE A RATHER
SPECIAL INTEREST IN IT.

1484
00:59:14,452 --> 00:59:16,087
MIGHTY JACK INTERESTS YOU, TOO,
I GUESS.

1485
00:59:16,120 --> 00:59:18,723
WHAT, NO, WE'RE JUST HAVING
SOME COFFEE...

1486
00:59:18,757 --> 00:59:21,158
I DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.

1487
00:59:21,192 --> 00:59:23,193
I'M ONLY A SALESGIRL
IN THE STORE HERE.

1488
00:59:23,227 --> 00:59:24,895
I GOT ANOTHER TIP
FOR MIGHTY JACK.

1489
00:59:24,928 --> 00:59:27,432
WHY DON'T WE STEP OUT AND HAVE
A LITTLE CUP OF COFFEE.

1490
00:59:27,465 --> 00:59:29,167
JUST THE TWO OF US.

1491
00:59:29,200 --> 00:59:31,502
BUILDING CASTLES
IN THE SAND.

1492
00:59:31,535 --> 00:59:33,237
WE CAN CHAT ABOUT MIGHTY JACK.

1493
00:59:33,270 --> 00:59:35,272
IT'S GOT A LOT OF FRIENDS
IN THIS STORE.

1494
00:59:35,305 --> 00:59:37,008
- ROBERTO.
- HMM?

1495
00:59:37,042 --> 00:59:39,910
I DON'T THINK THAT YOUR READERS
WOULD BE INTERESTED

1496
00:59:39,943 --> 00:59:41,812
IN WHAT GOES ON
AROUND HERE, DO YOU?

1497
00:59:41,845 --> 00:59:46,217
AH, YOU'RE THE PERSON IN CHARGE
HERE, MR. ATARI, RIGHT?

1498
00:59:46,250 --> 00:59:48,152
STILL TRYING
TO WATCH PONG, EH?

1499
00:59:48,185 --> 00:59:50,455
YES, THE FAMOUS MR. ATARI.

1500
00:59:50,488 --> 00:59:52,090
[CHUCKLING]

1501
00:59:52,123 --> 00:59:53,725
YOU KNOW WHAT PUZZLES ME?

1502
00:59:53,758 --> 00:59:56,027
THE NEWSPAPERS OFTEN
TALK ABOUT MIGHTY JACK,

1503
00:59:56,060 --> 00:59:57,862
BUT NOBODY DOES
ANYTHING ABOUT IT.

1504
00:59:57,895 --> 01:00:00,130
THEY NEVER MENTION THE CREW,
NOT ONCE.

1505
01:00:00,163 --> 01:00:02,833
ONLY THE MECHANICAL DETAILS.

1506
01:00:02,867 --> 01:00:05,202
THE DESIGN AND ALL ITS
LATEST EQUIPMENT.

1507
01:00:05,235 --> 01:00:07,905
I HAVE A RESPONSIBILITY
TO OUR READERS.

1508
01:00:07,938 --> 01:00:10,908
I'D LIKE TO WRITE
ABOUT WHO THE CREW IS.

1509
01:00:10,942 --> 01:00:13,310
ALL THE HUMAN INTEREST STUFF,
YOU KNOW.

1510
01:00:13,343 --> 01:00:15,513
WELL, THEN WRITE
WHAT YOU HAVE TO.

1511
01:00:15,547 --> 01:00:17,048
UH-OH.

1512
01:00:17,082 --> 01:00:19,417
[SCREAMING]

1513
01:00:19,450 --> 01:00:22,420
OH, I FORGOT IT'S
TUESDAY!

1514
01:00:22,453 --> 01:00:24,622
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT, ROBERTO?

1515
01:00:24,655 --> 01:00:27,392
NO, MY ELBOW EXPLODED,
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1516
01:00:27,425 --> 01:00:30,227
OH, OSWALD.

1517
01:00:30,260 --> 01:00:33,063
NO, NO, NO.

1518
01:00:33,097 --> 01:00:35,467
HEY, DON'T POINT,
THAT'S NOT POLITE.

1519
01:00:35,500 --> 01:00:39,837
BUT WAIT,
MR. ICE CREAM MAN.

1520
01:00:39,870 --> 01:00:42,440
UP THERE, THE ROOF!

1521
01:00:42,473 --> 01:00:44,508
UP YOURS, YOU GOOF!

1522
01:00:44,542 --> 01:00:46,543
KATO, LOOK OUT!

1523
01:00:52,550 --> 01:00:53,683
BLASTED.

1524
01:00:53,717 --> 01:00:55,853
DARN DERN-MA-GERGOT.

1525
01:00:55,887 --> 01:00:57,588
- JERRY!
- WHERE IS HE?

1526
01:00:57,622 --> 01:00:58,990
HE GOT AWAY.

1527
01:00:59,023 --> 01:01:00,257
OH, WHAT HAVE YOU GOT THERE?

1528
01:01:00,290 --> 01:01:01,558
WAITH, WAIT,
HE'S TALKING TO HIMSELF.

1529
01:01:01,592 --> 01:01:03,093
I FOUND THIS
ON THE STAIRCASE.

1530
01:01:05,295 --> 01:01:06,963
YOUR WINDSONG
STAYS ON MY MIND.

1531
01:01:06,997 --> 01:01:08,498
A STRANGE LOOKING BULLET.

1532
01:01:08,532 --> 01:01:10,067
IT'S TRANSPARENT.

1533
01:01:10,100 --> 01:01:11,568
LIKE THIS PLOT.

1534
01:01:11,602 --> 01:01:15,072
I'VE NEVER SEEN ANYTHING
LIKE THIS BEFORE.

1535
01:01:15,105 --> 01:01:18,777
- HOW DID IT GO?
- SAME RESULTS AS BEFORE.

1536
01:01:18,810 --> 01:01:20,412
IS THAT SO?

1537
01:01:20,445 --> 01:01:23,613
WE RAISED THE HEAT TO 800
DEGREES WITHOUT MELTING IT,

1538
01:01:23,647 --> 01:01:25,717
OR EVEN ALTERING
ITS MOLECULAR STRUCTURE.

1539
01:01:25,750 --> 01:01:27,185
IT'S DEFINITE PROOF THAT--

1540
01:01:27,218 --> 01:01:28,552
SHH!

1541
01:01:28,585 --> 01:01:30,822
THE MAN MIGHT BE LISTENING.

1542
01:01:34,258 --> 01:01:36,760
HA!

1543
01:01:36,793 --> 01:01:38,830
OH.

1544
01:01:38,863 --> 01:01:40,965
AH.

1545
01:01:40,998 --> 01:01:42,433
AH.

1546
01:01:42,467 --> 01:01:45,470
ROLLING PAPERS,
I'LL ROLL US A DOOB.

1547
01:01:45,503 --> 01:01:47,105
YOU PUT ON SOME
ALLMAN BROTHERS.

1548
01:01:47,138 --> 01:01:48,605
THAT "EAT A PEACH" ALBUM.

1549
01:01:48,638 --> 01:01:51,775
[CHUCKLING]

1550
01:01:51,808 --> 01:01:56,147
[GURGLING]
I HEAR IT'S A WONDERFUL
AFTERNOON TO BE DOING...

1551
01:01:56,180 --> 01:01:58,282
YOU KNEW ABOUT THAT?

1552
01:01:58,315 --> 01:02:00,785
SOMETIMES IT'S NECESSARY TO KEEP
THE ENEMY WELL INFORMED.

1553
01:02:00,818 --> 01:02:03,687
I THOUGHT THAT WE OUGHT TO TELL
THEM WE KNEW

1554
01:02:03,720 --> 01:02:05,690
ABOUT THE HIGH TEMPERATURE ICE.

1555
01:02:05,723 --> 01:02:07,458
NOW WE'LL WAIT AND SEE
HOW THEY REACT.

1556
01:02:07,492 --> 01:02:09,560
OH.

1557
01:02:09,593 --> 01:02:11,095
YOU MEAN, ROBERTO?

1558
01:02:11,128 --> 01:02:12,230
DURÁN?

1559
01:02:12,263 --> 01:02:13,965
YES, HE'S AN AGENT OF Q.

1560
01:02:13,998 --> 01:02:15,667
AND PEREZ?

1561
01:02:15,700 --> 01:02:17,033
WELL,
WE'LL ALWAYS HAVE PEREZ.

1562
01:02:17,067 --> 01:02:18,468
THERE'S NO PROOF YET.

1563
01:02:18,502 --> 01:02:19,970
CATHERINE'S INVESTIGATING
THAT NOW.

1564
01:02:20,003 --> 01:02:23,140
I UNDERSTAND DR. TAKEBANA
WILL BE RETURNING TOMORROW.

1565
01:02:23,173 --> 01:02:25,943
GOOD,
WE'LL GO QUESTION HIM.

1566
01:02:25,977 --> 01:02:27,077
IS THE DOCTOR A Q AGENT?

1567
01:02:27,110 --> 01:02:30,113
[MOCKING]
IS THE DOCTOR A Q AGENT?

1568
01:02:30,147 --> 01:02:32,217
- A JOB FOR YOU, ATARI.
- YES.

1569
01:02:35,252 --> 01:02:38,222
ON A VERY SPECIAL
"TRAPPER JOHN, MD."

1570
01:02:40,357 --> 01:02:42,260
OH, IT'S THIRSTY THURSDAY.

1571
01:02:42,293 --> 01:02:44,428
TWO BUCKS FOR A MUG AND THEN
RASPBERRY COSMOS

1572
01:02:44,462 --> 01:02:46,030
ARE A BUCK AFTER THAT.

1573
01:02:46,063 --> 01:02:49,367
- INTERESTING LECTURE.
- I'M GLAD YOU ENJOYED IT.

1574
01:02:49,400 --> 01:02:51,202
I DID SOME RESEARCH...

1575
01:02:51,235 --> 01:02:53,637
EXCUSE ME, DOCTOR,
WE'D LIKE TO SPEAK TO YOU.

1576
01:02:53,670 --> 01:02:55,807
- NOT NOW, I'M VERY BUSY.
- IT'S ABOUT HOT ICE.

1577
01:02:55,840 --> 01:02:56,973
[GASPING]

1578
01:02:57,007 --> 01:02:59,510
WOW, MY FAVORITE BAND.

1579
01:02:59,543 --> 01:03:00,945
HERE.

1580
01:03:06,017 --> 01:03:08,752
IT'S NOT MADE OF GLASS,
BUT ONLY OF WATER.

1581
01:03:08,785 --> 01:03:10,688
BUT IT'S THE BEST I CAN DO.

1582
01:03:10,722 --> 01:03:12,490
I BELIEVE YOU WERE WORKING ON
THIS EXPERIMENT.

1583
01:03:12,523 --> 01:03:14,492
UH, DID YOU CLEAN
THAT OFF REAL GOOD?

1584
01:03:14,525 --> 01:03:16,227
OOH.

1585
01:03:16,260 --> 01:03:18,628
ICE, ICE, BABY?

1586
01:03:20,497 --> 01:03:22,700
WOULD YOU GENTLEMEN EXCUSE ME?

1587
01:03:22,733 --> 01:03:24,368
- OF COURSE.
- THANK YOU.

1588
01:03:24,402 --> 01:03:26,370
ABOUT A THING...

1589
01:03:26,403 --> 01:03:28,005
THANK YOU.

1590
01:03:28,038 --> 01:03:29,573
OH, FRITZ, I'LL TAKE THAT.

1591
01:03:29,607 --> 01:03:30,942
FRITZ.

1592
01:03:30,975 --> 01:03:31,942
SURE THINK, STOTCH.

1593
01:03:31,975 --> 01:03:33,310
WE, UH...

1594
01:03:33,343 --> 01:03:35,012
THIS IS FRITZ,
HE'S MY ASSISTANT.

1595
01:03:35,045 --> 01:03:37,248
- ATARI.
- HOW DO YOU DO.

1596
01:03:37,282 --> 01:03:38,782
[CLEARING THROAT]

1597
01:03:38,815 --> 01:03:40,517
HOW DO YOU DO.

1598
01:03:40,550 --> 01:03:42,287
WELL, I MUST GO NOW.

1599
01:03:42,320 --> 01:03:43,520
GOODBYE.

1600
01:03:43,553 --> 01:03:45,488
- SHALL WE GO TO MY OFFICE?
- ALL RIGHT.

1601
01:03:45,522 --> 01:03:47,258
♪♪

1602
01:03:52,863 --> 01:03:54,998
SOMEONE BROKE IN
AND STOLE ALL MY RECORDS.

1603
01:03:55,032 --> 01:03:57,568
- JIM NABORS, ED AMES...
- TEN YEARS OF RESEARCH.

1604
01:03:57,602 --> 01:03:59,970
I'D NEARLY COMPLETED
ALL MY EXPERIMENTS.

1605
01:04:00,003 --> 01:04:02,840
AND THEN ONE DAY,
ALL MY PAPERS WERE GONE.

1606
01:04:02,873 --> 01:04:04,542
SO I QUIT MY ROUTE.

1607
01:04:04,575 --> 01:04:05,943
WHAT A TRAGEDY.

1608
01:04:05,977 --> 01:04:07,545
LIBERTÉ, ÉGALITÉ.

1609
01:04:07,578 --> 01:04:09,347
AND NOW I SEE THAT SOMEONE

1610
01:04:09,380 --> 01:04:12,283
HAS CARRIED MY WORK
TO ITS FINAL STAGE.

1611
01:04:12,317 --> 01:04:15,385
ICE THAT WON'T MELT EVEN UNDER
VERY HIGH TEMPERATURES.

1612
01:04:15,418 --> 01:04:17,288
[ALL]
SO WHAT?
SHEESH.

1613
01:04:17,322 --> 01:04:20,357
ATARI, HAVE YOU ANY IDEA
WHO COULD HAVE STOLEN THEM?

1614
01:04:20,390 --> 01:04:22,225
COULD IT BE DR. VON MULLER
FROM WEST GERMANY?

1615
01:04:22,258 --> 01:04:23,793
WRONG, GO FISH.

1616
01:04:23,827 --> 01:04:25,897
HE'S ENGAGED
IN SIMILAR RESEARCH

1617
01:04:25,930 --> 01:04:28,698
THOUGH OUR METHODS
ARE QUITE DIFFERENT.

1618
01:04:28,732 --> 01:04:30,567
IF YOU ANALYZE
THIS SUBSTANCE,

1619
01:04:30,600 --> 01:04:32,937
YOU WILL SEE THAT IT
COULD NOT HAVE BEEN MADE

1620
01:04:32,970 --> 01:04:34,572
WITHOUT USING MY PROCESS.

1621
01:04:34,605 --> 01:04:36,507
WHICH IS LIQUID METAL.

1622
01:04:36,540 --> 01:04:38,608
COULD IT HAVE BEEN FRITZ,
YOUR ASSISTANT?

1623
01:04:38,642 --> 01:04:40,978
- NO, DEFINITELY NOT.
- WHY NOT?

1624
01:04:41,012 --> 01:04:43,647
YOU SEE,
FRITZ IS MY SON.

1625
01:04:43,680 --> 01:04:45,683
YOU NAMED YOUR SON, FRITZ?

1626
01:04:45,717 --> 01:04:48,285
AND MY WIFE DIED
MANY YEARS AGO.

1627
01:04:48,318 --> 01:04:49,720
SHE WAS GERMAN.

1628
01:04:49,753 --> 01:04:51,555
- SO YOU'RE AVAILABLE.
- FRITZ IS MY SON.

1629
01:04:51,588 --> 01:04:53,490
HE GREW UP IN BERLIN.

1630
01:04:53,523 --> 01:04:55,258
I UNDERSTAND.

1631
01:04:55,292 --> 01:04:59,097
ATARI, I TOLD YOU
A LITTLE WHILE AGO

1632
01:04:59,130 --> 01:05:02,032
ALL THAT WORK OF TEN YEARS
HAD BEEN STOLEN.

1633
01:05:02,065 --> 01:05:04,035
I LIED.

1634
01:05:04,068 --> 01:05:06,370
IT WAS A GREAT LOSS.

1635
01:05:06,403 --> 01:05:09,807
BUT NOW I REALIZE I WAS WRONG TO
SPEAK ABOUT MY WORK PREMATURELY.

1636
01:05:09,840 --> 01:05:11,975
OOPS.

1637
01:05:12,008 --> 01:05:13,978
IT WAS OUT OF VANITY.

1638
01:05:14,012 --> 01:05:15,913
AND APOLLONIA.

1639
01:05:18,848 --> 01:05:23,187
♪♪

1640
01:05:23,220 --> 01:05:24,322
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1641
01:05:24,355 --> 01:05:25,422
LET'S GO ITALIAN TODAY.

1642
01:05:25,455 --> 01:05:27,558
IT'S HARD TO SAY IF HE'S
TELLING THE TRUTH.

1643
01:05:27,592 --> 01:05:29,327
BUT HE SOUNDED VERY SINCERE.

1644
01:05:29,360 --> 01:05:31,095
THERE'S STILL ONE SUSPECT.

1645
01:05:31,128 --> 01:05:32,430
WHO?

1646
01:05:32,463 --> 01:05:33,630
DR. VON MULLER.

1647
01:05:33,663 --> 01:05:34,998
OH, THE CHINESE GUY.

1648
01:05:35,032 --> 01:05:36,933
LET'S GO THEN.

1649
01:05:39,403 --> 01:05:42,373
MYSTERY GUEST,
SIGN IN, PLEASE!

1650
01:05:42,407 --> 01:05:45,843
WELL, HERE WE ARE AT DR. KLUTZY
VON DOORKNOBS PLACE.

1651
01:05:45,877 --> 01:05:48,612
WELL, ATARI,
IT'S GOOD YOU'RE HERE.

1652
01:05:48,645 --> 01:05:50,682
I'D LIKE TO INTRODUCE THIS
GENTLEMAN TO YOU.

1653
01:05:50,715 --> 01:05:52,148
THIS IS DR. VON MULLER.

1654
01:05:52,182 --> 01:05:53,650
WE'VE BEEN SMOKING
LEBANESE BLONDE

1655
01:05:53,683 --> 01:05:55,152
AND WE'RE FLYING RIGHT NOW.

1656
01:05:55,185 --> 01:05:56,687
- HOW DO YOU DO?
- DOCTOR.

1657
01:05:56,720 --> 01:05:58,088
[MIMICKING BUZZER]

1658
01:05:58,122 --> 01:06:00,190
- JOY BUZZER.
- LOVE THAT GAG.

1659
01:06:00,223 --> 01:06:01,825
PLEASE SIT DOWN.

1660
01:06:03,760 --> 01:06:05,863
- ATARI?
- SIR.

1661
01:06:05,897 --> 01:06:07,665
- WHERE DO YOU GET
YOUR SUIT WAXED?
- DR. VON MULLER ALSO CLAIMS

1662
01:06:07,698 --> 01:06:09,033
THAT ALL HIS RESEARCH AND
DOCUMENTS

1663
01:06:09,067 --> 01:06:10,333
HAVE BEEN STOLEN.

1664
01:06:10,367 --> 01:06:13,137
OH, ANDY, OH...
MY RESEARCH DOCUMENTS...

1665
01:06:13,170 --> 01:06:15,773
YEAH, IT'S TRUE, YEAH.

1666
01:06:15,807 --> 01:06:18,442
THEN YOU'RE HALF JAPANESE,
HALF FRENCH

1667
01:06:18,475 --> 01:06:20,510
WITH SOME VIETNAMESE MIXED IN,
IS THAT RIGHT?

1668
01:06:20,543 --> 01:06:22,178
YEAH,
THEY CALL ME MONGREL BOY.

1669
01:06:22,212 --> 01:06:25,415
DURING THE WAR,
I WAS SENT TO SCHOOL IN ITALY.

1670
01:06:25,448 --> 01:06:27,985
316 SPEED, THAT'S ALL
I EVER HEARD.

1671
01:06:28,018 --> 01:06:30,087
MY PARENTS THOUGHT I'D BE MORE
SHELTERED THERE.

1672
01:06:30,120 --> 01:06:32,657
I NEVER SAW
EITHER OF THEM AGAIN.

1673
01:06:32,690 --> 01:06:35,258
THEY BOTH DIED IN VIETNAM.

1674
01:06:35,292 --> 01:06:36,927
OH, THAT WAR.

1675
01:06:36,960 --> 01:06:39,297
[WHISPERING]
SHH, DON'T TALK ABOUT THAT WAR.

1676
01:06:39,330 --> 01:06:41,665
I'M SURE YOU SUFFERED
A GREAT DEAL THEN.

1677
01:06:41,698 --> 01:06:44,368
SUFFERED, OH, YES, YES.

1678
01:06:44,402 --> 01:06:45,568
BUT TODAY THE WORLD'S A
DIFFERENT PLACE.

1679
01:06:45,602 --> 01:06:47,638
THERE'S SO MUCH TO LIVE FOR.

1680
01:06:47,672 --> 01:06:50,540
OH, YOU DON'T KNOW
THE HALF OF IT, HM.

1681
01:06:50,573 --> 01:06:52,175
THEY SAY...

1682
01:06:52,208 --> 01:06:55,178
THAT THE HAPPIEST PEOPLE
ARE THE ONES WITH FAITH.

1683
01:06:55,212 --> 01:06:57,782
WHAT ARE YOU BARBRA STREISAND
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

1684
01:07:01,085 --> 01:07:02,520
OH...

1685
01:07:02,553 --> 01:07:05,055
I'M AFRAID THAT
I LEFT MY CIGARETTE LIGHTER

1686
01:07:05,088 --> 01:07:06,723
IN YOUR STORE THE OTHER DAY.

1687
01:07:06,757 --> 01:07:08,125
[CHUCKLING]

1688
01:07:08,158 --> 01:07:10,027
THE ONE WHO STOLE THOSE PAPERS
MUST BE WORKING FOR Q.

1689
01:07:10,060 --> 01:07:13,197
WE HAVE TO TRY AND SET SOME KIND
OF TRAP TO DISCOVER THE TRAITOR.

1690
01:07:13,230 --> 01:07:15,767
- RIGHT-- HARRY, EDDIE?
- YES, SIR?

1691
01:07:15,800 --> 01:07:17,868
FIND OUT WHO ELSE
HAD ACCESS TO THOSE FILES.

1692
01:07:17,902 --> 01:07:19,068
HEY, WHAT'S WILLIAM FAULKNER
DOING IN THERE?

1693
01:07:19,102 --> 01:07:20,938
DID YOU SEE A LIGHTER?

1694
01:07:20,972 --> 01:07:22,673
HEY, THAT SCENE JUST HOOKED UP
WITH THE OTHER SCENE.

1695
01:07:22,707 --> 01:07:25,142
- WOW, NOW THEY'RE BACK-- OH.
- HERE IT IS.

1696
01:07:25,175 --> 01:07:26,477
THANK YOU.

1697
01:07:26,510 --> 01:07:28,245
AND HERE'S SOMETHING FOR YOU.

1698
01:07:28,278 --> 01:07:29,980
OH.

1699
01:07:30,013 --> 01:07:31,882
WELL,
IT'S BEEN REAL NICE.

1700
01:07:31,915 --> 01:07:34,252
SEE YOU LATER, KID.

1701
01:07:34,285 --> 01:07:35,518
♪ OOH-BEE-DOO-BEE-DOO ♪

1702
01:07:35,552 --> 01:07:37,087
♪ BAH-DAH-DUB-DAH ♪

1703
01:07:37,120 --> 01:07:39,323
♪ BAH-BAH-BAH-BOOM ♪

1704
01:07:40,925 --> 01:07:42,993
AH, RUPERT MURDOCH.

1705
01:07:43,027 --> 01:07:45,963
[WHISTLING LA MARSEILLAISE]

1706
01:07:51,335 --> 01:07:52,770
ENOUGH.

1707
01:07:52,803 --> 01:07:54,438
NOW WE HAVE TO PAY
THE FRENCH GOVERNMENT.

1708
01:07:54,472 --> 01:07:56,640
OH, THIS IS JUST LIKE
THE CHASE SCENE

1709
01:07:56,673 --> 01:07:58,542
FROM "THE FRENCH CONNECTION."

1710
01:07:58,575 --> 01:08:02,880
SO THAT WAS FRENCH,
THE WHOLE FRENCH THING.

1711
01:08:02,913 --> 01:08:05,748
IT'S VERY FRENCH.

1712
01:08:05,782 --> 01:08:07,985
OH, THEY'RE JUST GOING
TO SPEND SOME TIME

1713
01:08:08,018 --> 01:08:10,087
IN THE DISCIPLINE BOX, THERE.

1714
01:08:12,455 --> 01:08:14,125
MIGHTY JACK.

1715
01:08:18,695 --> 01:08:21,098
PEREZ... AVANTI.

1716
01:08:21,132 --> 01:08:22,500
SI.

1717
01:08:22,533 --> 01:08:24,033
SI?

1718
01:08:27,203 --> 01:08:28,572
BEEN WAITING LONG?

1719
01:08:28,605 --> 01:08:29,807
ALL MY LIFE.

1720
01:08:29,840 --> 01:08:31,208
AH!

1721
01:08:31,242 --> 01:08:32,475
THAT LONG, HUH?

1722
01:08:32,508 --> 01:08:33,843
I'M GOING OUT TO EAT NOW.

1723
01:08:33,877 --> 01:08:34,945
I JUST CAME INTO
A LITTLE MONEY.

1724
01:08:34,978 --> 01:08:36,180
ARE YOU FREE FOR DINNER
TONIGHT?

1725
01:08:36,213 --> 01:08:37,615
YES, I AM.

1726
01:08:37,648 --> 01:08:38,882
ARBY'S OKAY?

1727
01:08:38,915 --> 01:08:40,117
IS THIS YOUR CAR?

1728
01:08:40,150 --> 01:08:41,718
NO, I BORROWED IT
FROM A FRIEND.

1729
01:08:41,752 --> 01:08:42,720
OH, I SEE.

1730
01:08:42,753 --> 01:08:44,522
I KNOW A TERRIFIC NEW PLACE.

1731
01:08:44,555 --> 01:08:46,423
COME ON, GET IN, OKAY?

1732
01:08:46,457 --> 01:08:47,858
DO YOU UNDERSTAND HIM?

1733
01:08:47,892 --> 01:08:49,827
UNH-UNH.

1734
01:08:49,860 --> 01:08:53,130
UM, TAKE ME
TO THE NEAREST PLOT POINT.

1735
01:08:54,932 --> 01:08:56,767
NICE HELMET, THERE.

1736
01:08:56,800 --> 01:08:58,768
♪♪

1737
01:08:58,802 --> 01:09:00,037
SAY, YOU'RE KINKY.

1738
01:09:00,070 --> 01:09:01,872
SO ANYWAY, THAT'S WHY
I USE OLD SPICE.

1739
01:09:01,905 --> 01:09:03,607
AHH.

1740
01:09:03,640 --> 01:09:05,275
ENTER.

1741
01:09:05,308 --> 01:09:08,912
ENTER, WHATEVER HAPPENED
TO COME IN?

1742
01:09:08,945 --> 01:09:11,982
SORRY, DEAR, I'M AFRAID
WE HAVE TO PUT YOU IN STEERAGE.

1743
01:09:12,015 --> 01:09:14,485
PLEASE.

1744
01:09:14,518 --> 01:09:16,620
TIGHT, THAT CAPTAIN.

1745
01:09:16,653 --> 01:09:18,522
HA, HA, ARRR.

1746
01:09:21,592 --> 01:09:23,327
PRONTO, PRONTO.

1747
01:09:23,360 --> 01:09:24,795
PUPS, MINI-DOUGHNUTS,

1748
01:09:24,828 --> 01:09:26,363
COTTON CANDY,
THAT SORT OF THING.

1749
01:09:26,397 --> 01:09:28,098
[SPEAKING ITALIAN]

1750
01:09:28,132 --> 01:09:30,367
[SPEAKING ITALIAN]

1751
01:09:30,400 --> 01:09:32,837
OOH-EE-OOH-AH-AH.

1752
01:09:32,870 --> 01:09:34,905
TING-TANG-WALLA-WALLA-BING-BANG.

1753
01:09:34,938 --> 01:09:37,742
WHAT KHADAFI'S HOSTING
SCIENCE THEATER?

1754
01:09:37,775 --> 01:09:39,710
OPERATION TWO, COMPLETED.

1755
01:09:39,743 --> 01:09:43,313
GET ON WITH THIS.

1756
01:09:43,347 --> 01:09:45,082
- [SPEAKING ITALIAN]
BENE, PRONTO.

1757
01:09:45,115 --> 01:09:47,450
I'M OFF SCRIPT NOW.

1758
01:09:47,483 --> 01:09:50,353
[CHUCKLING]

1759
01:09:50,387 --> 01:09:51,622
WHAT DID YOU SAY?

1760
01:09:51,655 --> 01:09:53,357
I DON'T KNOW,
IT WAS ITALIAN.

1761
01:09:53,390 --> 01:09:54,758
I THINK I ORDERED WINE.

1762
01:09:54,792 --> 01:09:57,595
IN AMORI BAY,
THEY'RE NOW CONSTRUCTING...

1763
01:09:57,628 --> 01:09:58,862
- AMORI?
- ... A NEW ISLAND

1764
01:09:58,895 --> 01:10:01,232
FOR THEIR EXPERIMENTS
TO REPLACE THE OLD ONE.

1765
01:10:01,265 --> 01:10:03,567
BUT I JUST GAVE ORDERS
TO HAVE IT DESTROYED

1766
01:10:03,600 --> 01:10:05,902
WITH OUR ICEBERG METHOD.

1767
01:10:05,935 --> 01:10:07,705
- ICEBERG MENACE?
- DESTROY IT?

1768
01:10:07,738 --> 01:10:09,407
OF COURSE.

1769
01:10:09,440 --> 01:10:12,475
ONCE IT IS DESTROYED
YOU WILL NO LONGER BE ABLE

1770
01:10:12,508 --> 01:10:14,545
TO DEVELOP THE WEAPONS
TO DEFEAT US.

1771
01:10:14,578 --> 01:10:18,982
Q WILL THEN BE THE MOST POWERFUL
ORGANIZATION IN THE WORLD.

1772
01:10:19,015 --> 01:10:22,585
THE WHOLE OF THE UNITED NATIONS
WILL HAVE TO SUBMIT TO OUR WILL.

1773
01:10:22,618 --> 01:10:24,053
YOU FILTHY TRAITOR.

1774
01:10:24,087 --> 01:10:25,822
THANK YOU,
SAY THAT AGAIN.

1775
01:10:25,855 --> 01:10:27,557
YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO GET AWAY WITH IT, THOUGH.

1776
01:10:27,590 --> 01:10:29,258
MIGHTY JACK WILL STOP YOU.

1777
01:10:29,292 --> 01:10:30,860
YEAH, WHATEVER.

1778
01:10:30,893 --> 01:10:32,730
SO YOU ADMIT
THERE'S A CONNECTION

1779
01:10:32,763 --> 01:10:34,398
BETWEEN MIGHTY JACK
AND YOU.

1780
01:10:34,432 --> 01:10:36,900
- SHE SANG LIKE A BIRD!
- D'OH.

1781
01:10:36,933 --> 01:10:40,337
NO MATTER WHAT THEY TRY,
MIGHTY JACK IS NOW POWERLESS.

1782
01:10:40,370 --> 01:10:41,538
[GASPING]

1783
01:10:41,572 --> 01:10:43,873
NO...
NOTHING WILL HELP THEM.

1784
01:10:43,907 --> 01:10:45,808
OH, WHY DO YOU SAY THAT?

1785
01:10:45,842 --> 01:10:47,510
'CAUSE IT'S MY LINE.

1786
01:10:47,543 --> 01:10:49,447
[MENACING LAUGHING]

1787
01:10:49,480 --> 01:10:50,747
YOU'RE STUCK HERE.

1788
01:10:50,780 --> 01:10:53,483
PEREZ, CONTACT OUR AGENT
RIGHT AWAY.

1789
01:10:53,517 --> 01:10:54,985
GET US OUT OF THIS FILM.

1790
01:10:55,018 --> 01:10:56,820
UM-HMM.

1791
01:10:56,853 --> 01:10:58,288
IT'S WOODY GUTHRIE.

1792
01:10:58,322 --> 01:11:01,192
HEY, MY MOOD RING'S
GOING ALL KOOKY.

1793
01:11:01,225 --> 01:11:03,827
HMM?

1794
01:11:03,860 --> 01:11:05,328
ADAM WEST?

1795
01:11:05,362 --> 01:11:06,830
PETE DUPONT?

1796
01:11:06,863 --> 01:11:08,665
THAT LOOKS LIKE PETE.

1797
01:11:12,435 --> 01:11:13,670
HELLO, FATHER.

1798
01:11:13,703 --> 01:11:14,872
HELLO, MOTHER.

1799
01:11:14,905 --> 01:11:17,140
UH, HERE I AM IN OKINAWA.

1800
01:11:17,173 --> 01:11:18,375
SO YOU WERE THE ONE.

1801
01:11:18,408 --> 01:11:19,777
YES.

1802
01:11:19,810 --> 01:11:22,312
YOU SHOULD HAVE REALIZED
IT LONG AGO.

1803
01:11:22,345 --> 01:11:25,448
I OPENED YOUR SAFE AND GAVE ALL
YOUR RECORDS TO Q.

1804
01:11:25,482 --> 01:11:26,450
- HOW COULD YOU?
- NO.

1805
01:11:26,483 --> 01:11:28,618
ALL MY LIFE'S WORK.

1806
01:11:28,652 --> 01:11:31,122
YOU OF ALL PEOPLE,
MY OWN SON.

1807
01:11:31,155 --> 01:11:33,723
YES, I KNEW YOU'D SAY THAT.

1808
01:11:33,757 --> 01:11:36,793
ALL MY LIFE, YOU COULD ONLY
THINK OF ME AS JAPANESE.

1809
01:11:36,827 --> 01:11:38,262
BUT INSIDE I'M GERMAN.

1810
01:11:38,295 --> 01:11:39,897
KIND OF
LIKE SUSHI STROGANOFF.

1811
01:11:39,930 --> 01:11:41,832
HOW MUCH DID THEY GIVE
YOU TO BETRAY ME

1812
01:11:41,865 --> 01:11:43,600
AND WORK
WITH THOSE MONSTERS?

1813
01:11:43,633 --> 01:11:44,768
YOU'VE NEVER ACKNOWLEDGED...

1814
01:11:44,802 --> 01:11:46,670
NOW HE LOOKS LIKE RODDY
MCDOWALL.

1815
01:11:46,703 --> 01:11:47,670
I DON'T GET IT.

1816
01:11:47,703 --> 01:11:50,673
ALL THOSE YEARS,
YOU TOOK THE CREDIT.

1817
01:11:50,707 --> 01:11:53,277
ONLY NOW THINGS WILL BE
DIFFERENT.

1818
01:11:53,310 --> 01:11:54,878
I'LL HAVE
MY OWN LABORATORY.

1819
01:11:54,912 --> 01:11:57,513
WITH Q I HAVE A
GREAT FUTURE.

1820
01:11:57,547 --> 01:11:58,815
MY OWN ROOM AND
MY OWN PHONE, TOO.

1821
01:11:58,848 --> 01:12:00,283
YOUR FUTURE FOR STEALING
ANOTHER MAN'S IDEAS.

1822
01:12:00,317 --> 01:12:01,285
OOH.

1823
01:12:01,318 --> 01:12:03,587
BETRAYING YOUR FATHER

1824
01:12:03,620 --> 01:12:05,255
BY DEALING WITH MURDERERS?

1825
01:12:05,288 --> 01:12:07,557
- YES.
- YES.

1826
01:12:07,590 --> 01:12:09,960
YOUR IDEAS AND ETHICS
ARE TOO ANTIQUATED

1827
01:12:09,993 --> 01:12:12,095
FOR YOU TO UNDERSTAND
WHAT WE ARE CREATING.

1828
01:12:12,128 --> 01:12:13,863
LOOK AT MY WARTS,
I HAVE TO BE EVIL.

1829
01:12:13,897 --> 01:12:15,965
WE WILL
CONQUER THE WHOLE WORLD.

1830
01:12:15,998 --> 01:12:17,467
WELL, IT'S GOOD
TO HAVE GOALS.

1831
01:12:17,500 --> 01:12:18,435
FRITZ.

1832
01:12:19,603 --> 01:12:20,570
THE WICKER MAN?

1833
01:12:20,603 --> 01:12:21,638
NOW THEY'RE IN IRELAND.

1834
01:12:21,672 --> 01:12:23,573
WHY DID WE COME HERE?

1835
01:12:23,607 --> 01:12:25,675
I HAVE PROOF THAT DR. TAKEBANA
WAS WORKING FOR Q.

1836
01:12:25,708 --> 01:12:26,743
[GASPING]

1837
01:12:26,777 --> 01:12:28,778
I'M GOING TO CHECK OUT HIS
APARTMENT.

1838
01:12:28,812 --> 01:12:30,180
YOU STAY AS LOOKOUT.

1839
01:12:30,213 --> 01:12:31,482
CAN I GO WITH YOU?

1840
01:12:31,515 --> 01:12:32,482
YOU STAY HERE.

1841
01:12:32,515 --> 01:12:33,483
OH, NO!

1842
01:12:33,517 --> 01:12:34,718
WE CAN'T STAY HERE,
WE GOTTA GO.

1843
01:12:34,752 --> 01:12:35,885
WE GO.

1844
01:12:35,918 --> 01:12:37,420
YOU STAY HERE,
WE'LL GO.

1845
01:12:37,453 --> 01:12:41,158
COME ALONG.

1846
01:12:41,192 --> 01:12:44,293
[GATES CLOSING]

1847
01:12:48,932 --> 01:12:51,768
HELP, HELP,
CROW'S FLOODED THE SHIP!

1848
01:12:51,802 --> 01:12:53,270
WE'RE ALL GONNA DIE!

1849
01:12:53,303 --> 01:12:54,572
A FIRE BALL!

1850
01:12:54,605 --> 01:12:56,207
JOEL, COME ON, YOU'RE NOT
FOOLING ANYBODY.

1851
01:12:56,240 --> 01:12:58,042
THAT'S AN AQUARIUM WE PUT IN
FRONT OF CAMBOT

1852
01:12:58,075 --> 01:12:59,175
THAT'S CAUSING
THIS EFFECT HERE.

1853
01:12:59,208 --> 01:13:00,710
I KNOW, I KNOW, I WAS JUST
GETTING READY

1854
01:13:00,743 --> 01:13:02,078
TO DO A BIG PITCH
TO HOLLYWOOD.

1855
01:13:02,112 --> 01:13:05,515
YOU KNOW, WE GOT TONS OF OFFERS
FROM INTERESTED EXECUTIVES

1856
01:13:05,548 --> 01:13:08,185
AFTER CROW READ HIS PIECE IN
READER'S THEATER

1857
01:13:08,218 --> 01:13:09,520
CALLED "EARTH VERSUS SOUP."

1858
01:13:09,553 --> 01:13:11,388
YUP, UH, NOW I'VE GOT A
DEVELOPMENT DEAL

1859
01:13:11,422 --> 01:13:13,657
WITH ANSON WILLIAMS
ENCHANTMENT PRODUCTIONS.

1860
01:13:13,690 --> 01:13:16,293
AND PLUS, I'M DOING A REWRITE
ON "NEXT OF KIN TWO."

1861
01:13:16,327 --> 01:13:19,062
YEAH, SO I THOUGHT WE COULD DO
THE PITCH UNDERWATER, YOU KNOW.

1862
01:13:19,095 --> 01:13:21,765
LIKE CASH IN ON SOME OF THE
EXCITEMENT THAT'S BEEN GENERATED

1863
01:13:21,798 --> 01:13:25,468
FROM MOVIES LIKE "THE DEEP" AND
"THE ABYSS" AND OTHERS.

1864
01:13:25,502 --> 01:13:26,937
WOW, THAT'S A
GREAT IDEA, JOEL.

1865
01:13:26,970 --> 01:13:28,938
AS A MATTER OF FACT, I WAS JUST
WATCHING "MIGHTY JACK,"

1866
01:13:28,972 --> 01:13:31,542
AND I COULDN'T HELP BUT THINK
THIS WOULD MAKE A GREAT MOVIE.

1867
01:13:31,575 --> 01:13:33,743
RIGHT, YEAH, OKAY.

1868
01:13:33,777 --> 01:13:35,478
I WAS THINKING
SOMETHING LIKE START IT OFF

1869
01:13:35,512 --> 01:13:37,013
WITH A SUBMARINE,
LIKE:

1870
01:13:37,047 --> 01:13:39,315
[MIMICKING SONAR PING]

1871
01:13:39,348 --> 01:13:41,852
GRAY LADY, DOWN!
GRAY LADY, DOWN!

1872
01:13:41,885 --> 01:13:44,922
I CAN'T SEE 'EM, THEY GOT A
CATERPILLAR HERE, SIR.

1873
01:13:44,955 --> 01:13:46,157
NICE, JOEL, THAT'S NICE.

1874
01:13:46,190 --> 01:13:48,125
HA-HA, GREAT, JOEL.

1875
01:13:48,158 --> 01:13:49,893
THE MAN SHOULD BE IN A
STRAITJACKET.

1876
01:13:49,927 --> 01:13:50,927
NOAH'S FLOATING.

1877
01:13:50,960 --> 01:13:53,263
HERE COME THE ANIMALS,
TWO BY TWO.

1878
01:13:53,297 --> 01:13:55,465
WHOA, WHAT DOES NOAH HAVE TO DO
WITH ANYTHING HERE, JOEL?

1879
01:13:55,498 --> 01:13:57,300
IT'S THE
ARK OF THE STORY.

1880
01:13:57,333 --> 01:13:58,535
THAT'S IT, THAT'S IT.

1881
01:13:58,568 --> 01:13:59,770
GO TEAR HIS ARM OFF.

1882
01:13:59,803 --> 01:14:02,072
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE,
WHAT ARE YOU TRYING TO DO?

1883
01:14:02,105 --> 01:14:03,307
UH, I WAS GONNA TEAR
YOUR ARM OFF.

1884
01:14:03,340 --> 01:14:04,675
OH, COME ON.

1885
01:14:04,708 --> 01:14:08,212
ANYWAY, THE REALLY GOOD THING IS
THAT STEVEN SPIELBERG

1886
01:14:08,245 --> 01:14:11,080
IS NOW DOING A BUNCH OF MOVIES
BASED ON CARTOON CHARACTERS.

1887
01:14:11,113 --> 01:14:14,183
YOU KNOW, LIKE "THE FLINTSTONES"
AND "BLOOM COUNTY."

1888
01:14:14,217 --> 01:14:16,453
AND, UH...
JUST GOES ON LIKE THAT.

1889
01:14:16,487 --> 01:14:17,453
YEAH, WHAT'S HE
GONNA DO NEXT?

1890
01:14:17,487 --> 01:14:18,822
CASPER, THE FRIENDLY GHOST?

1891
01:14:18,855 --> 01:14:19,823
OH, THAT'D BE RIDICULOUS.

1892
01:14:19,857 --> 01:14:20,823
YOU KNOW,
AND I WAS THINKING

1893
01:14:20,857 --> 01:14:22,192
IT'D BE A GREAT
TIME TO BRING

1894
01:14:22,225 --> 01:14:24,928
EVEN MORE CARTOON CHARACTERS TO
THE BIG SCREEN, YOU KNOW.

1895
01:14:24,962 --> 01:14:27,898
- LIKE, DEPUTY DOG.
- THAT'S DROOPY.

1896
01:14:27,932 --> 01:14:30,400
AND, UH, ODIE COLOGNIE.

1897
01:14:30,433 --> 01:14:31,568
AND JOSIE AND THE PUSSYCATS.

1898
01:14:31,602 --> 01:14:33,337
I CAN'T STAND TO SEE HIM
LIKE THIS, CROW.

1899
01:14:33,370 --> 01:14:37,007
NO, I CAN'T EITHER.

1900
01:14:37,040 --> 01:14:38,942
HEY, YOU GUYS, COME BACK.

1901
01:14:38,975 --> 01:14:41,212
I CAN BE NUTTY JUST LIKE
THE REST OF YOU

1902
01:14:41,245 --> 01:14:43,747
AND DO DUMB PUNS
AND STUFF LIKE THAT.

1903
01:14:43,780 --> 01:14:45,715
THERE'S NO REASON
WHY I CAN'T.

1904
01:14:45,748 --> 01:14:50,887
I'M-- YOU KNOW, I'M WEIRD AND
THAT RESULTS IN CREATIVITY.

1905
01:14:50,920 --> 01:14:52,488
WELL, SPEAKING OF
THE NUTTY,

1906
01:14:52,522 --> 01:14:55,625
HERE'S A WORD FROM OUR FRIENDS
AT SHAKE-A-PUDDING.

1907
01:14:55,658 --> 01:15:03,767
♪♪

1908
01:15:03,800 --> 01:15:07,703
I THOUGHT IT WAS A PRETTY GOOD
IDEA, ACTUALLY.

1909
01:15:07,737 --> 01:15:09,840
OH, IT'S SINATRA, HE'S GOING
RIGHT FOR THE SCOTCH.

1910
01:15:09,873 --> 01:15:12,642
YEAH, WOULDN'T YOU KNOW IT.

1911
01:15:12,675 --> 01:15:14,645
SHE'S GOT JUDY CARNE HAIR,
THERE.

1912
01:15:19,415 --> 01:15:20,383
MARY?

1913
01:15:20,417 --> 01:15:26,857
- TYLER?
- MOORE?

1914
01:15:26,890 --> 01:15:28,458
ALL RIGHT IN THE BOX?

1915
01:15:28,492 --> 01:15:30,060
IT'S OKAY.

1916
01:15:30,093 --> 01:15:31,395
OH, IT'S A ROCK TUMBLER.

1917
01:15:31,428 --> 01:15:32,762
THIS SHOULD PAD OUT
THE FILM A LITTLE.

1918
01:15:32,795 --> 01:15:34,097
- OH, NO.
- YEP.

1919
01:15:34,130 --> 01:15:35,465
A NICE LITTLE TOY.

1920
01:15:35,498 --> 01:15:37,700
A PORTABLE SYNCHROTON UNIT.

1921
01:15:37,733 --> 01:15:39,568
OH, YOU MADE THAT UP.

1922
01:15:39,602 --> 01:15:43,040
DR. TAKEBANA CHANGES WATER
TO ICE INSTANTLY

1923
01:15:43,073 --> 01:15:45,708
BY ACCELERATING
THEIR MOLECULES.

1924
01:15:45,742 --> 01:15:48,312
YOU ACCELERATE MY
MOLECULES, DOCTOR.

1925
01:15:48,345 --> 01:15:52,148
ANYONE HAS THE POWER TO ALTER
MOLECULAR STRUCTURE ANYWHERE.

1926
01:15:52,182 --> 01:15:54,652
AND THEY USUALLY DO.

1927
01:15:54,685 --> 01:15:56,353
AND YOU CAN EVEN MAKE ICE
BULLETS?

1928
01:15:56,387 --> 01:15:57,487
YES.

1929
01:15:57,520 --> 01:15:59,723
OH.

1930
01:15:59,757 --> 01:16:02,292
[LAUGHING]
YOU THINK THAT'S FUNNY?

1931
01:16:05,662 --> 01:16:06,763
IT'S FRITZ.

1932
01:16:06,797 --> 01:16:09,132
YOU CAN TELL BY HIS BLINKING
PINKY RING.

1933
01:16:09,165 --> 01:16:14,003
HMM.

1934
01:16:14,037 --> 01:16:15,272
OH!

1935
01:16:15,305 --> 01:16:16,272
- OOH.
- OUCH.

1936
01:16:16,305 --> 01:16:17,507
TAKEDOWN, TWO POINTS.

1937
01:16:17,540 --> 01:16:18,942
[GRUNTING]

1938
01:16:18,975 --> 01:16:21,912
OH, LOOK AT THAT REVERSAL,
ANOTHER TWO POINTS.

1939
01:16:21,945 --> 01:16:23,747
YOU TWO WANT SOME GUM?

1940
01:16:23,780 --> 01:16:26,048
IT'S A LADY SUNBEAM.

1941
01:16:26,082 --> 01:16:29,418
[BEEPING]

1942
01:16:29,452 --> 01:16:30,420
THAT'S MARY'S SIGNAL.

1943
01:16:30,453 --> 01:16:32,855
JUST WHAT I'VE BEEN
WAITING FOR.

1944
01:16:32,888 --> 01:16:34,157
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1945
01:16:34,190 --> 01:16:35,692
I ASSUMED Q WAS
CLEVER ENOUGH

1946
01:16:35,725 --> 01:16:37,160
TO DETECT
IF ANYONE WAS ACTING.

1947
01:16:37,193 --> 01:16:39,628
- OH, NO DANGER OF THAT.
- MARY DOESN'T KNOW WHO
THEIR AGENT IS.

1948
01:16:39,662 --> 01:16:40,797
OH, YOU LIKE
LIVING DANGEROUSLY?

1949
01:16:40,830 --> 01:16:42,732
- LET'S GO, DOCTOR.
- LET'S PLAY DOCTOR.

1950
01:16:42,765 --> 01:16:44,367
[CHUCKLING]

1951
01:16:44,400 --> 01:16:46,737
ANYTIME DADDY-O.

1952
01:16:46,770 --> 01:16:48,305
[TOM IMITATING MUSIC]

1953
01:16:48,338 --> 01:16:52,142
SEE IF YOU CAN GET RUSH
LIMBAUGH.

1954
01:16:52,175 --> 01:16:54,077
YEAH, THAT'S HIM.

1955
01:16:54,110 --> 01:16:55,912
CAN'T GET RID OF IT.

1956
01:16:55,945 --> 01:16:58,615
GET RID OF IT, DEAR GOD,
IT'S ON EVERY STATION!

1957
01:16:58,648 --> 01:17:01,283
GET RID OF IT!

1958
01:17:01,317 --> 01:17:02,385
WHOA.

1959
01:17:02,418 --> 01:17:04,587
WE'RE ON THE WRONG
SIDE OF THE STREET.

1960
01:17:04,620 --> 01:17:07,023
- MAJOR, I'M SO GLAD TO SEE YOU.
- IT'S JAPAN.
- WHERE'D THEY GO?

1961
01:17:07,057 --> 01:17:09,358
I'M NOT SURE ABOUT
DR. TAKEBANA.

1962
01:17:09,392 --> 01:17:11,928
ROBERTO TRIED TO STOP
FRITZ BUT HE GOT AWAY.

1963
01:17:11,962 --> 01:17:13,630
HE MADE OFF WITH THE
PORTABLE SYNCHROTON.

1964
01:17:13,663 --> 01:17:14,663
SYNCHROTRON?

1965
01:17:14,697 --> 01:17:15,998
- YES.
- SOUNDS LIKE A SOAP OPERA.

1966
01:17:16,032 --> 01:17:20,970
[PHONE RINGING]

1967
01:17:21,003 --> 01:17:23,440
FOLKS, IT'S JUST A PHONE.

1968
01:17:23,473 --> 01:17:24,808
- OOH.
- PICK IT UP.

1969
01:17:24,842 --> 01:17:26,510
HEY, COME ON, IT'S MY
DAD FROM FLORIDA.

1970
01:17:26,543 --> 01:17:30,113
SHUT UP, SVEN, COME ON!

1971
01:17:30,147 --> 01:17:31,582
- BE COOL.
- DR. FRITZ?

1972
01:17:31,615 --> 01:17:32,748
JA.

1973
01:17:32,782 --> 01:17:34,683
WE'LL GO AHEAD AS PLANNED.

1974
01:17:34,717 --> 01:17:37,587
THE SHIP IS WAITING AT THE
SHUBARO MARU DOCK.

1975
01:17:37,620 --> 01:17:39,957
THE SHEEP? THERE'S A SHEEP
WAITING FOR THEM?

1976
01:17:39,990 --> 01:17:40,957
JA.

1977
01:17:40,990 --> 01:17:45,062
JA, JAWOHL, MEIN KAMPF,
ALL THAT STUFF.

1978
01:17:45,095 --> 01:17:46,128
Q MUST BE TRYING TO HELP

1979
01:17:46,162 --> 01:17:48,098
DR. TAKEBANA
AND HIS SON ESCAPE.

1980
01:17:48,132 --> 01:17:49,432
IS THAT PART OF THE PLOT?

1981
01:17:49,465 --> 01:17:50,400
BETTER CALL FOR A BACKUP.

1982
01:17:50,433 --> 01:17:51,368
YES, SIR.

1983
01:17:56,172 --> 01:17:59,375
[HUMMING]

1984
01:17:59,408 --> 01:18:01,612
THE MAN THAT WE'RE
WAITING FOR.

1985
01:18:01,645 --> 01:18:05,415
WE'RE JUST
WAITING FOR A TABLE.

1986
01:18:05,448 --> 01:18:06,683
WELL...

1987
01:18:06,717 --> 01:18:10,820
SO JUST PLUMB RAN OUT OF THINGS
TO SAY HERE, HUH?

1988
01:18:10,853 --> 01:18:12,855
SENORITA,
YOU'RE COMING WITH US.

1989
01:18:12,888 --> 01:18:16,893
HE ASKED ME, HE ASKED ME,
TODAY MY DREAMS COME TRUE.

1990
01:18:16,927 --> 01:18:20,863
AND MAKE SURE THAT DR. TAKEBANA
DOESN'T COMMIT SUICIDE.

1991
01:18:20,897 --> 01:18:24,500
YEAH, HE'S ALWAYS PULLING THAT.

1992
01:18:24,533 --> 01:18:25,735
PAPA.

1993
01:18:25,768 --> 01:18:28,505
OH, GOOD, A FAMILIAR FACE,
ADAM WEST IS BACK.

1994
01:18:28,538 --> 01:18:32,108
DON'T GO AWAY,
I'LL COME RIGHT BACK.

1995
01:18:32,142 --> 01:18:34,377
PLEASE, DON'T YOU
TRY ANYTHING.

1996
01:18:34,410 --> 01:18:39,015
DON'T TOUCH THAT DIAL.

1997
01:18:39,048 --> 01:18:43,187
♪♪

1998
01:18:43,220 --> 01:18:45,488
OH.

1999
01:18:45,522 --> 01:18:49,592
- [TIRES SKIDDING]
- [CROW MAKING ENGINE NOISES]

2000
01:18:49,625 --> 01:18:53,997
OH, IT'S LIKE "WHAT'S UP, DOC"
ALL OF A SUDDEN.

2001
01:18:54,030 --> 01:18:58,168
COME ON, PUNCH IT, HAL,
I WANNA DIE WITH YOU.

2002
01:18:58,202 --> 01:18:59,903
OH, CHINESE FIRE DRILL.

2003
01:18:59,937 --> 01:19:01,170
YOU MEAN JAPANESE...

2004
01:19:01,203 --> 01:19:05,042
OH, RIGHT, RIGHT.

2005
01:19:05,075 --> 01:19:07,443
OH, THEY'RE GONNA MAKE BALLOONS.

2006
01:19:07,477 --> 01:19:08,478
THE SHIP'S DOWN THERE.

2007
01:19:08,512 --> 01:19:09,645
YOU COVER THE OTHER SIDE.

2008
01:19:09,678 --> 01:19:14,818
- I'LL COVER THE WATERFRONT.
- [HUMMING]

2009
01:19:14,852 --> 01:19:16,418
[ALARM SOUNDING]

2010
01:19:16,452 --> 01:19:17,920
WHO'S WHOOPING?

2011
01:19:17,953 --> 01:19:19,555
JUST ANOTHER FEW MINUTES.

2012
01:19:19,588 --> 01:19:20,623
I'M SURE FRITZ WILL SHOW UP.

2013
01:19:20,657 --> 01:19:22,392
YES.

2014
01:19:22,425 --> 01:19:23,393
ROBERTO...

2015
01:19:23,427 --> 01:19:24,727
CLEMENTE.

2016
01:19:24,760 --> 01:19:26,863
IT'S STRANGE YOU ONLY
MENTION FRITZ.

2017
01:19:26,897 --> 01:19:28,765
YOU SHOULD'VE SAID DR.
TAKEBANA AND FRITZ.

2018
01:19:28,798 --> 01:19:31,935
OOH!

2019
01:19:31,968 --> 01:19:33,870
IT'S NOT TRUE.

2020
01:19:33,903 --> 01:19:36,005
ALL RIGHT, MR. Q.

2021
01:19:36,038 --> 01:19:38,875
I THINK YOU BETTER
START TALKING.

2022
01:19:38,908 --> 01:19:41,578
I WAS BORN IN THE HOUSE MY
FATHER BUILT.

2023
01:19:41,612 --> 01:19:43,145
IF DR. TAKEBANA
ISN'T A Q AGENT,

2024
01:19:43,178 --> 01:19:44,948
WHY DID YOU LEAD US OUT
HERE LIKE THIS?

2025
01:19:44,982 --> 01:19:46,783
UH-OH.

2026
01:19:46,817 --> 01:19:48,485
LOOK!

2027
01:19:48,518 --> 01:19:49,552
- NO, YOU DON'T!
- I DON'T BELIEVE

2028
01:19:49,585 --> 01:19:54,157
- HE FELL FOR THAT.
- UNBELIEVABLE.

2029
01:19:54,190 --> 01:19:56,760
HE WAS ONLY STALLING US TO GIVE
THEM TIME TO GET AWAY.

2030
01:19:56,793 --> 01:19:58,862
HE'LL KILL CATHERINE.

2031
01:19:58,895 --> 01:19:59,863
[GUNFIRE]

2032
01:19:59,897 --> 01:20:03,367
THEY HATE THESE CANS!

2033
01:20:03,400 --> 01:20:07,670
HELL, THESE LUDLUM
NOVELS ARE-- HUH?

2034
01:20:07,703 --> 01:20:12,908
ALL RIGHT, GET INSIDE,
COME ON.

2035
01:20:12,942 --> 01:20:14,243
MIGHTY JACK.

2036
01:20:14,277 --> 01:20:15,612
MIGHTY JACK!

2037
01:20:15,645 --> 01:20:18,482
THE DOOR WILL ONLY OPEN FOR
11 PRE-REGISTERED VOICES.

2038
01:20:18,515 --> 01:20:20,317
"OCEAN'S ELEVEN."

2039
01:20:20,350 --> 01:20:22,385
I'M NOT ONE OF THEM.

2040
01:20:22,418 --> 01:20:23,687
BRING HER HERE.

2041
01:20:23,720 --> 01:20:25,788
OH.

2042
01:20:25,822 --> 01:20:29,658
TRY SWORDFISH.

2043
01:20:29,692 --> 01:20:31,695
WELL, THEN...

2044
01:20:31,728 --> 01:20:34,563
I'M GOING TO CHANGE
YOUR SPARK PLUGS.

2045
01:20:34,597 --> 01:20:37,200
THAT WILL MAKE HER TALK.

2046
01:20:37,233 --> 01:20:40,103
I DON'T THINK SHOOTING ME IS
GOING TO HELP.

2047
01:20:40,137 --> 01:20:41,537
YOU ARE RIGHT.

2048
01:20:41,570 --> 01:20:44,873
BUT NOW WE'LL GET A CHANCE TO
SEE HOW GOOD THIS GADGET IS.

2049
01:20:44,907 --> 01:20:51,180
WE'RE GOING TO MAKE
MONSTER BUBBLES.

2050
01:20:51,213 --> 01:20:54,483
GEE, NO, OH!

2051
01:20:54,517 --> 01:20:56,887
MAJOR NELSON SNOWED ON HER.

2052
01:20:56,920 --> 01:20:59,022
THERE YOU SEE, IT FLOCKS EVENLY
WITH NO MESS.

2053
01:20:59,055 --> 01:21:04,627
HAVE A CHRISTMAS TREE,
THIS'LL DO THE TRICK.

2054
01:21:04,660 --> 01:21:07,130
♪ DAH-DAH-DUM ♪

2055
01:21:07,163 --> 01:21:10,000
ROBERT LUDLUM WILL BE BACK IN
THE UVULA SCENARIO.

2056
01:21:10,033 --> 01:21:11,702
DON'T SHOOT HER.

2057
01:21:11,735 --> 01:21:14,403
IT'S NO USE, WE'RE LOST.

2058
01:21:14,437 --> 01:21:15,572
Q IS TOO STRONG.

2059
01:21:15,605 --> 01:21:17,507
THERE'S NOTHING WE CAN DO TO
STOP THEM.

2060
01:21:17,540 --> 01:21:19,208
[MENACING CHUCKLE]

2061
01:21:19,242 --> 01:21:21,177
GO ON!

2062
01:21:21,210 --> 01:21:24,613
OH, FITTING ROOM NUMBER
FOUR IS OPEN, SIR.

2063
01:21:24,647 --> 01:21:27,417
HEY, THERE'S A RULE, ONE
PERSON PER FITTING ROOM.

2064
01:21:27,450 --> 01:21:29,052
THIS IS QUITE AN
INSTALLATION HERE.

2065
01:21:29,085 --> 01:21:30,853
YES, RICK, IT IS.

2066
01:21:30,887 --> 01:21:33,255
[GUNFIRE]

2067
01:21:33,288 --> 01:21:35,392
UH, GIVE ME A SANDWICH,
WOULD YOU?

2068
01:21:35,425 --> 01:21:36,392
WOULD YOU GET TO THE PIER?

2069
01:21:36,425 --> 01:21:37,393
YES, SIR.

2070
01:21:37,427 --> 01:21:38,628
NO, I'LL GO INSTEAD.

2071
01:21:38,662 --> 01:21:39,862
- HURRY!
- YEAH, HAM ON RYE

2072
01:21:39,895 --> 01:21:40,863
AND TAKE OFF THE ANISE SEEDS,

2073
01:21:40,897 --> 01:21:43,065
I HATE THOSE, OKAY? THANKS.

2074
01:21:43,098 --> 01:21:46,468
- [WATER SPLASHING]
- OH, SHE'S GOING TO
THE AQUA DELI.

2075
01:21:46,502 --> 01:21:49,272
SCARF THEATER WILL BE BACK
RIGHT AFTER THIS.

2076
01:21:49,305 --> 01:21:53,977
OKAY.

2077
01:21:54,010 --> 01:21:56,078
IT'S THE RIGHTEOUS BROTHERS.

2078
01:21:56,112 --> 01:21:59,848
- ♪ YOU'VE LOST THAT... ♪
- ♪ SYNCHROCYLOTRON ♪

2079
01:21:59,882 --> 01:22:02,018
OH, GOT A BAD CLAM, HUH?

2080
01:22:02,052 --> 01:22:08,758
[MUFFLED GROANING]

2081
01:22:08,792 --> 01:22:13,228
OH, NOT THAT OLD GAG.

2082
01:22:13,262 --> 01:22:14,197
COME ON.

2083
01:22:16,967 --> 01:22:17,900
MOVE.

2084
01:22:17,933 --> 01:22:20,237
- GO ON.
- NO TRICKS.

2085
01:22:20,270 --> 01:22:22,872
[GRUNTING]

2086
01:22:22,905 --> 01:22:25,842
OOH, SAMSONITE LUGGAGE.

2087
01:22:25,875 --> 01:22:27,143
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE.

2088
01:22:27,177 --> 01:22:28,612
WAIT.

2089
01:22:28,645 --> 01:22:31,080
- HMM? WHAT?
- OKAY.

2090
01:22:31,113 --> 01:22:34,050
OH, THE PLOT WAS MOVING A LITTLE
TOO FAST FOR HIS LIKING.

2091
01:22:34,083 --> 01:22:37,787
♪♪

2092
01:22:40,523 --> 01:22:42,458
WELL, THEN.

2093
01:22:42,492 --> 01:22:43,793
IT'S A PINEAPPLE ROASTER.

2094
01:22:43,827 --> 01:22:46,495
WATCH US ROAST YOUR PINEAPPLE
SLICE, YOU PICK IT.

2095
01:22:46,528 --> 01:22:48,432
PINEAPPLE ROASTER?

2096
01:22:48,465 --> 01:22:50,533
I LOVE IT.

2097
01:22:50,567 --> 01:22:52,268
THAT'S FUNNY, YOU
GOTTA ADMIT,

2098
01:22:52,302 --> 01:22:57,507
ROASTED PINEAPPLE
SLICES, IT'S NEAT.

2099
01:22:57,540 --> 01:23:01,110
OKAY, COME.

2100
01:23:01,143 --> 01:23:02,678
HOLD IT.

2101
01:23:02,712 --> 01:23:04,480
NOW HOLD IT UP TO
THE LIGHTS.

2102
01:23:06,715 --> 01:23:09,685
OH, THAT'S BETTER, WE'RE IN A
COMPLETELY DIFFERENT FILM NOW.

2103
01:23:13,122 --> 01:23:15,023
[HUMMING]

2104
01:23:15,057 --> 01:23:19,195
AND WE CALL IT THE
POSTAGE METER.

2105
01:23:19,228 --> 01:23:22,498
WE WILL SURPRISE
THEM, COME ON.

2106
01:23:22,532 --> 01:23:25,768
- HAVING FUN?
- SURPRISE!

2107
01:23:25,802 --> 01:23:26,770
[LAUGHING]

2108
01:23:26,803 --> 01:23:28,303
NOW!

2109
01:23:28,337 --> 01:23:31,673
[GUNFIRE]
AH, WE SHOULDN'T HAVE TAKEN
THE TIME TO LAUGH.

2110
01:23:35,378 --> 01:23:41,150
THIS THING IS GREAT.

2111
01:23:41,183 --> 01:23:44,853
OOH.

2112
01:23:44,887 --> 01:23:47,590
WILLIAM FAULKNER GRABS
THE PACKAGE.

2113
01:23:51,995 --> 01:23:53,863
OOH.

2114
01:23:53,897 --> 01:23:57,100
DARN.

2115
01:23:57,133 --> 01:23:59,202
YOU, STUNT LEFT,
YOU, SLANT DEEP.

2116
01:23:59,235 --> 01:24:00,837
YOU, WRITE "SOUND
AND THE FURY."

2117
01:24:00,870 --> 01:24:05,442
LET'S GO.

2118
01:24:05,475 --> 01:24:07,443
YEAH, YOU GOT HOLES
IN YOUR GUN!

2119
01:24:07,477 --> 01:24:09,512
YEAH, WELL, YOU GOT PEANUT
BUTTER IN MY CHOCOLATE.

2120
01:24:09,545 --> 01:24:10,613
YEAH, BUT T-- HMM?

2121
01:24:10,647 --> 01:24:14,283
[WATER RUNNING]

2122
01:24:14,317 --> 01:24:16,252
- PEW PEW.
- DROP IT!

2123
01:24:16,285 --> 01:24:19,055
[ALL]
DA-DOH, DA-DOH.

2124
01:24:21,690 --> 01:24:24,393
- COME ON.
- I'M SHOT.

2125
01:24:24,427 --> 01:24:26,528
COME ON, COME ON.

2126
01:24:26,562 --> 01:24:27,863
OOH.

2127
01:24:27,897 --> 01:24:30,867
ALL RIGHT, NOW, YOU, SLOW DANCE
AND DON'T TRY TO LEAD.

2128
01:24:30,900 --> 01:24:32,902
- I GOT A GUN.
- [JOEL LAUGHS]

2129
01:24:32,935 --> 01:24:34,837
IT'S THE YANCY STREET GANG.

2130
01:24:34,870 --> 01:24:36,505
HASTA LA VISTA, BABY.

2131
01:24:36,538 --> 01:24:40,610
I MAY BE GERMAN BUT I'M FAST.
[LAUGHING]

2132
01:24:40,643 --> 01:24:44,147
DON'T MOVE!

2133
01:24:44,180 --> 01:24:46,917
OH, NO WAY OUT.

2134
01:24:46,950 --> 01:24:49,785
[ALL]
HEY, FRITZ... OH, COME ON,
WHAT--

2135
01:24:49,818 --> 01:24:50,787
[EXPLOSION]

2136
01:24:50,820 --> 01:24:52,055
- OOH!
- NO.

2137
01:24:52,088 --> 01:24:53,055
- BOY.
- FRITZ.

2138
01:24:53,088 --> 01:24:55,358
HE DIED AS HE LIVED.

2139
01:24:55,392 --> 01:24:57,260
LOVING HIS WORK.

2140
01:24:58,227 --> 01:25:01,965
♪♪

2141
01:25:03,800 --> 01:25:05,033
♪♪

2142
01:25:05,067 --> 01:25:11,540
IT'S DISNEYLAND TOKYO.

2143
01:25:11,573 --> 01:25:15,212
- AH, HERE WE ARE AT
PLOT RECOVERY.
- [JOEL IMITATING VENTILATOR]

2144
01:25:15,245 --> 01:25:18,815
- ALL RIGHT.
- [VENTILATOR NOISES CONTINUE]

2145
01:25:18,848 --> 01:25:20,850
EVERYBODY GET IN THE SHOT,
COME ON, STAY ON CAMERA.

2146
01:25:20,883 --> 01:25:21,852
HOW ARE YOU?

2147
01:25:21,885 --> 01:25:24,220
A LITTLE WEAK.

2148
01:25:24,253 --> 01:25:25,755
Q IS GOING TO...

2149
01:25:25,788 --> 01:25:27,523
- WHAT ABOUT Q?
- YES?

2150
01:25:27,557 --> 01:25:30,693
THEY'RE GOING TO DESTROY THE
ISLAND IN AMORI BAY.

2151
01:25:30,727 --> 01:25:32,462
WITH THE FREEZING PROCESS?

2152
01:25:32,495 --> 01:25:33,830
YES.

2153
01:25:33,863 --> 01:25:35,698
I OVERHEARD ROBERTO
GIVE THE ORDER.

2154
01:25:35,732 --> 01:25:38,033
IT WAS FOR TODAY.

2155
01:25:38,067 --> 01:25:39,168
- YOU MUST HURRY, SIR.
- DON'T TOUCH ME.

2156
01:25:39,202 --> 01:25:40,168
LET GO OF ME.

2157
01:25:40,202 --> 01:25:41,737
YOU MUST HURRY.

2158
01:25:41,770 --> 01:25:44,040
YOU MUST SINK THE BISMARCK.

2159
01:25:44,073 --> 01:25:45,942
GET BACK TO MIGHTY JACK,
FULL SCALE ALERT.

2160
01:25:45,975 --> 01:25:47,177
- YES, SIR.
- COMBAT STATIONS.

2161
01:25:47,210 --> 01:25:48,177
YES, SIR.

2162
01:25:48,210 --> 01:25:50,713
♪♪

2163
01:25:50,747 --> 01:25:53,617
AGAIN WITH THE BANK TURN.
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

2164
01:25:53,650 --> 01:25:54,617
INCREASE SPEED.

2165
01:25:54,650 --> 01:25:56,218
BUT I'LL GET CAR SICK.

2166
01:25:56,252 --> 01:25:58,087
INCREASE SPEED.

2167
01:25:58,120 --> 01:25:59,422
NUCLEAR ROCKETS.

2168
01:25:59,455 --> 01:26:02,092
READY TO FIRE.

2169
01:26:02,125 --> 01:26:03,192
ENGINE ROOM.

2170
01:26:03,225 --> 01:26:07,163
GAUGE INDICATES
TEMPERATURE'S RISING.

2171
01:26:07,197 --> 01:26:09,765
- PINEAPPLE'S UP.
- HMM?

2172
01:26:09,798 --> 01:26:12,635
FROST 'EM.

2173
01:26:12,668 --> 01:26:13,770
MAKE 'EM ICY.

2174
01:26:13,803 --> 01:26:16,538
OH, MASTER, READY TO ENGAGE
MIGHTY JACK.

2175
01:26:16,572 --> 01:26:17,873
AM I STILL IN THIS FILM?

2176
01:26:17,907 --> 01:26:19,542
[CROW MEOWS]
AT LAST.

2177
01:26:19,575 --> 01:26:22,345
COOLANT NOT REACTING,
TEMPERATURE RISING.

2178
01:26:22,378 --> 01:26:25,047
- MOJO RISING.
- INCREASE SPEED.

2179
01:26:25,080 --> 01:26:28,050
THE ICEBERG,
Q'S HEADQUARTERS.

2180
01:26:28,083 --> 01:26:29,552
MAJOR, LET'S HIT
THEM RIGHT NOW.

2181
01:26:29,585 --> 01:26:31,220
WE'LL NEVER HAVE A
BETTER CHANCE THAN THIS.

2182
01:26:31,253 --> 01:26:32,555
YEAH.

2183
01:26:32,588 --> 01:26:33,890
- GET READY TO FIRE.
- RIGHT.

2184
01:26:33,923 --> 01:26:34,923
[WHISTLING SOUND]
HUH?

2185
01:26:34,957 --> 01:26:36,858
UH-OH.

2186
01:26:36,892 --> 01:26:38,962
FRIES ARE UP.

2187
01:26:38,995 --> 01:26:40,563
WHAT IS IT, WHAT'S WRONG?

2188
01:26:40,597 --> 01:26:41,998
THE A'S ARE MUCH
TOO HIGH, SIR.

2189
01:26:42,032 --> 01:26:44,700
200, SIR, THE TEMPERATURE IS
CONTINUALLY RISING.

2190
01:26:44,733 --> 01:26:45,935
ANOTHER 100 DEGREES

2191
01:26:45,968 --> 01:26:47,803
AND THE ENGINE ROOM
WILL EXPLODE.

2192
01:26:47,837 --> 01:26:49,072
WHAT ARE WE GONNA DO?

2193
01:26:49,105 --> 01:26:50,807
WELL, DON'T GO IN
THE ENGINE ROOM.

2194
01:26:50,840 --> 01:26:53,175
WE GOTTA FIND A WAY TO
REDUCE THE TEMPERATURE.

2195
01:26:53,208 --> 01:26:56,178
JERRY, SEE IF DR. TAKEBANA
CAN HELP US, GO ON.

2196
01:26:56,212 --> 01:26:57,513
YES, SIR.

2197
01:27:00,215 --> 01:27:01,783
UM.

2198
01:27:01,817 --> 01:27:03,385
[ALARM SOUNDING]

2199
01:27:03,418 --> 01:27:04,820
JERRY!

2200
01:27:04,853 --> 01:27:07,657
THEY'D BETTER HURRY OR Q WILL
BLAST US RIGHT OUT OF HERE.

2201
01:27:07,690 --> 01:27:10,158
THEY'RE WORKING ON THE
SYNCHROTON NOW.

2202
01:27:10,192 --> 01:27:14,697
THEY BOUGHT THAT
SYNCHOTRON THING.

2203
01:27:14,730 --> 01:27:16,832
HIGH SCHOOL SHOP CLASSES ARE
QUICKLY TAKEN.

2204
01:27:16,865 --> 01:27:17,933
CAN'T YOU HURRY?

2205
01:27:17,967 --> 01:27:19,468
THEY'RE HELPLESS OUT THERE.

2206
01:27:19,502 --> 01:27:21,503
I'M DOING ALL I CAN.

2207
01:27:21,537 --> 01:27:22,538
TRY THAT SWITCH.

2208
01:27:22,572 --> 01:27:24,173
YOU TRY IT, I'M BITTER.

2209
01:27:24,207 --> 01:27:25,173
I'LL TAKE OVER.

2210
01:27:25,207 --> 01:27:26,208
TRY THE BACKUP SYSTEM.

2211
01:27:26,242 --> 01:27:27,377
YES, SIR.

2212
01:27:27,410 --> 01:27:31,280
YOU GUYS HAD ALL SEMESTER TO
WORK ON THIS.

2213
01:27:31,313 --> 01:27:34,383
JERRY, JERRY, HOW'S IT GOING?

2214
01:27:34,417 --> 01:27:37,153
THE TEMPERATURE'S STILL RISING,
I CAN'T SEEM TO CONTROL IT.

2215
01:27:37,187 --> 01:27:38,320
OOH.

2216
01:27:38,353 --> 01:27:40,957
HURRY, DOCTOR, YOU'VE GOTTA
GET IT WORKING.

2217
01:27:40,990 --> 01:27:42,358
UM, UM...

2218
01:27:42,392 --> 01:27:44,493
SIR, THE TEMPERATURE
IS STILL RISING.

2219
01:27:44,527 --> 01:27:47,597
WE'LL EXPLODE ANY SECOND,
WHAT SHALL WE DO?

2220
01:27:47,630 --> 01:27:50,065
I CAN'T CHANGE THE LAWS OF
PHYSICS, CAPTAIN.

2221
01:27:50,098 --> 01:27:51,967
I'VE GOT TO HAVE 30 MINUTES.

2222
01:27:52,000 --> 01:27:53,803
I'VE GOT IT,
IT'S WORKING NOW.

2223
01:27:53,837 --> 01:27:54,803
IT'S WORKING.

2224
01:27:54,837 --> 01:27:55,805
HE JUST PLUGGED IT IN.

2225
01:27:55,838 --> 01:27:58,207
IT'S WORKING, IT'S WORKING.

2226
01:27:58,240 --> 01:27:59,875
DIRECT IT ONTO THE ENGINES.

2227
01:27:59,908 --> 01:28:02,378
AND GET A LITTLE ON
THE PLOT IF YOU CAN.

2228
01:28:02,412 --> 01:28:04,580
RIGHT THERE.

2229
01:28:04,613 --> 01:28:06,482
YOU DIE, BAZOOKA JOE.

2230
01:28:06,515 --> 01:28:08,450
ALL RIGHT, NOW, FIRE.

2231
01:28:08,483 --> 01:28:09,452
OH, YEAH.

2232
01:28:09,485 --> 01:28:12,688
[TOM BREATHING HEAVILY]

2233
01:28:12,722 --> 01:28:14,923
OH, IT'S GOOD FOR ME,
HOW ABOUT YOU?

2234
01:28:14,957 --> 01:28:16,458
THE ICE IS MELTING.

2235
01:28:16,492 --> 01:28:19,495
THE TEMPERATURE'S DROPPING,
THE TEMPERATURE'S DROPPING!

2236
01:28:19,528 --> 01:28:21,930
GREAT.

2237
01:28:21,963 --> 01:28:24,000
THE A'S ARE DOWN BUT YOU CAN
NEVER COUNT 'EM OUT.

2238
01:28:24,033 --> 01:28:25,902
YOU KNOW WITH THOSE A'S...

2239
01:28:25,935 --> 01:28:27,503
ALL SYSTEMS FUNCTIONING.

2240
01:28:27,537 --> 01:28:28,503
START UP.

2241
01:28:28,537 --> 01:28:31,807
SHUT UP.
[CROW LAUGHS]

2242
01:28:31,840 --> 01:28:34,110
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GET THEM.

2243
01:28:34,143 --> 01:28:36,078
CONTINUOUS BANK
TURN CONTINUING, SIR.

2244
01:28:36,112 --> 01:28:37,680
[LAUGHING]

2245
01:28:37,713 --> 01:28:43,920
ALL RIGHT, ENOUGH OF
THAT SHOT, TOO.

2246
01:28:43,953 --> 01:28:44,987
IT'S BALSA WOOD.

2247
01:28:45,020 --> 01:28:47,022
I THINK SO.

2248
01:28:47,055 --> 01:28:48,390
THEY ALWAYS WHISTLE
UNDER WATER,

2249
01:28:48,423 --> 01:28:50,125
THEY ARE UNDER
WATER, AREN'T THEY?

2250
01:28:50,158 --> 01:28:55,330
I DON'T KNOW BUT
IT'S REALLY DARK.

2251
01:28:55,363 --> 01:28:57,433
[TOM HUMMING]

2252
01:28:57,467 --> 01:28:58,868
OH, THEY BENT THE SHIP.

2253
01:28:58,902 --> 01:29:01,903
HEY, GO DOWN TO BEN FRANKLIN AND
PICK UP ANOTHER ONE, WOULD YOU?

2254
01:29:03,338 --> 01:29:05,575
[TOM HUMMING]

2255
01:29:05,608 --> 01:29:08,745
HERE COMES SUPER CAR.

2256
01:29:08,778 --> 01:29:11,713
[ALL]
SUPER CAR.

2257
01:29:11,747 --> 01:29:17,687
LOOK, NEW UNDERWEAR,
FRUIT OF THE LOOM.

2258
01:29:17,720 --> 01:29:22,925
[CROW MAKING CAR NOISES]

2259
01:29:22,958 --> 01:29:24,460
IT'S GAMERA.

2260
01:29:24,493 --> 01:29:25,862
OH.

2261
01:29:25,895 --> 01:29:32,135
IT'S THE BUBBLE AND
FLOW VERSION.
[LAUGHS]

2262
01:29:32,168 --> 01:29:33,535
LASER GUN.

2263
01:29:33,568 --> 01:29:34,570
LASER GUN.

2264
01:29:38,707 --> 01:29:39,875
LAUNCH ROCKETS.

2265
01:29:39,908 --> 01:29:42,978
BLAND MOVIE.

2266
01:29:43,012 --> 01:29:46,515
OOH.

2267
01:29:46,548 --> 01:29:48,683
YOU KNOW, THIS REALLY ISN'T A
VERY GOOD MOVIE.

2268
01:29:48,717 --> 01:29:50,920
- NO, IT'S NOT.
- SECOND BATTERY.

2269
01:29:50,953 --> 01:29:52,655
FIRE, SECOND BATTERY.

2270
01:29:52,688 --> 01:29:56,092
FIRE SCREENWRITER.

2271
01:29:56,125 --> 01:29:59,628
♪ WE HAVE TO SINK THE BISMARCK
WE HAD TO DO THE JOB ♪

2272
01:29:59,662 --> 01:30:04,600
HEY, JOHNNY, QUIT
SPLASHING IN THE TUB.

2273
01:30:04,633 --> 01:30:05,602
OOH.

2274
01:30:05,635 --> 01:30:06,602
THIRD BATTERY!

2275
01:30:06,635 --> 01:30:10,105
WHAT'S-- DID HE SAY
TURD BATTERY?

2276
01:30:10,138 --> 01:30:12,242
- HMM.
- ATTACK.

2277
01:30:12,275 --> 01:30:17,045
WHAT DO YOU THINK THEY'VE BEEN
DOING, COME ON.

2278
01:30:17,078 --> 01:30:18,247
DEFROST.

2279
01:30:18,280 --> 01:30:19,315
OOH!

2280
01:30:19,348 --> 01:30:21,417
OH, THEY HIT THE
CHERRY CENTER.

2281
01:30:21,450 --> 01:30:23,518
DOGGONE IT, THAT ABOUT
DOES IT, DOESN'T IT?

2282
01:30:26,488 --> 01:30:27,857
- YES.
- THEY STOPPED FIRING.

2283
01:30:27,890 --> 01:30:29,858
WE GOT THEM.

2284
01:30:29,892 --> 01:30:31,193
WE SHOT THEM.

2285
01:30:31,227 --> 01:30:35,030
AND THE FRIES ARE UP, IT'S
A GLORIOUS MOMENT FOR ALL.

2286
01:30:35,063 --> 01:30:36,265
BASK.

2287
01:30:36,298 --> 01:30:38,167
THEY BEAT US, FLOPSY.

2288
01:30:38,200 --> 01:30:42,238
- IT'S GENERIC KITTY
LITTER FROM NOW ON.
- [CROW MEOWS]

2289
01:30:42,272 --> 01:30:45,240
THE GUNS OF NAVARONE.

2290
01:30:50,412 --> 01:30:52,147
SEE YOU ON THE OTHER
SIDE, FLOPSY.

2291
01:30:52,180 --> 01:30:56,152
NO WAY, I GOT EIGHT MORE
LIVES, DICKWEED, MEOW.

2292
01:30:56,185 --> 01:31:01,290
NOW WHAT?

2293
01:31:01,323 --> 01:31:02,692
OOH.

2294
01:31:06,562 --> 01:31:09,632
OH, THAT RHUBARB,
IT'S FLOATING RHUBARB?

2295
01:31:09,665 --> 01:31:11,233
[SCREAMING]

2296
01:31:11,267 --> 01:31:15,203
IN THE LAND OF DAIRY QUEEN,
WE BLOW YOU UP.

2297
01:31:18,107 --> 01:31:20,577
OOH.

2298
01:31:20,610 --> 01:31:22,110
WE'RE BLOWING UP RHUBARB.

2299
01:31:22,143 --> 01:31:23,645
A BALL OF FIRE.

2300
01:31:23,678 --> 01:31:26,748
OOH, OOH, THAT ALL
THE RHUBARB, OOH.

2301
01:31:26,782 --> 01:31:30,720
OVERBAKED ALASKA.
[LAUGHS]

2302
01:31:34,823 --> 01:31:39,095
IT'S BEAUTIFUL,
IN SOME SICK WAY.

2303
01:31:39,128 --> 01:31:42,632
[GROANS]

2304
01:31:42,665 --> 01:31:45,668
UH-OH.

2305
01:31:45,702 --> 01:31:47,035
WHO AM I?

2306
01:31:47,068 --> 01:31:48,270
ERNEST HEMINGWAY,
GET IT.

2307
01:31:48,303 --> 01:31:50,072
NO, NO, NO.

2308
01:31:50,105 --> 01:31:52,608
HEY, THAT'S THE
COWARD'S WAY OUT.

2309
01:31:57,580 --> 01:32:00,448
♪ NOW IT'S OVER ♪

2310
01:32:00,482 --> 01:32:05,320
♪ THE MAN WHO SHOT HIMSELF ♪

2311
01:32:05,353 --> 01:32:07,823
♪♪

2312
01:32:07,857 --> 01:32:11,327
WE NOW RETURN TO "ICE STATION
ZEBRA" ALREADY IN PROGRESS.

2313
01:32:11,360 --> 01:32:12,362
WELL, THAT'S THE END OF Q.

2314
01:32:12,395 --> 01:32:13,695
GOOD WORK, MEN.

2315
01:32:13,728 --> 01:32:15,430
IT WAS A DIFFICULT
MISSION BUT WE DID IT.

2316
01:32:15,463 --> 01:32:16,465
- YES.
- OOH.

2317
01:32:16,498 --> 01:32:17,700
I HOPE IT WASN'T TOO
TOUGH ON YOU.

2318
01:32:17,733 --> 01:32:18,935
IT'S BEEN AN HONOR
WORKING WITH YOU, SIR.

2319
01:32:18,968 --> 01:32:19,902
I LOVE YOU, S--.

2320
01:32:19,935 --> 01:32:20,903
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO HOME.

2321
01:32:20,937 --> 01:32:22,037
YES, SIR.

2322
01:32:22,070 --> 01:32:23,805
IT WILL TAKE US ABOUT A HALF
HOUR TO GET HOME

2323
01:32:23,838 --> 01:32:27,677
AND WE'RE GONNA FILM EVERY
MINUTE OF IT.

2324
01:32:27,710 --> 01:32:33,348
♪ THIS IS THE END
OF THE MOVIE ♪

2325
01:32:36,352 --> 01:32:39,288
MIGHTY JACK WILL BE BACK IN
ROBERT LUDLUM'S

2326
01:32:39,322 --> 01:32:41,857
THE GRIM-JIN FLIM-THIN
PRIM-PRIM CONSPIRACY.

2327
01:32:41,890 --> 01:32:43,758
OH, WAIT, WAIT, WE GOTTA SEE THE
SANDY FRANK SIDE HERE.

2328
01:32:43,792 --> 01:32:45,527
LET'S JUST STAY QUIET.

2329
01:32:45,560 --> 01:32:47,397
THAT'S MY FAVORITE PART.

2330
01:32:47,430 --> 01:32:48,863
YOU'VE SEEN
IT A MILLION TIMES.

2331
01:32:48,897 --> 01:32:50,332
WHAT A BOTHER.

2332
01:32:50,365 --> 01:32:51,333
JUST A MOMENT.

2333
01:32:51,367 --> 01:32:54,670
♪ SANDY FRANK, SANDY FRANK ♪

2334
01:32:54,703 --> 01:32:57,373
♪♪

2335
01:32:57,407 --> 01:33:00,542
[GATES CLOSING]

2336
01:33:04,180 --> 01:33:05,948
[ACCORDION MUSIC PLAYING]

2337
01:33:05,982 --> 01:33:08,617
[ROBOTS CHUCKLING AS PIRATES]
WELL, ME CLAMMY BUCKOS,
THE MOVIE'S OVER,

2338
01:33:08,650 --> 01:33:12,253
THE PAIN IS PAST AND I'S FEEL
LIKE SINGING A PLOT SHANTY.

2339
01:33:12,287 --> 01:33:15,925
BE LIVELY NOW,
ME BONNIE RAITTS.

2340
01:33:15,958 --> 01:33:19,562
♪ OH SLOW
THE PLOT DOWN, LADDIE ♪

2341
01:33:19,595 --> 01:33:21,963
♪ SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2342
01:33:21,997 --> 01:33:26,502
♪ WAY HEY SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2343
01:33:26,535 --> 01:33:31,607
♪ WE'LL SCUTTLE THE STORY
AND RUN HER AGROUND ♪

2344
01:33:31,640 --> 01:33:36,212
♪ WE'LL TRY SO HARD
TO SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2345
01:33:36,245 --> 01:33:38,580
OKAY, NOW, WHO CAN TELL ME

2346
01:33:38,613 --> 01:33:41,817
THEIR FAVORITE SCENE FROM THE
MOVIE SO FAR.

2347
01:33:41,850 --> 01:33:43,352
TOM, GO AHEAD.

2348
01:33:43,385 --> 01:33:45,822
THERE WAS THE, UH...
THERE WAS, UH...

2349
01:33:45,855 --> 01:33:47,390
UM, UH...

2350
01:33:47,423 --> 01:33:50,225
♪ OH SLOW THE PLOT DOWN,
LADDIE ♪

2351
01:33:50,258 --> 01:33:52,895
♪ SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2352
01:33:52,928 --> 01:33:57,332
♪ WAY HEY SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2353
01:33:57,365 --> 01:34:02,405
♪ WITH GERMAN ITALIAN
AND JAPANESE CLOWNS ♪

2354
01:34:02,438 --> 01:34:07,510
♪ WE'LL TRY SO HARD
TO SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2355
01:34:07,543 --> 01:34:09,512
OKAY, WELL,
HOW ABOUT YOU, CROW?

2356
01:34:09,545 --> 01:34:11,880
YOU MUST BE FULL TO BURSTING
WITH SOME FOND MEMORIES

2357
01:34:11,913 --> 01:34:13,882
OF TODAY'S MOVIE,
COME ON, THINK HARD.

2358
01:34:13,915 --> 01:34:17,620
OH, UH... UH... UM..

2359
01:34:17,653 --> 01:34:19,988
UH, GEEZ, JOEL,
I'M DRAWING A BLANK.

2360
01:34:20,022 --> 01:34:21,757
- YEAH, ME TOO.
- I, UM...

2361
01:34:21,790 --> 01:34:24,760
OH, OH, I REMEMBER, UH, VAGUELY,
A GUY LOCKED--

2362
01:34:24,793 --> 01:34:28,763
LOCKED IN A ROOM WITH ANOTHER
GUY AND SOMEONE RUNNING.

2363
01:34:28,797 --> 01:34:32,367
♪ OH MAKE YOU A MOVIE ♪

2364
01:34:32,400 --> 01:34:35,270
♪ THAT'S LONG AND A MESS ♪

2365
01:34:35,303 --> 01:34:39,842
♪ WAY HEY SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2366
01:34:39,875 --> 01:34:44,880
♪ JUST GIVE US A SCRIPT THAT
MAKES NO FRIGGIN' SENSE ♪

2367
01:34:44,913 --> 01:34:49,918
♪ WE'LL TRY SO HARD
TO SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2368
01:34:49,952 --> 01:34:52,855
WELL, COME ON, YOU GUYS, I CAN
REMEMBER, I FOR ONE,

2369
01:34:52,888 --> 01:34:57,058
IN VIVID DETAIL OF FROGMEN
WHO, UH...

2370
01:34:57,092 --> 01:34:59,528
JUST WHO-- WHO IS MIGHTY JACK,
ANYWAY?

2371
01:34:59,562 --> 01:35:01,530
OH, WOW, IT JUST HIT ME,
I REMEMBER.

2372
01:35:01,563 --> 01:35:03,798
THE SCENE WHERE QUEEQUEG SITS
MOTIONLESS ON THE DECK

2373
01:35:03,832 --> 01:35:05,868
MEDITATING, FORETELLING THE
DEATH OF THE CREW...

2374
01:35:05,902 --> 01:35:08,003
OH, YEAH, YEAH, AND SCOUT SEES
ATTICUS SHOOT THE MAD DOG

2375
01:35:08,037 --> 01:35:10,238
IN THE STREET AND ALEX
GOES AND COMES...

2376
01:35:10,272 --> 01:35:12,508
I REMEMBER, AND THEN PATRICK
SWAYZE WALKS IN AND SAYS,

2377
01:35:12,542 --> 01:35:15,210
[ALL]
"IT'S MY WAY
OR THE HIGHWAY."

2378
01:35:15,243 --> 01:35:17,378
[LAUGHING LIKE PIRATES]

2379
01:35:17,412 --> 01:35:19,548
- COME ON, GUYS.
- OH, MY BRAIN HURTS.

2380
01:35:19,582 --> 01:35:21,183
JOEL, I'M SO CONFUSED.

2381
01:35:21,217 --> 01:35:23,885
IT'S REALLY NOT THAT BAD, YOU
GUYS, I FOR ONE ACTUALLY FEEL

2382
01:35:23,918 --> 01:35:26,088
LIKE I JUST GOT DONE LISTENING
TO TWO HOURS

2383
01:35:26,122 --> 01:35:27,857
OF LOU REED'S
"METAL MACHINE MUSIC."

2384
01:35:27,890 --> 01:35:30,793
YOU KNOW, MY BRAIN FEELS CLEAN
AS A WHISTLE.

2385
01:35:30,827 --> 01:35:32,260
- AND THAT'S PRETTY GOOD.
- YEAH, IT IS.

2386
01:35:32,293 --> 01:35:33,862
- LET'S TAKE IT HOME.
- OKAY.

2387
01:35:33,895 --> 01:35:39,335
♪ OH SLOW THE PLOT DOWN LADDIES
SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2388
01:35:39,368 --> 01:35:44,105
♪ WAY HEY SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪

2389
01:35:44,138 --> 01:35:49,178
♪ JUST SCUTTLE THE STORY
AND RUN HER AGROUND ♪

2390
01:35:49,212 --> 01:35:53,882
♪ WE'LL TRY SO HARD
TO SLOW THE PLOT DOWN ♪♪

2391
01:35:53,915 --> 01:35:55,550
[TALKING LIKE PIRATES]

2392
01:35:55,583 --> 01:35:59,422
MY BONNIE OVERLORDS,
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

2393
01:35:59,455 --> 01:36:01,457
WELL, I THINK I'M GOING TO
HAVE TO ADJUST

2394
01:36:01,490 --> 01:36:03,158
YOUR AIR MIXTURE AGAIN,
PIRATE DOG.

2395
01:36:03,192 --> 01:36:05,493
IT LOOKS LIKE IT'S GETTING
A LITTLE THIN UP THERE.

2396
01:36:05,527 --> 01:36:07,095
PUSH THE BUTTON, FRANK.

2397
01:36:07,128 --> 01:36:09,365
HARD BERG METHOUGHT,
SO COLD, SO VAST,

2398
01:36:09,398 --> 01:36:11,867
WITH MORTAL DAMPS
SET OVERCAST.

2399
01:36:11,900 --> 01:36:14,403
EXALTING STILL THY
DANKISH BREATH,

2400
01:36:14,437 --> 01:36:17,305
ADRIFT DISSOLVING,
BOUND FOR DEATH.

2401
01:36:17,338 --> 01:36:18,873
ISN'T THAT RIGHT,
BLIND JIM?

2402
01:36:18,907 --> 01:36:21,077
- [SNARLING LIKE A PIRATE]
- OH, GREAT, YOU'VE GOT
FRANK LOCKED UP,

2403
01:36:21,110 --> 01:36:22,512
HE'S QUOTING MELVILLE.

2404
01:36:22,545 --> 01:36:25,113
GO AWAY.

2405
01:36:25,147 --> 01:36:27,983
NOR STIR THE SLIMY SLUG THAT
SPRAWLS ALONG...

2406
01:36:28,017 --> 01:36:30,818
OH, SHUT UP, FRANK.

2407
01:36:30,852 --> 01:36:34,757
♪♪
